  ('soya-protein-isolate', 'UIL-0015', 'Soya Protein Isolate', 'Soy protein isolate; SPI; isolated soy protein', 'Protein ingredients', 'Soya bean', 'A highly purified protein fraction separated from defatted soya.', 'Soya beans.', 'Raises protein; binds water and fat; improves texture; supports meat alternatives and bars.', 'Processed ingredient', 'High protein with little carbohydrate or fat; amino-acid profile is complete but methionine is relatively lower than some animal proteins.', 'High', 'Low', 'Low', 'Low', 'Usually low direct effect unless combined with sugars or starches.', 'May cause symptoms in people with soya allergy; some may experience digestive discomfort.', 'Not established as inherently inflammatory for most people; allergy is the primary established immune concern.', 'Soya is one of the 14 UK-regulated allergens. Soya protein isolate retains soya protein and is not covered by the exemption that applies to fully refined soybean oil.', 'People with soya allergy; consumers comparing isolated protein with less-refined soya foods.', 'Meat alternatives; protein powders; bars; bakery products; meal replacements.', 'Soya protein isolate; soy protein isolate; isolated soy protein; SPI', 'Tofu, tempeh, edamame, beans, lentils or less-isolated protein sources.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free, but check the product.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Highly isolated plant protein', 'High', 'Soya is one of the 14 UK-regulated allergens and must be declared.', 'Soya isolate is a concentrated complete plant protein with useful functionality. It supplies protein efficiently, but it lacks much of the fibre and food structure of whole soya foods.', 'soya protein isolate|soy protein isolate|spi|isolated soy protein', 'soya protien isolate; soy protien isolate', 'Soya protein concentrate; tofu; textured vegetable protein', 'Flavourings; emulsifiers; stabilisers', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirement