  ('pea-protein-isolate', 'UIL-0016', 'Pea Protein Isolate', 'Pea protein; isolated pea protein; yellow pea protein isolate', 'Protein ingredients', 'Yellow split pea', 'A concentrated protein fraction separated from peas, usually by wet or dry processing.', 'Yellow peas.', 'Raises protein; supports structure and texture in plant-based foods; binds water.', 'Processed ingredient', 'High plant protein; relatively rich in lysine but lower in methionine.', 'High', 'Low', 'Low', 'Low', 'Usually low direct effect unless combined with carbohydrate ingredients.', 'Can cause bloating or discomfort in some people; pea allergy exists and may cross-react in some legume-allergic individuals.', 'Not established as inherently inflammatory.', 'Pea allergy can cause IgE-mediated reactions. Pea is not one of the 14 UK-regulated allergens, and clinically relevant cross-reactivity with other legumes has been reported, although the extent is uncertain.', 'People with diagnosed pea allergy; people with clinically relevant legume allergies who have been advised to assess cross-reactivity; consumers using concentrated pea-protein products.', 'Plant protein powders; meat alternatives; bars; dairy alternatives; ready meals.', 'Pea protein isolate; pea protein; yellow pea protein', 'Whole peas, lentils, beans, tofu, tempeh or mixed whole-food proteins.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free, but check the product.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Highly isolated plant protein', 'Moderate', 'Not one of the 14 UK mandatory allergens, but must still be accurately named in the ingredients list.', 'Pea isolate is a useful plant protein, especially in vegan products, but it removes much of the fibre and structure found in whole peas.', 'pea protein isolate|pea protein|isolated pea protein|yellow pea protein', 'pea protien isolate; pee protein isolate', 'Pea protein concentrate; lentil protein; soya protein isolate', 'Flavourings; stabilisers; emulsifiers', 'https://science.food.gov.uk/article/154198-safety-assessment-of-pea-protein-fermented-by-shiitake-lentinula-edodes-mushroom-mycelia-as-a-novel-food-rp1759', '2026-08-08', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('yeast-extract', 'UIL-0017', 'Yeast Extract', 'Autolysed yeast extract; hydrolysed yeast extract; yeast autolysate', 'Flavouring ingredients', 'Yeast', 'A concentrated soluble extract from broken-down yeast cells containing amino acids, peptides and naturally occurring flavour compounds.', 'Usually baker''s or brewer''s yeast.', 'Adds savoury or umami taste; boosts flavour; can reduce the need for some added salt while still contributing sodium.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Small amounts of amino acids and peptides; sodium varies widely.', 'Low in normal serving amounts.', 'Negligible', 'Low', 'Negligible', 'Usually little direct effect.', 'No consistent ingredient-specific gut effect is established for typical dietary amounts; individual tolerance varies.', 'No good evidence that yeast extract is inherently inflammatory.', 'Yeast allergy is possible but is not one of the 14 UK-regulated allergens. Sodium and glutamate content vary by product and are nutritional/compositional issues rather than allergy by default.', 'People with confirmed yeast allergy; people limiting sodium when the finished product is high in salt.', 'Soups; stock cubes; crisps; savoury spreads; sauces; meat alternatives; seasoning.', 'Yeast extract; autolysed yeast extract; yeast autolysate', 'Herbs, spices, mushrooms, reduced stock or fermented whole-food flavour sources.', 'Usually', 'Usually', 'Usually gluten-free by ingredient, but brewer''s-yeast sourcing and final-product contamination should be checked.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Concentrated savoury flavour ingredient', 'Limited', 'Permitted food ingredient; it is not the same as separately added monosodium glutamate, although it naturally contains glutamate compounds.', 'Yeast extract concentrates savoury flavour. It is not automatically MSG, but it can increase glutamate-rich taste and may add meaningful sodium depending on the product.', 'yeast extract|autolysed yeast extract|hydrolysed yeast extract|yeast autolysate', 'yeas