  ('hydrolysed-vegetable-protein', 'UIL-0018', 'Hydrolysed Vegetable Protein', 'HVP; hydrolyzed vegetable protein; hydrolysed plant protein', 'Flavouring ingredients', 'Plant protein', 'Plant protein broken into smaller peptides and amino acids using acid or enzymes, producing a strong savoury flavour.', 'Often soya, maize, wheat or other plant proteins.', 'Adds savoury taste; boosts aroma; improves meat-like flavour; supplies soluble protein fragments.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Small protein fragments and amino acids; sodium can be high depending on formulation.', 'Low to moderate in normal use.', 'Negligible', 'Low', 'Negligible', 'Usually little direct effect.', 'Tolerance varies; source allergens remain important.', 'Not established as inherently inflammatory.', 'Allergen relevance depends on the source protein. Hydrolysed soya or wheat protein can remain relevant to people with the corresponding allergy; cereal source also matters for gluten-related labelling.', 'People with relevant source-protein allergies; people with coeliac disease when the product is wheat-derived; people limiting sodium if the finished product is high in salt.', 'Seasonings; soups; gravies; snacks; ready meals; meat alternatives.', 'Hydrolysed vegetable protein; hydrolysed plant protein; HVP; hydrolyzed vegetable protein', 'Herbs, spices, mushrooms, fermented foods or reduced stocks.', 'Usually', 'Usually', 'Source-dependent; wheat-derived versions require careful allergen assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Highly processed savoury flavour ingredient', 'Moderate', 'Source allergens must be declared where applicable.', 'Hydrolysed vegetable protein is used to build intense savoury flavour. The key questions are its source, sodium contribution and the overall formulation—not a claim that it is universally harmful.', 'hydrolysed vegetable protein|hydrolyzed vegetable protein|hydrolysed plant protein|hvp', 'hydrolised vegetable protein; hydrolysed veg protein', 'Yeast extract; 