  ('shea-fat', 'UIL-0058', 'Shea Fat', 'Shea butter; shea stearin; shea olein', 'Oils and fats', 'Shea nut kernel', 'A plant fat extracted from shea kernels and sometimes fractionated for confectionery use.', 'Kernels of the shea tree; pressed or solvent-extracted, then refined or fractionated.', 'Used in confectionery fats, bakery fillings and cocoa-butter equivalents.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Almost entirely fat; mixture of saturated and monounsaturated fatty acids.', 'None', 'High', 'None', 'None', 'No direct blood-glucose effect.', 'Generally well tolerated.', 'No established ingredient-specific inflammatory effect.', 'Shea allergy appears uncommon; shea is not one of the 14 UK-regulated allergens.', 'People with rare shea allergy and those assessing substitute fats in confectionery.', 'Chocolate-style coatings, fillings, spreads, bakery fats and confectionery.', 'Shea fat; shea butter; shea stearin; shea olein', 'Cocoa butter where required for authentic chocolate; unsaturated oils for routine cooking.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free.', 'Context dependent', 'Speciality confectionery fat', 'Moderate', 'Permitted food ingredient; finished-product chocolate naming and composition rules may apply.', 'Shea fat is mainly a texture fat used in confectionery. Its role is functional rather than nutritional.', 'shea fat|shea butter|shea stearin|shea olein', 'shear butter|shea fatt', 'Cocoa butter; palm kernel oil; confectionery fat', 'Emulsifiers may be used alongside it', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid | https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/dietary-reference-values | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidanceindustry-specific-advice/allergen-labelling', '2026-08-04', '{}'::jsonb),
