  ('margarine', 'UIL-0060', 'Margarine', 'Vegetable spread; table margarine; baking margarine', 'Dairy fats and spreads', 'Oil-and-water emulsion', 'A spreadable emulsion made mainly from vegetable oils and fats with water, and sometimes milk ingredients, salt, vitamins, colours or emulsifiers.', 'Blended plant oils and fats; exact formulation varies by brand and intended use.', 'Used as a spread, baking fat and lower-cost or lower-saturated-fat alternative to butter.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly fat; profile varies from mostly unsaturated to more saturated depending on oils used.', 'Low unless milk or other protein ingredients are added.', 'High; fatty-acid quality is product-specific.', 'Low', 'None', 'Minimal direct carbohydrate effect.', 'Usually well tolerated; ingredient-specific sensitivities depend on formulation.', 'Margarine is not automatically inflammatory or healthy; compare saturated fat, trans fat, salt and ingredient list.', 'May contain milk or soy, both regulated UK allergens; some products are vegan and others are not.', 'People with milk or soy allergy; people comparing saturated fat, trans fat, salt and fortification.', 'Spreads, baking, pastries, cakes and commercial food manufacture.', 'Margarine; vegetable spread; baking margarine; table spread', 'Choose a soft spread based mainly on unsaturated oils and low saturated fat, or use olive/rapeseed oil where practical.', 'Formulation dependent', 'Usually', 'Usually gluten-free, but check flavourings and cross-contact.', 'Context dependent', 'Variable formulated spread', 'High', 'Compositional naming rules may distinguish margarine from other fat spreads; allergens must be declared.', 'Margarine is a category, not one nutritional profile. The oils, saturated-fat level, additives and allergens decide whether one product is a better choice than another.', 'margarine|vegetable spread|table margarine|baking margarine|fat spread', 'margerine|margarin', 'Butter; vegetable shortening; plant-based sp