  ('skimmed-milk-powder', 'UIL-0066', 'Skimmed Milk Powder', 'Non-fat dry milk; dried skimmed milk; skim milk powder', 'Dairy powders', 'Milk', 'Milk with most fat removed, then concentrated and dried into powder.', 'Skimmed mammalian milk, usually cow’s milk.', 'Adds dairy solids, protein, lactose, browning, flavour and body while improving shelf life.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Protein, lactose, calcium and other milk minerals; low fat.', 'Moderate to high.', 'Low.', 'High relative to concentrated protein isolates because lactose remains.', 'Negligible.', 'Can raise blood glucose depending on quantity and product context; lactose is a natural milk sugar.', 'Can cause bloating, pain or diarrhoea in lactose intolerance because lactose remains.', 'No reliable basis for a blanket inflammatory label; allergy and intolerance are individual issues.', 'Milk allergen and lactose-intolerance relevance.', 'Milk allergy; lactose intolerance; vegans.', 'Chocolate, bread, biscuits, yoghurt, soups, sauces, confectionery and infant foods.', 'Skimmed milk powder; non-fat dry milk; dried skimmed milk', 'Fresh milk or plain dairy where appropriate; milk-free alternatives for allergy, not merely lactose-free products.', 'No', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free by composition; verify cross-contact.', 'Context dependent', 'Dried dairy ingredient', 'High', 'Milk must be emphasised on UK labels.', 'A traditional dried milk ingredient, not simply a protein powder. It contributes lactose as well as protein and minerals.', 'skimmed milk powder|skim milk powder|nonfat dry milk', 'skimmed milk poweder|skim milk poweder', 'Whole milk powder; whey powder; milk protein concentrate', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid', '2026-08-04', '{}'::jsonb),
