  ('wheat-gluten', 'UIL-0078', 'Wheat Gluten', 'Vital wheat gluten; gluten flour; wheat protein', 'Cereal proteins', 'Wheat', 'The concentrated protein fraction of wheat flour, produced by washing away much of the starch and drying the remaining gluten.', 'Wheat.', 'Strengthens dough, improves elasticity and raises protein; also creates chewy textures in meat alternatives.', 'Processed ingredient', 'High protein but not a complete standalone protein source; low in lysine relative to many animal proteins.', 'High.', 'Low.', 'Low, though residual starch varies.', 'Low.', 'Usually low direct impact when little starch remains; the full food determines response.', 'Can cause intestinal injury in coeliac disease and symptoms in some people with wheat or gluten sensitivity.', 'Can trigger immune-mediated disease in coeliac disease and allergy; this must not be generalised to everyone.', 'Major UK allergen and unsuitable for coeliac disease.', 'People with coeliac disease, wheat allergy or non-coeliac gluten sensitivity diagnosed or suspected with clinical support.', 'Bread, pizza dough, high-protein bakery foods, seitan and meat alternatives.', 'Wheat gluten; vital wheat gluten; wheat protein; gluten flour', 'Gluten-free flours and binders for coeliac-safe products; alternative proteins for meat substitutes.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Contains wheat gluten; not suitable for a gluten-free diet.', 'Often associated with NOVA 3', 'Concentrated cereal protein', 'High', 'Wheat must be declared and emphasised; gluten-free claims require legal thresholds and controls.', 'A concentrated wheat protein useful for structure. It is a clear avoid for coeliac disease and wheat allergy, but not inherently harmful to everyone.', 'wheat gluten|vital wheat gluten|wheat protein|gluten flour', 'wheat glutan|vital wheat gluton', 'Seitan; wheat flour; textured wheat protein', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidan