  ('rice-protein-concentrate', 'UIL-0079', 'Rice Protein Concentrate', 'Rice protein; brown rice protein; rice protein powder', 'Plant protein ingredients', 'Rice', 'A protein-rich powder produced by concentrating protein from rice, often using enzymes and filtration.', 'White or brown rice.', 'Adds plant protein to powders, bars and dairy-free formulations.', 'Processed ingredient', 'High protein; amino-acid profile is relatively low in lysine, so combining sources can improve balance.', 'High.', 'Usually low.', 'Low to moderate depending on grade.', 'Low.', 'Usually low when unflavoured; finished products may contain added sugars or starches.', 'Usually well tolerated; individual rice allergy or sensitivity is uncommon but possible.', 'No reliable evidence of a unique inflammatory effect.', 'Rice is not one of the 14 UK allergens, but individual allergy and cross-contact are possible.', 'People relying on it as their only protein source; those with rare rice allergy; consumers checking heavy-metal testing in supplements may prefer transparent suppliers.', 'Vegan protein powders, bars, shakes, infant foods and dairy alternatives.', 'Rice protein concentrate; brown rice protein; rice protein powder', 'Whole legumes, varied protein blends or minimally processed protein foods where suitable.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free by composition; verify cross-contact and certification where required.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Concentrated plant protein', 'High', 'General food-labelling and claims rules apply.', 'A useful hypoallergenic-leaning plant protein option, but its amino-acid profile is stronger when paired with lysine-rich foods such as legumes.', 'rice protein concentrate|rice protein|brown rice protein', 'rice protien', 'Pea protein; hemp protein; soya protein', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid', '2026-08-04', '{}'::json