  ('hemp-protein', 'UIL-0080', 'Hemp Protein', 'Hemp protein powder; hemp seed protein; concentrated hemp protein', 'Plant protein ingredients', 'Hemp seed', 'A protein-rich powder made by milling and sometimes concentrating defatted hemp seeds.', 'Hemp seeds from Cannabis sativa varieties grown for food.', 'Adds plant protein, fibre, earthy flavour and minerals to powders and foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Protein with variable fibre and residual fat; generally less refined than many isolates.', 'Moderate to high; amino-acid quality is useful but not identical to animal protein.', 'Low to moderate, often including unsaturated fats.', 'Low.', 'Moderate to high depending on processing.', 'Usually low direct impact when unsweetened.', 'Retained fibre may increase fullness or cause bloating if intake rises quickly.', 'No reliable evidence of a general inflammatory effect; unsaturated fats and fibre may support a balanced diet in context.', 'Not one of the 14 UK allergens; individual seed allergy and cross-contact remain possible.', 'People with rare hemp allergy; those expecting intoxicating effects should know food-grade hemp protein is not used for that purpose.', 'Protein powders, smoothies, bars, porridge and baking mixes.', 'Hemp protein; hemp seed protein; hemp protein powder', 'Whole hemp seeds, legumes, nuts or varied protein blends depending on needs.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free by composition; verify cross-contact.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Fibre-containing plant protein', 'High', 'Must comply with general UK food law; cannabinoid controls are separate from ordinary hemp-seed food use.', 'A plant protein that often retains more fibre than an isolate. It contributes useful nutrition but should still be part of a varied protein intake.', 'hemp protein|hemp seed protein|hemp protein powder', 'hemp protien', 'Hemp seeds; pea protein; rice protein', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://www.gov.uk/government/pub