  ('rolled-oats', 'UIL-0089', 'Rolled Oats', 'Oat flakes; porridge oats; old-fashioned oats', 'Wholegrain cereal ingredients', 'Oats', 'Whole oat groats that are steamed and rolled into flakes; thickness and cooking time vary.', 'Oat grain.', 'Used as a breakfast cereal and to add texture, fibre and binding to foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Carbohydrate with beta-glucan fibre, moderate protein and unsaturated fat.', 'Moderate.', 'Moderate for a cereal, mainly unsaturated.', 'High.', 'High relative to refined cereals.', 'Usually low to moderate depending on flake size, cooking and additions.', 'Often supports fullness and bowel regularity; large or sudden portions may cause bloating.', 'No general inflammatory classification; coeliac and oat-specific responses require individual care.', 'Oats are a regulated allergen and may be contaminated with other gluten cereals.', 'People with oat allergy, coeliac disease or sensitive digestion during rapid fibre increases.', 'Porridge, granola, flapjacks, muesli, bars and baking.', 'Rolled oats; oat flakes; porridge oats', 'Certified gluten-free rolled oats when required; steel-cut oats for a less processed texture if suitable.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Oats must be declared; certified gluten-free status depends on controlled production and legal thresholds.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Minimally processed whole grain', 'High', 'Oats must be emphasised as an allergen.', 'Rolled oats are a minimally processed whole grain with useful soluble fibre. Added sugars and fats in the finished product often matter more than the oats themselves.', 'rolled oats|porridge oats|oat flakes|old fashioned oats', 'role oats|rolled oates', 'Oat flour; steel-cut oats; oat bran', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-da