  ('oat-bran', 'UIL-0090', 'Oat Bran', 'Oat bran fibre; milled oat bran', 'Cereal fibre ingredients', 'Oats', 'The fibre-rich outer layers of the oat grain, separated during milling.', 'Oat grain.', 'Raises fibre, water binding and texture in cereals, baking and supplements.', 'Processed ingredient', 'High in fibre, including beta-glucan, with some protein, starch and fat.', 'Moderate.', 'Low to moderate.', 'Moderate.', 'High.', 'Usually lower than refined flour when eaten in a mixed food, but product context matters.', 'Can support bowel regularity; excess or rapid introduction may cause bloating or loose stools.', 'No general inflammatory classification; immune reactions are individual and established in specific conditions.', 'Oat allergen and coeliac cross-contamination considerations remain.', 'People with oat allergy, coeliac disease, bowel narrowing, or those increasing fibre rapidly.', 'Bran cereals, breads, muffins, porridge blends and fibre supplements.', 'Oat bran; oat bran fibre', 'Whole oats for a less fractionated option, or certified gluten-free oat bran where required.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Oats must be declared; certified gluten-free sourcing is needed for coeliac-safe use.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Concentrated cereal fibre', 'High', 'Oats remain an allergen even in gluten-free products.', 'Oat bran concentrates the fibre-rich parts of the grain. It can be useful, but more is not always better if the gut is not used to a high fibre load.', 'oat bran|oat bran fibre|milled oat bran', 'oat brand|oat brann', 'Rolled oats; oat flour; beta-glucan', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://data.food.gov.uk/codes/alerts/def/allergen/oats-gluten-free', '2026-08-04', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('rice-flour', 'UIL-0091', 'Rice Flour', 'White rice flour; milled rice; rice powder', 'Gluten-free cereal flours', 'Rice', 'A fine powder made by milling white rice.', 'White rice grain.', 'Provides bulk, crispness and thickening, especially in gluten-free foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mostly starch with low fibre and modest protein.', 'Low to moderate.', 'Low.', 'High.', 'Low.', 'Often moderate to high, especially when finely milled and used alone.', 'Usually well tolerated; low fibre may reduce satiety compared with wholegrain alternatives.', 'No reliable basis for a general inflammatory classification.', 'Rice is not one of the 14 UK allergens, but individual allergy and cross-contact are possible.', 'People managing blood glucose or relying heavily on refined gluten-free foods.', 'Gluten-free bread, noodles, baby foods, sauces, batters, crackers and snacks.', 'Rice flour; white rice flour; milled rice', 'Brown rice flour, buckwheat flour or mixed wholegrain gluten-free flours for more fibre where suitable.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free by composition; cross-contact controls still matter.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Refined gluten-free starch flour', 'High', 'General ingredient-list rules apply; gluten-free claims require appropriate controls.', 'Rice flour is a useful gluten-free base, but white versions are mainly refined starch and may need fibre- and protein-rich ingredients alongside them.', 'rice flour|white rice flour|milled rice|rice powder', 'rice flower|rise flour', 'Brown rice flour; rice starch; rice protein', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-08-04', '{}'::jsonb),
