  ('white-rice', 'UIL-0118', 'White Rice', 'Polished rice; milled rice; long-grain rice; basmati rice; jasmine rice', 'Processed cereal ingredients', 'Rice', 'Rice grain milled to remove the hull, bran and germ, leaving mainly the starchy endosperm.', 'Rice grain.', 'Provides a neutral, quick-cooking starch base and soft texture.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Mostly starch with small amounts of protein; enrichment varies by product and country.', 'Low to moderate.', 'Very low.', 'High.', 'Low.', 'Moderate to high depending on variety, cooking, cooling, portion and meal composition; basmati is often lower than some sticky varieties.', 'Usually easy to digest but less fibre-rich than wholegrain rice.', 'No specific inflammatory effect established.', 'Rice is not a mandatory UK allergen, though individual allergy is possible.', 'People monitoring blood glucose or relying heavily on rice without dietary variety.', 'Side dishes; curries; sushi; ready meals; puddings; cereals.', 'White rice; polished rice; long-grain rice; basmati rice; jasmine rice.', 'Brown rice, mixed grains or adding legumes and vegetables for more fibre and protein.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; contamination possible', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Refined staple; context matters', 'High', 'No specific allergen declaration required for rice; normal food safety and labelling rules apply.', 'White rice is a simple refined grain, not an additive. It is easy to digest but lower in fibre, so the portion and rest of the meal shape its impact.', 'white rice; polished rice; basmati rice; jasmine rice', 'wite rice; basmatti', 'Brown rice; rice flour; rice starch', 'None inherently', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-guidelines-and-