  ('coconut', 'UIL-0159', 'Coconut', 'Coconut flesh; desiccated coconut; shredded coconut; coconut flakes', 'Fruit, nuts and seeds', 'Coconut palm fruit', 'The edible flesh of a mature coconut, used fresh, dried or processed into milk, cream, flour and oil.', 'Cocos nucifera fruit kernel.', 'Used in baking, curries, desserts, cereals, confectionery and plant-based products.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Provides fat and fibre; coconut fat is high in saturated fatty acids.', 'Low to modest.', 'High in dried forms; predominantly saturated.', 'Low to moderate; sweetened coconut products differ.', 'Moderate to high in flesh and desiccated forms.', 'Usually low when unsweetened, but sweetened products differ.', 'Fibre and fat can affect tolerance; coconut milk and cream are concentrated.', 'No special anti-inflammatory effect established; high saturated-fat intake is relevant to overall diet.', 'Coconut is not one of the named regulated nuts in UK allergen rules, but coconut allergy can occur.', 'People with coconut allergy; those monitoring saturated-fat intake; users comparing coconut milk, cream and oil.', 'Curries; desserts; cereals; bakery products; confectionery; plant drinks.', 'Coconut; desiccated coconut; coconut flakes; coconut milk; coconut cream.', 'Unsaturated-fat ingredients where the aim is to reduce saturated fat; alternatives depend on recipe.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; cross-contact is possible', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Whole fruit ingredient; saturated-fat rich', 'High', 'Coconut is not one of the eight named regulated nuts in UK rules and should not be emphasised as a regulated nut solely for that reason.', 'Coconut is a food ingredient, not automatically a health upgrade. Whole flesh adds fibre, while coconut oil and cream concentrate saturated fat.', 'coconut; coconut flesh; desiccated coconut; coconut flakes', 'cocunut; coco nut', 'Coconut milk; coconut cream; coconut oil; coconut flour', 'None inherently', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/