  ('chestnuts', 'UIL-0160', 'Chestnuts', 'Chestnuts; sweet chestnuts; roasted chestnuts; chestnut kernels', 'Nuts and seeds', 'Sweet chestnut tree', 'Starchy edible nuts with much less fat and more carbohydrate than most culinary nuts.', 'Castanea sativa or related species nuts.', 'Used roasted, boiled, in stuffings, soups, purees, desserts and flour.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Mainly carbohydrate, with fibre and relatively little fat.', 'Low to modest.', 'Low compared with most nuts.', 'High; mainly starch.', 'Moderate.', 'Moderate; portion and preparation matter.', 'Generally tolerated; starch and fibre may affect some people.', 'No general inflammatory effect established.', 'Chestnut is not one of the eight named regulated nuts in UK allergen rules, but chestnut allergy can occur.', 'People with chestnut allergy; latex-allergic individuals may sometimes show cross-reactivity.', 'Roasted snacks; stuffing; purees; soups; desserts; chestnut flour.', 'Chestnut; chestnuts; sweet chestnut; chestnut flour.', 'Other whole starchy foods or nuts depending on recipe and allergy status.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; flour products need cross-contact checks', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Starchy whole nut; non-listed allergen risk', 'High', 'Chestnuts are not among the eight named regulated nuts in UK allergen rules and should not be emphasised as one solely on that basis.', 'Chestnuts do not share the same nutrition profile as almonds or walnuts. They behave more like a starchy whole food and are much lower in fat.', 'chestnut; chestnuts; sweet chestnut; chestnut flour', 'chest nut; chesnut', 'Chestnut flour; chestnut puree; roasted chestnuts', 'None inherently', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-