  ('date-paste', 'UIL-0163', 'Date Paste', 'Date paste; date purée; date puree; date pulp', 'Dried-fruit ingredients', 'Dates', 'Dates ground or blended into a dense paste, sometimes with added water.', 'Dried date fruit.', 'Provides sweetness, stickiness, binding and dark colour in bars, bakery products and sauces.', 'Processed ingredient', 'High in carbohydrate and naturally occurring sugars, with some fibre and minerals.', 'Low.', 'Very low.', 'High; concentrated natural sugars.', 'Moderate if whole date solids remain.', 'Moderate to high; portion and food matrix matter.', 'Can cause bloating or loose stools in some people when eaten in larger amounts.', 'No general inflammatory effect established.', 'Date allergy is uncommon; sulphites may be present in some processed dried-fruit products if used and must be declared above the legal threshold.', 'People monitoring sugar intake, dental health, portion size, or sensitivity to dried fruit.', 'Energy bars; raw desserts; bakery fillings; sauces; breakfast products.', 'Date paste; date purée; date puree; date pulp; ground dates.', 'Whole fruit in measured portions; compare with products using added syrups as well as date paste.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; cross-contact depends on manufacturing', 'Context dependent', 'Concentrated whole-fruit sweetener', 'High', 'Sulphites above 10 mg/kg or 10 mg/L in the finished product are regulated allergens and must be declared.', 'Date paste retains more fruit structure than refined syrup, but it is still a concentrated source of sugar and should not disappear from the sugar conversation.', 'date paste; date puree; date purée; date pulp; ground dates', 'dates paste; date pure', 'Dates; date syrup; raisin paste; fig paste', 'Sulphites may be used in some products', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/guidance/food-labelling-giving-food-information-to-consumers; https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-we