  ('mango-puree', 'UIL-0172', 'Mango Purée', 'Mango puree; mango purée; mango pulp', 'Fruit-derived ingredients', 'Mango', 'Ripe mango flesh crushed or blended into a smooth pulp, often pasteurised.', 'Mango fruit.', 'Adds sweetness, colour, flavour and body to drinks, desserts, sauces and baby foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly carbohydrate and natural sugars, with some fibre and carotenoids.', 'Low.', 'Very low.', 'Moderate to high depending on ripeness and concentration.', 'Low to moderate.', 'Usually moderate; portion and added sugar matter.', 'May affect people sensitive to fructose; mango can be high in fermentable carbohydrates at some portions.', 'No general inflammatory effect established.', 'Mango allergy can occur; peel-related cross-reactions are possible in sensitive individuals.', 'People with mango allergy, fructose/FODMAP sensitivity or those monitoring sugars.', 'Smoothies; yoghurts; desserts; chutneys; sauces; baby foods.', 'Mango purée; mango puree; mango pulp; mango preparation.', 'Whole mango or unsweetened purée; compare compound preparations for added sugar.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; cross-contact depends on product', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Whole-fruit derivative; naturally sweet', 'High', 'Any added sugars, preservatives or stabilisers must be separately declared in a compound preparation.', 'Mango purée carries fruit nutrients, but its smooth texture and natural sweetness make it easy for drinks and desserts to deliver large portions quickly.', 'mango puree; mango purée; mango pulp; mango preparation', 'mango pure; mangoe puree', 'Mango; mango concentrate; fruit purée', 'Preservatives or stabilisers may appear in preparations', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/5-a-day/5-a-day-what-counts/', '2026-08-04', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('tomato-puree', 'UIL-0173', 'Tomato Purée', 'Tomato puree; tomato purée; concentrated tomato purée', 'Vegetable and fruit concentrates', 'Tomato', 'Cooked, sieved and concentrated tomato pulp; UK products vary in concentration.', 'Ripe tomatoes.', 'Adds tomato flavour, colour, acidity, body and umami to sauces, soups and ready meals.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Carbohydrate, potassium and concentrated tomato solids including carotenoids; usually low in fat.', 'Low.', 'Very low.', 'Low to moderate; naturally low in sugars per typical portion.', 'Low to moderate.', 'Usually low in typical culinary portions.', 'Acidity may affect reflux; otherwise generally tolerated.', 'No general inflammatory effect established; tomato sensitivity is individual rather than universal.', 'Tomato allergy is uncommon; some people report intolerance to acidic foods.', 'People with tomato allergy, reflux or sensitivity to acidic foods.', 'Pasta sauces; soups; stews; pizzas; ready meals; ketchup.', 'Tomato purée; tomato puree; double concentrated tomato purée.', 'Plain tomato purée over sweetened tomato sauces; whole or chopped tomatoes where suitable.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; cross-contact depends on product', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Concentrated vegetable ingredient; generally useful', 'High', 'Tomato purée counts toward fruit and vegetable intake in UK public-health guidance; finished products may add salt or sugar.', 'Tomato purée is concentrated, but it is not automatically an ultra-processed ingredient. The bigger issue is what is added around it in sauces and ready meals.', 'tomato puree; tomato purée; concentrated tomato puree; double concentrate', 'tomato pure; tomoto puree', 'Tomatoes; tomato paste; tomato powder; passata', 'None inherently', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/5-a-day/5-a-day-what-counts/; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-li