  ('almond-meal', 'UIL-0230', 'Almond Meal', 'Ground almonds; almond flour; unblanched almond meal', 'Nut and seed derivatives', 'Almond', 'Coarsely ground almonds, often with skins retained. The term overlaps heavily with almond flour and is already captured as a synonym under UIL-0098.', 'Almond kernels.', 'Adds texture, fat, protein and moisture to baking and coatings.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Provides unsaturated fat, protein, fibre and minerals.', 'Moderate.', 'High, mainly unsaturated fat.', 'Low to moderate; naturally low in sugars.', 'Moderate.', 'Usually low compared with cereal flour, but energy density and portion remain relevant.', 'Fibre and fat may support fullness; large portions can cause digestive discomfort in some people.', 'No general inflammatory effect established.', 'Contains almond, one of the specifically named regulated tree-nut allergens.', 'People with almond or tree-nut allergy; those monitoring energy-dense foods.', 'Gluten-free baking; macarons; cakes; coatings; snack products.', 'Almond meal; ground almonds; almond flour.', 'Other ground seeds where nut avoidance is required, subject to allergy needs.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; cross-contact matters', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Linked variant — canonical profile UIL-0098', 'High', 'Almond must be clearly named and emphasised as a regulated allergen.', 'Almond meal is usually a coarser or skin-on form of almond flour, not a completely separate ingredient family.', 'almond meal; ground almonds; unblanched almond meal', 'almond meel; almon meal', 'Almond Flour UIL-0098; almonds; defatted almond flour', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cold-pressed-rapeseed-oil', 'UIL-0231', 'Cold-Pressed Rapeseed Oil', 'Virgin rapeseed oil; cold pressed canola oil; extra virgin rapeseed oil', 'Oils and fats', 'Rapeseed oil', 'Oil mechanically extracted from rapeseeds at relatively low temperatures, then filtered; it is less refined than standard deodorised rapeseed oil.', 'Rapeseeds, commonly low-erucic-acid food varieties.', 'Adds fat, moisture and flavour; used for dressings, cooking and finishing.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Almost entirely fat, with mainly unsaturated fatty acids and some vitamin E; exact composition varies.', 'None.', 'Very high; predominantly unsaturated fat.', 'None.', 'None.', 'No direct carbohydrate effect; energy density still matters.', 'Generally tolerated; fat quantity can affect symptoms in people with fat-malabsorption or gallbladder conditions.', 'Replacing saturated fat with unsaturated fat is generally favoured; no special anti-inflammatory claim should be made for every product.', 'Rapeseed allergy is uncommon; not one of the 14 regulated allergens.', 'People managing total energy intake or requiring low-fat diets for a clinical reason.', 'Dressings; marinades; mayonnaise; cooking oils; premium crisps and sauces.', 'Cold-pressed rapeseed oil; virgin rapeseed oil; cold pressed canola oil.', 'Extra virgin olive oil or other unsaturated oils according to taste and cooking use; no universal winner.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Less-refined unsaturated culinary oil; linked to UIL-0009', 'High', 'Food oils must meet applicable compositional and safety requirements; allergen declarations depend on the actual product.', 'Cold-pressed rapeseed oil is a distinct processing form of rapeseed oil, but it is still energy-dense fat. Its main advantage is flavour and less refining, not magic health properties.', 'Cold-Pressed Rapeseed Oil; cold pressed rapeseed oil; cold-pressed canola oil; virgin rapeseed oil', 'cold press rapeseed oil; rape seed oil', 'Rapeseed Oil UIL-0009; olive oil; sunflower oil', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/different-fats-nutrition/', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('whole-milk', 'UIL-0232', 'Whole Milk', 'Full-fat milk; full cream milk; whole cows milk', 'Dairy ingredients', 'Cow milk', 'Cow’s milk with its natural fat largely retained, typically standardised to meet whole-milk composition requirements.', 'Milk from cows.', 'Used as a drink and to add moisture, protein, fat, lactose and creaminess to foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Provides protein, fat, lactose, calcium, iodine and several vitamins; values vary.', 'High-quality complete protein.', 'Moderate, including saturated fat.', 'Contains lactose as the main carbohydrate.', 'None.', 'Lactose produces a moderate glucose response; portion matters.', 'Lactose may cause symptoms in people with lactose intolerance; milk proteins are separate from lactose.', 'Milk is not generally inflammatory for the population; allergy is an immune reaction and intolerance is different.', 'Contains milk, a regulated allergen. Lactose intolerance does not equal milk allergy.', 'People with milk allergy, lactose intolerance or those monitoring saturated fat and energy intake.', 'Drinks; sauces; cereals; bakery; desserts; soups; ready meals.', 'Whole milk; full-fat milk; full cream milk; milk.', 'Semi-skimmed milk where lower fat is desired; fortified unsweetened alternatives where dairy avoidance is required, checking protein and iodine.', 'No', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; compound products may vary', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Nutrient-dense dairy food; allergy and lactose distinctions matter', 'High', 'Milk must be declared and emphasised as an allergen. Reserved dairy descriptions and compositional standards may apply.', 'Whole milk provides useful protein and micronutrients, but it also contains lactose and more saturated fat than lower-fat milk.', 'whole milk; full fat milk; full cream milk; cows milk', 'hole milk; fullfat milk', 'Semi-skimmed milk; skimmed milk; whole milk powder', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-