  ('whole-egg', 'UIL-0233', 'Whole Egg', 'Liquid whole egg; shell egg; beaten whole egg; pasteurised whole egg', 'Egg ingredients', 'Hen egg', 'The yolk and white of an egg used together, either from shell eggs or as pasteurised liquid egg.', 'Usually hens’ eggs.', 'Adds protein, fat, emulsification, colour, structure and binding.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Provides high-quality protein, fat, choline and several vitamins and minerals.', 'High-quality complete protein.', 'Moderate, concentrated in the yolk.', 'Very low.', 'None.', 'Low direct impact.', 'Generally well tolerated unless allergic; fat and protein can slow digestion of a mixed meal.', 'Egg is not generally inflammatory; egg allergy is an immune reaction.', 'Contains egg, a regulated allergen.', 'People with egg allergy; those needing product-specific advice on raw or lightly cooked egg safety.', 'Bakery; pasta; mayonnaise; quiche; coatings; ready meals.', 'Egg; whole egg; liquid whole egg; pasteurised egg.', 'Flax or aquafaba may replace some functions in vegan recipes, but nutritional and functional results differ.', 'No', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; check compound products', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Nutrient-dense whole-food ingredient and regulated allergen', 'High', 'Egg must be clearly named and emphasised as a regulated allergen.', 'Whole egg is nutritionally different from egg powder or isolated egg white. It provides protein, fat and useful micronutrients, while allergy remains the main safety issue.', 'whole egg; liquid whole egg; shell egg; pasteurised egg', 'hole egg; whole eg', 'Dried whole egg; egg white; egg yolk', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('beef', 'UIL-0234', 'Beef', 'Beef meat; bovine meat; minced beef; diced beef', 'Meat and poultry ingredients', 'Cattle meat', 'Edible muscle and associated tissues from cattle. Fat content varies greatly by cut and preparation.', 'Cattle.', 'Provides protein, flavour, texture, iron and vitamin B12.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'High-quality protein, haem iron, zinc and vitamin B12; fat varies by cut.', 'High-quality complete protein.', 'Variable from lean to high; saturated fat rises with fattier cuts.', 'None unless coatings or sauces are added.', 'None.', 'Low direct impact.', 'Generally tolerated; high-fat portions may be harder to digest for some people.', 'No basis for labelling plain beef as inherently inflammatory; dietary pattern, processing and amount matter.', 'Beef allergy is uncommon; alpha-gal syndrome and cross-reactivity can occur.', 'People with beef allergy, alpha-gal syndrome, or those limiting saturated fat or red-meat intake on professional advice.', 'Fresh meals; mince dishes; burgers; pies; ready meals; stocks.', 'Beef; beef meat; minced beef; diced beef.', 'Leaner cuts, smaller portions, poultry, fish or pulses depending on nutritional and dietary goals.', 'No', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; processed beef products may contain wheat or other allergens', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Protein- and micronutrient-rich whole food; cut and processing matter', 'High', 'Species and ingredient composition must be described accurately; compound meat products must list added ingredients and allergens.', 'Plain beef is different from a highly processed burger or cured meat. Judge the cut, fat level, portion and full ingredient list.', 'beef; beef meat; minced beef; diced beef; bovine meat', 'beaf; meet beef', 'Veal; beef fat; beef stock; collagen', 'Preservatives, phosphates or flavourings may occur in processed beef products, not plain beef', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('salmon', 'UIL-0235', 'Salmon', 'Atlantic salmon; Pacific salmon; salmon fillet; farmed salmon; wild salmon', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'Salmon fish', 'An oily fish used fresh, frozen, canned, smoked or as an ingredient.', 'Salmon species including Salmo salar and Pacific Oncorhynchus species.', 'Provides protein, fat, flavour and omega-3 fatty acids.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'High-quality protein, long-chain omega-3 fats, vitamin D, selenium and vitamin B12; levels vary by species and farming.', 'High-quality complete protein.', 'Moderate to high, rich in unsaturated fat including EPA and DHA.', 'None when plain.', 'None.', 'Low direct impact.', 'Generally tolerated unless allergic; smoked or heavily salted forms differ from plain salmon.', 'Oily fish is not generally considered inflammatory; omega-3 content is nutritionally relevant, but no single food cures inflammation.', 'Contains fish, a regulated allergen.', 'People with fish allergy; those limiting salt should distinguish plain from smoked or cured salmon.', 'Fresh meals; sushi; fishcakes; pâté; sandwiches; ready meals; canned fish.', 'Salmon; Atlantic salmon; salmon fillet; smoked salmon.', 'Other oily fish such as sardines, mackerel or trout; plant alternatives do not provide identical EPA/DHA.', 'No', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; coatings and sauces may contain gluten', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Nutrient-dense oily fish and regulated allergen', 'High', 'Fish must be clearly named and emphasised as a regulated allergen.', 'Plain salmon provides protein and omega-3 fats. Smoking, curing, breading and sauces can change the salt, additives and allergen profile.', 'salmon; atlantic salmon; salmon fillet; farmed salmon; wild salmon', 'samon; salman', 'Trout; mackerel; fish oil', 'Smoke flavourings, preservatives or phosphates may occur in processed products', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-aller