  ('vanilla-bean', 'UIL-0239', 'Vanilla Bean', 'Vanilla pod; vanilla pods; whole vanilla bean; cured vanilla pod', 'Flavouring food ingredients', 'Vanilla orchid fruit', 'The cured seed pod of vanilla orchids, used whole, split, scraped or ground for flavour.', 'Primarily Vanilla planifolia or related vanilla species.', 'Adds natural vanilla aroma, flavour and visible seeds.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Used in small amounts; negligible macronutritional contribution.', 'Negligible.', 'Negligible.', 'Very low at culinary doses.', 'Very low per serving.', 'Low direct impact.', 'Generally tolerated; contact sensitivity or allergy is uncommon.', 'No general inflammatory effect established.', 'Vanilla allergy or contact sensitivity is rare but possible.', 'People with a known vanilla allergy or those distinguishing genuine vanilla from generic flavouring.', 'Custards; ice cream; bakery; desserts; drinks; confectionery.', 'Vanilla bean; vanilla pod; vanilla seeds.', 'Vanilla extract or powder where more practical; imitation flavour is a different ingredient.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Whole botanical flavouring ingredient', 'High', 'Food labelling must not mislead consumers about the presence or amount of real vanilla; flavouring rules may apply to claims.', 'Vanilla bean is the whole cured spice. It is different from vanilla flavouring, vanillin and sweetened vanilla paste.', 'vanilla bean; vanilla pod; vanilla seeds; whole vanilla bean', 'vanila bean; vanilla been', 'Vanilla extract; vanilla powder; vanillin', 'None inherent', 'https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/flavouring_authorisations/guidance; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('tomato-ketchup', 'UIL-0240', 'Tomato Ketchup', 'Ketchup; tomato sauce; red sauce', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Tomato-based condiment', 'A formulated condiment usually made from tomatoes or tomato concentrate, vinegar, sugar, salt and seasonings. Recipes vary considerably.', 'Tomatoes plus other recipe ingredients.', 'Adds sweet, acidic, salty tomato flavour and moisture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Provides tomato solids but may also contribute meaningful free sugar and salt.', 'Low.', 'Usually low, though formulations vary.', 'Moderate; much is commonly added sugar.', 'Usually low.', 'Can raise blood glucose depending on sugar content and serving size, though typical portions are small.', 'Acidity may aggravate reflux; onion or garlic can affect people sensitive to FODMAPs.', 'No single inflammatory classification is justified; sugar, salt, portion and overall diet matter.', 'Recipes may contain celery, mustard, sulphites or other regulated allergens; always check the label.', 'People limiting salt or free sugars, those with reflux, and people with specific sauce allergens.', 'Burgers; chips; sandwiches; marinades; sauces; ready meals.', 'Tomato ketchup; ketchup; tomato sauce.', 'Lower-salt or no-added-sugar ketchup; tomato paste, passata or homemade sauce depending on use.', 'Usually', 'Usually', 'Often gluten-free, but check each product', 'Context dependent', 'Compound condiment — assess sugar, salt and full recipe', 'High', 'All component ingredients and regulated allergens must be declared; nutrition and claims rules apply.', 'Ketchup contains tomato, but it is not nutritionally the same as tomatoes. Compare the sugar, salt and ingredient list between brands.', 'tomato ketchup; ketchup; tomato sauce; red sauce', 'tomato catchup; ketcup; ketchip', 'Tomato paste; tomato purée; barbecue sauce', 'Preservatives, thickeners, flavourings or sweeteners may occur depending on brand', 'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/salt-in-your-diet/; ht