  ('lactic-acid-bacteria-culture', 'UIL-0242', 'Lactic Acid Bacteria Culture', 'LAB culture; starter culture; lactic culture; bacterial starter culture', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Microbial culture', 'A selected culture of bacteria used to ferment food by converting sugars mainly into lactic acid. Effects and properties are strain-specific.', 'Food-grade bacterial strains such as Lactobacillus-related genera, Lactococcus, Streptococcus thermophilus or others.', 'Starts fermentation; develops acidity, flavour and texture; can support preservation.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually contributes negligible macronutrients at use levels.', 'Negligible.', 'Negligible.', 'May consume sugars during fermentation; contribution depends on finished food.', 'Negligible directly.', 'Usually low direct impact; finished fermented food varies.', 'Tolerance depends on the finished food; live cultures may not remain viable after processing.', 'No general anti-inflammatory claim should be made for an unspecified culture.', 'Not itself one of the 14 regulated allergens, but growth media or the finished food may involve allergens.', 'People with severe immunocompromise should seek clinical advice before using concentrated live-culture products; ordinary fermented foods are product-specific.', 'Yoghurt, cheese, fermented vegetables, sourdough, cultured drinks and meat fermentation.', 'Lactic culture; starter culture; bacterial culture; live cultures', 'A clearly identified strain and product-specific information where a probiotic effect is claimed.', 'Source dependent', 'Usually', 'No inherent gluten, but carrier or growth medium may vary.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Neutral — functional fermentation culture', 'High', 'Health or probiotic claims must not be inferred from the generic term alone.', 'A lactic culture tells you how a food was fermented, not that it automatically has a proven probiotic benefit.', 'lactic acid bacteria culture|LAB culture|starter culture|lactic culture