  ('vitamin-a', 'UIL-0243', 'Vitamin A', 'Retinol; retinyl acetate; retinyl palmitate; beta-carotene (provitamin A)', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Fat-soluble vitamin', 'A fat-soluble vitamin involved in vision, immune function and normal cell development. Food labels may use preformed retinol forms or provitamin A carotenoids.', 'Naturally present in animal foods and carotenoid-rich plants; also added as permitted vitamin compounds.', 'Fortifies foods and supplements to increase vitamin A content.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Vitamin A activity; no energy contribution.', 'None.', 'Fat-soluble but does not itself contribute dietary fat.', 'None.', 'None directly.', 'No direct blood sugar effect.', 'No direct fibre or gut contribution.', 'Deficiency and excess both matter; no simple inflammation rating is appropriate.', 'Excess preformed vitamin A can be harmful; beta-carotene is not equivalent to retinol in risk profile.', 'Pregnant people or those trying to conceive should avoid excessive retinol; people taking supplements or liver products should watch cumulative intake.', 'Fortified spreads, cereals, dairy alternatives, supplements, liver and some dairy products.', 'Vitamin A; retinol; retinyl acetate; retinyl palmitate; beta-carotene', 'Meet needs mainly through a balanced diet; use supplements only as appropriate.', 'Source dependent', 'Source dependent', 'No inherent gluten.', 'Context dependent', 'Context-dependent — essential nutrient with excess risk', 'High', 'Only authorised vitamin sources may be added to foods; nutrition and health claims are regulated.', 'Vitamin A is essential, but more is not always better. Preformed retinol and beta-carotene should not be treated as identical.', 'vitamin a|retinol|retinyl acetate|retinyl palmitate|beta carotene', 'vitamin-a|retinol palmitate', 'Beta-Carotene; Liver; Fortified Foods', 'May appear with antioxidants or carriers in premixes.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-supplements-guidance/food-supplemen