  ('l-tyrosine', 'UIL-0245', 'L-Tyrosine', 'Tyrosine; L-tyrosine amino acid', 'Amino acids and functional nutrition', 'Amino acid', 'An amino acid used by the body to make proteins and as a precursor for several signalling molecules. It is naturally present in protein foods and may also be added in purified form.', 'Protein-containing foods or industrially produced food-grade amino acid.', 'Adds amino acid content to supplements, medical nutrition or specialised formulations.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Amino acid/protein-related contribution.', 'Direct amino acid contribution, but not a complete protein.', 'None.', 'None.', 'None.', 'No direct blood sugar effect.', 'No direct fibre contribution; high supplemental doses may cause gastrointestinal symptoms in some people.', 'No general anti-inflammatory effect established.', 'Not one of the 14 regulated allergens, but source materials and product allergens should be checked.', 'People taking thyroid medication, levodopa, monoamine oxidase inhibitors or with relevant medical conditions should seek professional advice before supplements.', 'Sports supplements, nootropic-style products, medical nutrition and protein formulations.', 'L-tyrosine; tyrosine', 'Protein-rich foods where appropriate; supplements should have a clear purpose.', 'Source dependent', 'Usually', 'No inherent gluten.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Caution — functional amino acid, dose and context matter', 'Limited', 'Food supplements cannot claim to treat or prevent disease; product-specific safety and labelling rules apply.', 'L-tyrosine is a real amino acid, but that does not make every focus, mood or performance claim proven.', 'l-tyrosine|tyrosine|l tyrosine', 'l-tyrosene|tyrosene', 'Protein; Phenylalanine; Amino Acid Blend', 'May appear with caffeine, vitamins or other amino acids.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-supplements-guidance/food-supplements-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/nutrition-healt