  ('rock-salt', 'UIL-0248', 'Rock Salt', 'Halite salt; mined salt; pink salt; Himalayan salt', 'Salt and savoury bases', 'Sodium chloride', 'Food-grade salt mined from underground deposits. Colour and trace minerals vary by source, but it remains mainly sodium chloride.', 'Natural mineral deposits, then crushed, cleaned and graded.', 'Adds salty taste; supports preservation, fermentation and texture.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Sodium and chloride; no energy.', 'None.', 'None.', 'None.', 'None.', 'No direct glucose effect.', 'High salt intake may increase thirst; no fibre or probiotic benefit.', 'Excess sodium intake is associated with raised blood pressure risk; colour does not remove this concern.', 'Not an allergen. Additives such as anti-caking agents may be present in some products.', 'People managing blood pressure, kidney disease or total sodium intake.', 'Seasonings, cured foods, snacks, bakery and cooking salt.', 'Rock salt; pink salt; Himalayan salt; halite salt', 'Use less salt overall; herbs, spices, acid and aromatics can add flavour.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Amber — simple ingredient with sodium-load concern', 'High', 'Salt labelling and nutrition information must not imply unsupported health superiority.', 'Rock salt may look less processed, but it is still mainly sodium chloride. The amount matters more than the colour.', 'rock salt|pink salt|himalayan salt|halite salt', 'rocksalt|himalyan salt', 'Sea Salt; Table Salt; Sodium Chloride', 'May contain anti-caking agents depending on product.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/others/; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/nutrition-health-claims-and-supplement-labelling', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
