  ('dried-apple', 'UIL-0250', 'Dried Apple', 'Dehydrated apple; apple pieces dried; apple flakes', 'Fruit ingredients', 'Apple', 'Apple with much of its water removed. It may be plain, treated with sulphites or infused with sugar or juice concentrate.', 'Fresh apple, dried by hot air, freeze-drying or other dehydration methods.', 'Adds fruit pieces, sweetness, flavour, chew and shelf stability.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Concentrated carbohydrate, natural sugars and some fibre.', 'Low.', 'Low.', 'Higher sugar density per gram than fresh apple because water is removed.', 'Usually retains fibre, though structure and amount vary.', 'Moderate per gram; portion size and added sugars matter.', 'Can contribute fibre; dried fruit may cause bloating in sensitive people and is higher in fermentable carbohydrates.', 'No unique inflammatory effect established.', 'Apple allergy is possible; sulphites must be declared above the legal threshold.', 'People monitoring sugar portions, those with IBS/FODMAP sensitivity, apple allergy or sulphite sensitivity.', 'Cereals, snack bars, bakery, stuffing, teas and fruit mixes.', 'Dried apple; dehydrated apple; apple pieces; apple flakes', 'Fresh apple for lower energy density; unsweetened dried apple when shelf-stable fruit is needed.', 'Usually', 'Yes', 'No inherent gluten; cross-contact and added ingredients vary.', 'Context dependent', 'Green/amber — useful fruit ingredient, concentrated by drying', 'High', 'Added sugar and sulphites must be declared as applicable.', 'Dried apple keeps some whole-fruit fibre, but removing water concentrates its sugars and makes portions easier to underestimate.', 'dried apple|dehydrated apple|apple flakes|dried apple pieces', 'dried appel|dehydrated appel', 'Apple Pieces; Apple Purée; Apple Juice Concentrate', 'Sulphites or added sugars may be present.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-inf