  ('toasted-wheat-flakes', 'UIL-0252', 'Toasted Wheat Flakes', 'Toasted wheat cereal flakes; crisp wheat flakes', 'Cereal and grain derivatives', 'Wheat flakes', 'Wheat flakes that have been heat-treated or toasted to develop flavour, crispness and shelf stability. They may be plain or sweetened.', 'Wheat grain, usually rolled or formed then toasted.', 'Adds crunch, cereal flavour and visual texture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mostly carbohydrate; wholegrain versions can provide fibre and micronutrients.', 'Low to moderate.', 'Usually low unless oil-coated.', 'Moderate to high starch; added sugars vary.', 'Depends on wholegrain content and processing.', 'Usually moderate to high; final product and portion matter.', 'Wholegrain versions can support fibre intake; refined flakes contribute less.', 'No unique inflammatory effect established; gluten is the key concern for affected people.', 'Contains wheat and gluten; may be made on lines handling other allergens.', 'People with coeliac disease, wheat allergy or those monitoring added sugar.', 'Breakfast cereals, granola, snack bars and bakery toppings.', 'Toasted wheat flakes; crisp wheat flakes; wheat cereal flakes', 'Plain wholegrain flakes with little added sugar where appropriate.', 'Formulation dependent', 'Usually', 'Contains wheat/gluten.', 'Context dependent', 'Amber — cereal ingredient, quality depends on wholegrain and coating', 'High', 'Wheat must be declared and emphasised as a regulated allergen.', 'Toasting changes texture and flavour, but the main questions remain: wholegrain or refined, plain or coated, and how much sugar is added.', 'toasted wheat flakes|crisp wheat flakes|wheat cereal flakes', 'toasted wheet flakes|wheat flaks', 'Wheat Flakes; Rolled Wheat; Breakfast Cereal', 'May include sugar, malt extract, oils or emulsifiers in compound forms.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information