  ('high-oleic-rapeseed-oil', 'UIL-0257', 'High-Oleic Rapeseed Oil', 'High oleic canola oil; HOLL rapeseed oil; high-oleic low-linolenic rapeseed oil', 'Oils and fats', 'Rapeseed oil', 'Rapeseed oil from varieties selected for a higher proportion of oleic acid and often lower linolenic acid, improving heat and oxidation stability.', 'High-oleic rapeseed varieties; usually refined for commercial food use.', 'Provides frying stability, shelf life, texture and neutral flavour.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Fat and energy; mainly monounsaturated fat.', 'None.', 'High; fatty-acid profile is generally richer in oleic acid than standard rapeseed oil.', 'None.', 'None.', 'No direct blood sugar effect, though energy density matters.', 'No fibre; generally well tolerated.', 'Replacing saturated fats with unsaturated fats may improve lipid profiles, but the whole food and frying conditions matter.', 'Rapeseed is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; fully refined oils generally contain very little protein, but product-specific advice matters for allergy.', 'People monitoring total energy intake or repeatedly heated fried-food consumption.', 'Fried snacks, bakery, dressings, mayonnaise and commercial frying.', 'High-oleic rapeseed oil; HOLL rapeseed oil; high oleic canola oil', 'Cold-pressed rapeseed or extra virgin olive oil for flavour; high-oleic oils can be suitable for higher-heat use.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free.', 'Context dependent', 'Amber/green — unsaturated oil, context and use matter', 'High', 'Must not be marketed with unsupported disease claims; nutrition claims require legal criteria.', 'High-oleic rapeseed oil is designed to be more stable and rich in monounsaturated fat. It does not make a fried or ultra-processed product healthy by itself.', 'High-Oleic Rapeseed Oil; high oleic rapeseed oil; HOLL rapeseed oil; high oleic canola oil', 'high-oleic rape seed oil|hol rapeseed oil', 'Rapeseed Oil; Cold-Pressed Rapeseed Oil; High-Oleic Sunflower Oil', 'Antioxidants suc