  ('semi-skimmed-milk', 'UIL-0258', 'Semi-Skimmed Milk', 'Reduced-fat milk; partly skimmed milk; 1.5–1.8% milk', 'Dairy ingredients', 'Cow’s milk', 'Cow’s milk with part of its fat removed, while retaining milk protein, lactose and many micronutrients.', 'Cow’s milk, separated and standardised to the required fat level.', 'Used as a drink and ingredient; adds protein, lactose, minerals, moisture and dairy flavour.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Protein, lactose, calcium and other micronutrients with less fat than whole milk.', 'Moderate, high-quality complete protein.', 'Lower than whole milk; still contains some saturated fat.', 'Contains lactose, a natural milk sugar.', 'None.', 'Usually low to moderate depending on portion and food context.', 'Lactose may cause symptoms in lactose intolerance; milk proteins trigger milk allergy.', 'No simple inflammation rating; tolerance and dietary pattern matter.', 'Milk is a regulated allergen. Contains lactose.', 'People with milk allergy, lactose intolerance or those monitoring saturated fat.', 'Drinks, cereals, sauces, tea, coffee, desserts and cooking.', 'Semi-skimmed milk; partly skimmed milk; reduced-fat milk', 'Unsweetened fortified alternatives for those avoiding milk; whole or skimmed milk depending on dietary need.', 'No', 'Yes', 'No inherent gluten.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Green/amber — nutrient-rich basic food with allergen relevance', 'High', 'Milk must be declared as a regulated allergen. Reserved descriptions and compositional rules apply to milk categories.', 'Semi-skimmed milk keeps the protein and lactose of milk while reducing some of the fat. Milk allergy and lactose intolerance are different issues.', 'semi skimmed milk|semi-skimmed milk|partly skimmed milk|reduced fat milk', 'semi skim milk|semiskimmed milk', 'Whole Milk; Skimmed Milk; Milk Powder', 'None inherently.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling