  ('liquid-whole-egg', 'UIL-0259', 'Liquid Whole Egg', 'Pasteurised liquid whole egg; whole egg liquid; liquid egg', 'Egg ingredients', 'Whole egg', 'Egg yolk and white blended in their natural proportions and sold as a liquid, usually pasteurised for food manufacturing or catering.', 'Hen eggs or other bird eggs; species should be clear where relevant.', 'Provides binding, emulsification, structure, colour, richness and protein.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Protein, fat, choline and micronutrients.', 'Moderate to high, complete protein.', 'Moderate; mainly from yolk.', 'Very low.', 'None.', 'Usually low.', 'Generally well tolerated unless allergic; pasteurisation improves microbiological safety but does not remove allergenicity.', 'No unique inflammatory effect established.', 'Egg is a regulated allergen and must be declared.', 'People with egg allergy; vulnerable groups should follow product storage and cooking instructions.', 'Bakery, mayonnaise, sauces, ready meals, pasta and catering products.', 'Liquid whole egg; pasteurised whole egg; whole egg liquid', 'Shell whole egg for home cooking where practical; egg alternatives for allergy or vegan use.', 'No', 'Yes', 'No inherent gluten.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Green/amber — useful whole-food ingredient with allergen relevance', 'High', 'Egg must be named and emphasised as a regulated allergen; pasteurisation does not remove allergy risk.', 'Liquid whole egg is simply the yolk and white in a convenient pasteurised form. It should link to the whole-egg profile, not be treated as a new nutritional category.', 'liquid whole egg|pasteurised whole egg|whole egg liquid|liquid egg', 'liquid hole egg|pasteurized whole egg', 'Whole Egg; Egg Yolk; Egg White; Egg Powder', 'May include permitted processing aids or stabilisation depending on supplier.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('beef-mince', 'UIL-0260', 'Beef Mince', 'Minced beef; ground beef; beef mince meat', 'Meat and poultry ingredients', 'Beef', 'Beef muscle and associated fat mechanically minced. Fat content varies widely and may be declared by percentage or product category.', 'Cuts and trimmings from cattle.', 'Provides protein, flavour and structure for burgers, meatballs, sauces and fillings.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Protein, fat, iron, zinc and vitamin B12; amounts vary with fat level.', 'High, complete protein.', 'Low to high depending on mince fat percentage; saturated fat rises with total fat.', 'None unless combined with fillers or sauces.', 'None.', 'No direct carbohydrate effect.', 'No fibre; handling and cooking are important for microbiological safety.', 'Evidence differs for unprocessed red meat and processed meat; amount and dietary pattern matter.', 'Beef is not one of the 14 regulated allergens, though rare meat allergy can occur. Compound mince products may contain wheat, egg, milk or soya.', 'People monitoring saturated fat, red-meat intake or with alpha-gal/meat allergy diagnosed by a clinician.', 'Bolognese, burgers, meatballs, pies, chilli and ready meals.', 'Beef mince; minced beef; ground beef', 'Leaner mince, whole cuts, poultry, fish or pulses depending on the dish and dietary goal.', 'No', 'No', 'Plain beef mince is gluten-free; formed or seasoned products may not be.', 'Context dependent', 'Green/amber — whole-food protein, fat level and processing matter', 'High', 'Plain mince and a formulated beef burger are not the same product; added ingredients and allergens must be declared.', 'Beef mince is still plain beef when nothing else is added. Check the fat percentage and whether the product contains fillers, seasoning or preservatives.', 'beef mince|minced beef|ground beef|beef mince meat', 'beef minse|minced beaf', 'Beef; Lean Beef Mince; Beef Burger', 'Formulated products may contain preservatives, phosphates, breadcrumbs or flavourings.', 'http