  ('smoked-salmon', 'UIL-0261', 'Smoked Salmon', 'Cold-smoked salmon; hot-smoked salmon; smoked salmon slices', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'Salmon', 'Salmon preserved and flavoured by salting and exposure to smoke. Cold-smoked and hot-smoked products differ in cooking, texture and microbiological handling.', 'Salmon fish, salt and smoke or smoke condensate; recipes may include sugar or other seasonings.', 'Provides fish protein, omega-3 fats, savoury flavour and extended refrigerated shelf life.', 'Processed ingredient', 'High-quality protein, fat including long-chain omega-3, vitamin B12 and selenium; usually high in salt.', 'High, complete animal protein.', 'Moderate; includes EPA and DHA, but total fat varies by species and cut.', 'Usually low; some cures contain added sugar.', 'None.', 'Low direct effect unless served with carbohydrate-rich foods or sweet cure.', 'No fibre. Salt level and cold-chain safety matter; vulnerable groups should follow current food-safety advice.', 'Omega-3 intake may support cardiovascular health, but smoking and high salt mean it should not be treated as identical to fresh salmon.', 'Fish is one of the 14 regulated allergens. Histamine-sensitive people may react to some fish products.', 'People with fish allergy, those limiting salt, pregnant or immunocompromised people following food-safety guidance.', 'Sandwiches, salads, bagels, canapés, breakfast dishes and ready meals.', 'Smoked salmon; cold-smoked salmon; hot-smoked salmon; salmon (fish)', 'Fresh or frozen salmon for less salt; lower-salt smoked salmon where available.', 'No', 'No', 'Plain smoked salmon is gluten-free; marinades and flavourings must be checked.', 'Context dependent', 'Amber — nutrient-rich fish, but salt and processing matter', 'High', 'Salmon must be clearly identified as fish for allergen labelling. Product-level ingredients and storage instructions take priority.', 'Smoked salmon provides useful protein and omega-3 fats, but it is also a salted processe