  ('potato-protein-isolate', 'UIL-0262', 'Potato Protein Isolate', 'Potato protein; potato protein concentrate; potato protein isolate', 'Protein concentrates and isolates', 'Potato', 'A concentrated protein fraction separated from potato juice during starch processing and dried into a powder.', 'Potatoes, commonly as a co-product of potato starch manufacture.', 'Raises protein content; improves binding, foaming, water retention and texture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Concentrated plant protein with little of the whole potato carbohydrate or fibre.', 'High; amino-acid profile is relatively complete for a plant protein, but quality depends on processing and use.', 'Usually low.', 'Usually low, though specifications vary.', 'Very low or none.', 'Low direct carbohydrate effect; finished product composition matters.', 'Removes most whole-potato structure; tolerance is usually product-specific.', 'No strong evidence of unique inflammatory harm in normal food use.', 'Potato is not one of the 14 regulated allergens, but rare allergy is possible. Cross-contact and compound formulations must be checked.', 'People with diagnosed potato allergy or those comparing highly processed protein ingredients.', 'Plant-based meats, protein foods, bakery products, sports nutrition and emulsified foods.', 'Potato protein; potato protein isolate; potato protein concentrate', 'Whole pulses, eggs, dairy, fish or less-refined plant proteins depending on diet and product purpose.', 'Check manufacturer', 'Usually', 'Naturally gluten-free; cross-contact must be controlled for a gluten-free claim.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Amber — concentrated protein, useful function but little whole-food structure', 'Limited', 'The ingredient name should reflect the actual specification; isolate and concentrate are not always interchangeable.', 'Potato protein isolate is a concentrated functional protein, not powdered whole potato. It can be useful, but its presence does not make the finished product 