  ('acacia-fibre', 'UIL-0263', 'Acacia Fibre', 'Acacia gum fibre; gum arabic fibre; soluble acacia fibre; acacia senegal fibre', 'Fibres and prebiotic ingredients', 'Acacia Gum', 'A soluble, fermentable fibre obtained from dried exudate of Acacia trees. It is closely related to gum arabic used as a food additive and fibre source.', 'Acacia senegal or related permitted Acacia species.', 'Adds soluble fibre; provides mild thickening and stabilisation; supports texture and fibre claims.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Soluble fermentable fibre with low digestible carbohydrate contribution.', 'Negligible.', 'None.', 'Chemically carbohydrate, but largely not digested as available sugar.', 'High soluble fibre.', 'Generally low direct glycaemic contribution; the finished food remains decisive.', 'Fermented by gut microbes; may support stool regularity, but higher amounts can cause gas, bloating or discomfort.', 'Human evidence for specific anti-inflammatory effects is limited and should not be overstated.', 'Not one of the 14 regulated allergens. Rare hypersensitivity is possible.', 'People with sensitive digestion, IBS or those rapidly increasing fibre intake.', 'Fibre powders, bars, drinks, supplements, bakery products and confectionery.', 'Acacia fibre; soluble acacia fibre; gum arabic; acacia gum', 'Whole pulses, oats, fruit, vegetables, nuts and seeds for fibre plus wider nutrients.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; verify cross-contact.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Green/amber — useful soluble fibre, but dose and tolerance matter', 'Moderate', 'Depending on use and jurisdiction, acacia gum may also be identified as gum arabic or E414; fibre claims must meet applicable conditions.', 'Acacia fibre is a genuine soluble fibre, but it is still an isolated ingredient. Start gradually if you are sensitive to fermentable fibres.', 'acacia fibre|acacia fiber|soluble acacia fibre|gum arabic fibre|acacia gum', 'acacia fibar|accacia fibre|acacia fiber', 'Gum Arabic; Inulin; Chicory Root Fibre', 'E414 Gum Arabic', 'https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('natural-cocoa-powder', 'UIL-0264', 'Natural Cocoa Powder', 'Non-alkalised cocoa powder; natural cacao powder; untreated cocoa powder', 'Cocoa and chocolate ingredients', 'Cocoa Powder', 'Cocoa solids ground into powder without alkalisation. It is naturally acidic and differs from Dutch-processed or alkalised cocoa.', 'Roasted cocoa beans after much of the cocoa butter is pressed out.', 'Adds cocoa flavour, colour and dry solids to baking, drinks and confectionery.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Cocoa solids, fibre and polyphenols; some protein, minerals and residual fat.', 'Low to moderate.', 'Low to moderate depending on residual cocoa butter.', 'Usually low in sugar when unsweetened; carbohydrate includes fibre.', 'Moderate to high for a powder.', 'Unsweetened cocoa has low direct sugar impact; sweetened products differ greatly.', 'Provides fibre and polyphenols; large amounts may be stimulating or irritant for some people.', 'Cocoa polyphenol research is promising, but effects depend on dose and the whole product.', 'Cocoa is not one of the 14 regulated allergens. Products may contain or contact milk, nuts or soya.', 'People sensitive to caffeine/theobromine, reflux, migraines or compound-product allergens.', 'Cakes, brownies, hot cocoa, cereals, protein products and confectionery.', 'Cocoa powder; natural cocoa powder; non-alkalised cocoa', 'Unsweetened cocoa with minimal added sugar; cacao nibs for more structure.', 'Formulation dependent', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; cross-contact must be checked.', 'Context dependent', 'Green/amber — useful cocoa solids; judge the added sugar and formulation', 'Moderate', 'Do not collapse natural cocoa and alkalised cocoa into one scanner result because acidity and processing differ.', 'Natural cocoa powder is unsweetened cocoa that has not been alkalised. It is very different from a sugary hot-chocolate mix.', 'natural cocoa powder|non alkalised cocoa|non-alkalized cocoa|natural cacao powder|cocoa powder', 'coco powder|co