  ('yoghurt-culture', 'UIL-0268', 'Yoghurt Culture', 'Yogurt culture; starter culture; live yoghurt cultures; Streptococcus thermophilus and Lactobacillus delbrueckii subsp. bulgaricus', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Lactic Acid Bacteria Culture', 'A starter culture used to ferment milk into yoghurt, traditionally including Streptococcus thermophilus and Lactobacillus delbrueckii subsp. bulgaricus. Additional strains may be added.', 'Selected food-grade bacterial strains grown under controlled conditions.', 'Ferments lactose into lactic acid; thickens milk; develops yoghurt flavour and helps preservation.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Used in tiny amounts; contribution is functional rather than nutritional.', 'Negligible direct contribution.', 'None.', 'Consumes some lactose during fermentation; final lactose depends on product and storage.', 'None.', 'Culture itself has no meaningful effect; the finished yoghurt and added sugars matter.', 'Live-culture effects are strain- and dose-specific. A culture name alone does not prove a probiotic benefit.', 'Strain-specific research exists, but generic health claims should not be inferred.', 'Culture preparations may be grown in media containing allergens; finished yoghurt contains milk unless plant-based.', 'People with milk allergy, lactose intolerance or those seeking a specifically evidenced probiotic strain.', 'Yoghurt, fermented milk, cultured cream and some plant-based fermented products.', 'Yoghurt cultures; live cultures; starter culture; S. thermophilus; L. bulgaricus', 'Not directly applicable; choose plain fermented foods with clearly named strains if that matters to you.', 'Formulation dependent', 'Source dependent', 'Culture itself is generally gluten-free; carrier and finished food must be checked.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Green/amber — useful fermentation tool; benefits are strain-specific', 'High', 'Do not make probiotic or health claims unless the strain, dose and authorised wording support them.', 'A