  ('retinyl-palmitate', 'UIL-0269', 'Retinyl Palmitate', 'Vitamin A palmitate; retinol palmitate; retinyl palmitate vitamin A', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Vitamin A', 'A fat-soluble ester of retinol used as a stable source of preformed vitamin A in fortified foods and supplements.', 'Manufactured vitamin compound; may be carried in oil or encapsulated with stabilisers.', 'Fortifies foods with vitamin A and improves stability during storage.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Preformed vitamin A.', 'None.', 'Delivered as a fat-soluble vitamin; carrier oil amount is usually tiny.', 'None except carrier ingredients.', 'None.', 'No direct effect.', 'Absorption requires dietary fat; excessive supplemental intake can be harmful.', 'No basis to classify normal fortified-food use as inflammatory.', 'Not one of the 14 regulated allergens; carriers may contain allergenic ingredients.', 'Pregnant people, those taking vitamin A supplements or retinoid medicines, and people with liver disease under clinical care.', 'Fortified spreads, cereals, milks, meal replacements and supplements.', 'Retinyl palmitate; vitamin A palmitate; vitamin A', 'Obtain vitamin A from a balanced diet unless fortification or supplementation is indicated.', 'Source dependent', 'Source dependent', 'Generally gluten-free; check carriers.', 'Often associated with NOVA 3', 'Neutral/amber — essential nutrient form; excess preformed vitamin A matters', 'High', 'Fortification levels and nutrition claims must comply with applicable rules. Preformed retinol is not equivalent to beta-carotene for excess-risk assessment.', 'Retinyl palmitate is a stable form of preformed vitamin A. It can be useful in fortification, but high total vitamin A intake—especially in pregnancy—needs care.', 'retinyl palmitate|vitamin a palmitate|retinol palmitate', 'retinyl palm itate|retinol palmitat', 'Vitamin A; Retinol; Beta-Carotene', 'Antioxidants and encapsulating agents may be used in premixes.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/