  ('calcium-citrate', 'UIL-0270', 'Calcium Citrate', 'Calcium citrate salts; tricalcium dicitrate; calcium citrate supplement', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Calcium', 'A calcium salt of citric acid used to provide calcium and sometimes regulate acidity.', 'Manufactured from calcium compounds and citric acid.', 'Fortifies foods and supplements with calcium; may also influence acidity and stability.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Calcium.', 'None.', 'None.', 'No meaningful sugar contribution.', 'None.', 'No direct effect.', 'Often well tolerated, though larger supplemental doses may cause gastrointestinal symptoms.', 'No evidence of unique inflammatory harm at permitted food-use levels.', 'Not one of the 14 regulated allergens; compound premixes may contain carriers.', 'People with kidney disease, kidney stones, high blood calcium or taking interacting medicines should seek professional advice for supplements.', 'Calcium supplements, fortified drinks, meal replacements and nutrition products.', 'Calcium citrate; calcium salts of citric acid; tricalcium dicitrate', 'Calcium-rich foods or other permitted calcium forms depending on diet and clinical need.', 'Check manufacturer', 'Usually', 'Generally gluten-free.', 'Often associated with NOVA 3', 'Neutral/amber — useful mineral source; dose and need matter', 'High', 'Nutrition claims require qualifying calcium amounts. Supplement doses should not be inferred from generic ingredient presence.', 'Calcium citrate is a legitimate calcium source, but seeing it on a label does not tell you the dose or whether extra calcium is needed.', 'calcium citrate|tricalcium dicitrate|calcium salts of citric acid', 'calcium citrat|calcium citratee', 'Calcium Carbonate; Calcium; Citric Acid', 'Citric acid and anti-caking agents may be present in premixes.', 'https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list; https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/composition-of-foods-integrated-dataset-cofid', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
