  ('spring-water', 'UIL-0272', 'Spring Water', 'Bottled spring water; water from a spring', 'Water and liquid bases', 'Water', 'Water from a protected underground source, tapped at a natural or drilled exit and marketed under specific spring-water rules.', 'A registered underground spring or borehole protected from pollution.', 'Consumed as drinking water or used as a liquid base in foods and beverages.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Hydration; mineral content varies by source and does not have to be stable in the same way as natural mineral water.', 'None.', 'None.', 'None.', 'None.', 'No direct effect when plain.', 'Supports hydration; microbiological safety is regulated.', 'No basis to claim generic anti-inflammatory effects.', 'No regulated food allergen in plain spring water.', 'People requiring controlled mineral or sodium intake should check the individual water analysis if relevant.', 'Bottled water, drinks and food formulations.', 'Spring water; bottled spring water', 'Safe tap water or other compliant drinking water depending on access, preference and local quality.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Green — plain hydration source', 'High', 'In England, spring water must come from a protected underground source and be labelled with the spring name and place of exploitation. It is distinct from natural mineral water and bottled drinking water.', 'Spring water is regulated by where it comes from, not by a promise that it has special health powers. Plain water remains a simple hydration choice.', 'spring water|bottled spring water|water from spring', 'spring watter|sprng water', 'Water; Natural Mineral Water; Bottled Drinking Water', 'None in plain spring water.', 'https://www.gov.uk/guidance/spring-water-how-to-produce-and-label; https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('chilli-flakes', 'UIL-0273', 'Chilli Flakes', 'Crushed chillies; crushed red pepper; red pepper flakes; chilli pepper flakes', 'Herbs, spices and seasonings', 'Chilli Pepper', 'Dried chilli peppers crushed into flakes, sometimes including seeds. Heat varies by chilli type and blend.', 'Dried fruits of Capsicum species.', 'Adds heat, colour and chilli flavour.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Used in small amounts; contributes flavour and small amounts of plant compounds rather than major nutrition.', 'Negligible.', 'Negligible.', 'Negligible at usual servings.', 'Small amount.', 'No meaningful direct effect at culinary doses.', 'Capsaicin can irritate reflux, IBS or sensitive digestion in some people.', 'Capsaicin is biologically active, but culinary chilli should not be marketed as a treatment.', 'Not one of the 14 regulated allergens; spice allergy or cross-contact can occur.', 'People with reflux, oral sensitivity, IBS or known Capsicum allergy.', 'Pizza, pasta, curries, sauces, marinades and seasoning blends.', 'Chilli flakes; crushed chillies; red pepper flakes', 'Paprika, herbs or black pepper for flavour with less heat.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Naturally gluten-free; seasoning blends may not be.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Green — simple spice; personal tolerance matters', 'High', 'Pure chilli flakes and compound chilli seasoning should be separate scanner results.', 'Chilli flakes are simply dried crushed chillies when pure. They add flavour without sugar or salt, but heat tolerance is personal.', 'chilli flakes|chili flakes|crushed chillies|crushed red pepper|red pepper flakes', 'chilli flaks|chili flake', 'Cayenne Pepper; Chilli Powder; Paprika', 'Anti-caking agents may appear in blends, not usually pure flakes.', 'https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-08-05', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('table-salt', 'UIL-0274', 'Table Salt', 'Salt; sodium chloride; common salt; iodised table salt', 'Salt and savoury bases', 'Salt', 'Food-grade sodium chloride, usually finely ground and sometimes fortified with iodine or treated with anti-caking agents.', 'Mined rock salt or evaporated seawater/brine, then refined.', 'Adds saltiness; enhances flavour; supports preservation, dough structure and food processing.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Sodium and chloride; iodised versions also provide iodine.', 'None.', 'None.', 'None.', 'None.', 'No direct glucose effect, but high sodium intake is relevant to blood pressure.', 'Normal amounts are tolerated; excessive sodium can affect fluid balance and health.', 'Do not label salt as directly inflammatory; the established concern is excessive sodium and blood pressure/cardiovascular risk.', 'Salt itself is not an allergen. Anti-caking agents or flavour blends should be assessed separately.', 'People with high blood pressure, cardiovascular or kidney conditions following professional dietary advice.', 'Nearly all savoury processed foods, bread, cheese, sauces, cured foods and home cooking.', 'Salt; table salt; sodium chloride; iodised salt', 'Use less overall; herbs, spices, acids and aromatics can add flavour without matching salt’s sodium load.', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Gluten-free.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Amber — essential mineral ingredient, but excess intake matters', 'High', 'Nutrition labels express salt, while sodium may appear in technical information. Iodised salt should declare iodine fortification appropriately.', 'Table salt, sea salt and rock salt are all mainly sodium chloride. The key difference for health is usually how much you use, not the marketing name.', 'table salt|salt|sodium chloride|iodised salt|iodized salt', 'tabl salt|sodum chloride', 'Sea Salt; Rock Salt; Iodised Salt', 'Anti-caking agents may be present.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/salt-in-your-diet/; https://www.gov.uk/food-