  ('apple-cider-vinegar', 'UIL-0275', 'Apple Cider Vinegar', 'ACV; cider vinegar; apple vinegar', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Vinegar', 'Vinegar produced by fermenting apple juice or cider first to alcohol and then to acetic acid. Filtered, unfiltered and pasteurised forms differ.', 'Apples or apple cider fermented by yeasts and acetic acid bacteria.', 'Adds acidity, sour flavour and preservation; used in dressings, pickles and drinks.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Very little energy or micronutrition at culinary servings; mainly water and acetic acid.', 'Negligible.', 'None.', 'Usually very low residual sugar, but sweetened drinks and dressings differ.', 'None or negligible, even when unfiltered.', 'Some studies suggest modest post-meal effects, but evidence is not strong enough to treat it as diabetes treatment.', 'Acidic; can aggravate reflux, nausea or dental erosion when taken undiluted.', 'No established broad detoxifying or anti-inflammatory effect.', 'Not one of the 14 regulated allergens; sulphites may be present above declaration thresholds in some products.', 'People with reflux, dental erosion, low potassium, gastroparesis or taking medicines affected by vinegar use should seek advice before concentrated use.', 'Dressings, marinades, pickles, sauces, tonics and wellness shots.', 'Apple cider vinegar; cider vinegar; apple vinegar; ACV', 'Other vinegars, lemon juice or yoghurt-based dressings depending on use.', 'Usually', 'Usually', 'Naturally gluten-free when made from apples; cross-contact and compound recipes must be checked.', 'Context dependent', 'Green/amber — useful vinegar, but not a cure or detox', 'Mixed', 'Health claims must not imply treatment of diabetes, weight loss or detoxification.', 'Apple cider vinegar is a useful acidic condiment. It is not a magic detox, and taking it undiluted can damage teeth or irritate digestion.', 'apple cider vinegar|cider vinegar|apple vinegar|acv', 'apple cyder vinegar|apple cider vinigar', 'Sp