  ('tuna', 'UIL-0313', 'Tuna', 'Tuna fish', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'Tuna species', 'Edible tuna flesh sold fresh, frozen, canned or prepared in different ways.', 'Tuna species including skipjack, yellowfin and albacore; species affects composition and mercury exposure.', 'Protein food or ingredient in meals and fillings.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Protein; fat and salt depend on species and preparation.', 'A source of fish protein and essential amino acids.', 'Varies; packing oil can increase fat. NHS guidance does not classify tuna as oily fish.', 'Little in plain fish; sauces and recipe ingredients can add carbohydrate.', 'None in plain tuna.', 'Little direct carbohydrate contribution; assess the full meal.', 'No fibre contribution; fish allergy and product handling affect suitability.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains FISH; applies to fresh and canned tuna.', 'Pregnant people or those trying for a baby should follow NHS tuna limits because of mercury; people with fish allergy must avoid it.', 'Fish dishes, canned fish, sandwiches, salads, pasta and ready meals.', 'Tuna; Tuna fish', 'Other suitable fish or protein foods; vary choices and observe relevant pregnancy advice.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in plain tuna; sauces, coatings and compound recipes can contain it.', 'Context dependent', 'Protein food — species, preparation and mercury context', 'High', 'Fish allergen requirements apply; product identity, preparation and labelling should be checked.', 'Tuna can provide useful protein. Check the species, packing medium and salt, and follow pregnancy advice on mercury exposure.', 'tuna|tuna fish', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Skipjack Tuna; Yellowfin Tuna; Canned Tuna; Fish', 'None inherent; assess the complete product.', 'https://www.nhs.uk