  ('mayonnaise', 'UIL-0318', 'Mayonnaise', 'Mayo; traditional mayonnaise', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Oil-based emulsion / condiment', 'An emulsified condiment usually based on oil, egg and an acid. Reduced-fat and egg-free products have different recipes.', 'Recipe-dependent oils, eggs, vinegar/lemon juice and other ingredients.', 'Creamy condiment; adds moisture, flavour and fat.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually mainly fat and energy; lighter versions differ.', 'Usually a small contribution despite containing egg.', 'Principal contribution in traditional versions; fatty-acid profile depends on oil.', 'Usually limited in traditional versions; starch/sugar can vary.', 'Usually negligible.', 'Depends on carbohydrates and serving size in the actual recipe; not a glucose-lowering food.', 'No special gut benefit established; acid, fat and individual tolerance matter.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Traditional recipes contain EGG; MUSTARD and other allergens such as MILK can occur.', 'People with egg/mustard or other recipe allergies; those comparing fat, salt and portions.', 'Sandwiches, dressings, dips, salads and sauces.', 'Mayonnaise; Mayo; traditional mayonnaise', 'A suitable lower-fat or egg-free option if needed; compare actual recipes and allergens.', 'Not vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'No gluten necessarily inherent, but malt vinegar, thickeners and other recipe ingredients require checking.', 'Context dependent', 'Compound condiment — assess recipe, portion and allergens', 'Moderate', 'Component ingredients and regulated allergens must be assessed. Egg-free mayonnaise-style products require a separate formulation profile.', 'Mayonnaise is mainly an oil-based sauce, not an egg-protein food. Check the oil, portion, salt and allergens rather than the name alone.', 'mayonnaise|mayo|traditional mayonnaise', 'None specifically validated; spelling correc