  ('sourdough-culture', 'UIL-0346', 'Sourdough Culture', 'Sourdough starter culture; sourdough starter; sourdough leaven', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Microbial fermentation culture / cereal starter', 'A culture of yeasts and bacteria used for sourdough fermentation, often carried in a flour-and-water starter.', 'Selected or maintained microbial communities; cereal base/carriers vary.', 'Ferments dough, develops acidity/flavour and can help dough rise.', 'Processed ingredient', 'The culture organisms contribute little at use levels; flour/water starter nutrition depends on its base and amount.', 'Depends mainly on flour/carrier rather than microbes.', 'Depends on the carrier/base; usually limited in a simple starter.', 'Cereal starter contains starch and sugars; microbes consume some during fermentation.', 'Depends on the flour/base; not a generic fibre supplement.', 'No fixed glucose benefit from the word sourdough culture alone.', 'Not automatically probiotic; baking changes organism viability. Fermentation does not guarantee gluten-free or symptom-free bread.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Starter often contains WHEAT, RYE or another regulated cereal; carrier and recipe allergens need assessment.', 'People with coeliac disease, cereal allergy or sensitivity to specific recipe ingredients.', 'Sourdough bread and other fermented bakery products.', 'Sourdough Culture; Sourdough starter culture; sourdough starter; sourdough leaven', 'A starter compatible with the intended cereal and dietary needs; no universal need to replace it.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Usually depends on the cereal base. Ordinary wheat/rye sourdough is not made gluten-free by fermentation.', 'Context dependent', 'Fermentation ingredient — cereal, strains and final food matter', 'Moderate', 'Ingredient/allergen rules depend on the actual preparation and use; health c