  ('vanilla-oleoresin', 'UIL-0369', 'Vanilla Oleoresin', 'Vanilla bean oleoresin; vanilla oleoresin extract', 'Flavouring food ingredients', 'Vanilla beans', 'A concentrated, viscous vanilla-bean extract used as a flavouring preparation; strength and carrier system vary.', 'Cured vanilla beans extracted with a suitable food-use solvent; commercial preparations may have carriers.', 'Adds concentrated vanilla aroma and flavour at low inclusion levels.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Usually negligible nutrient contribution at flavouring amounts; carriers can change composition.', 'Usually negligible at flavouring amounts.', 'Carrier oils may add fat; the term oleoresin does not define a fixed fat content.', 'Sugars or other carriers may be present; assess the formulation and amount used.', 'No meaningful fibre contribution expected at flavouring amounts.', 'Usually little direct contribution at flavouring doses; sweetened carriers and the finished food matter.', 'No established special digestive benefit from generic vanilla oleoresin.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Vanilla itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; carriers and blends need separate assessment.', 'People checking carrier allergens or requiring a specifically verified food-grade preparation.', 'Bakery products, desserts, confectionery, dairy/plant desserts and flavouring blends.', 'Vanilla Oleoresin; Vanilla bean oleoresin; vanilla oleoresin extract', 'Vanilla beans or a suitable vanilla extract where the recipe permits; flavour strengths and carriers differ.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Vanilla flavouring — food grade, strength and carriers matter', 'Moderate', 'Food flavouring and extraction-solvent rules apply. A ''natural vanilla'' description requires the relevant criteria; fragrance grades are not automatically food ingredients.', 'Vanilla oleoresin provides concentrated vanilla flavour. Check its food-grade specification and any carriers; it is not nutritionally equivalent to whole beans or simply another name for vanillin.', 'vanilla oleoresin|vanilla bean oleoresin|vanilla oleoresin extract', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Vanilla Extract (UIL-0196); Vanilla Bean (UIL-0239); Vanilla Paste (UIL-0265); Vanillin', 'Flavouring preparation, not an assumed E-number additive; carriers or additional flavouring substances may be present.', 'https://www.biolandes.com/wp-content/uploads/fiche-technique-F9980.pdf | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/flavourings-authorisation-guidance/flavourings-authorisation-guidance | https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('mustard', 'UIL-0370', 'Mustard', 'Prepared mustard; mustard condiment; mustard paste', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Mustard seeds / prepared condiment', 'A prepared condiment based on mustard seed or flour, usually mixed with water/vinegar and other recipe ingredients.', 'Mustard seeds/flour plus a product-specific recipe, which may include salt, sugar, vinegar or wheat flour.', 'Adds pungent flavour and helps texture/emulsification in condiments and sauces.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually a small contribution at condiment portions; salt, sugar, fat and carbohydrate vary.', 'Contains some seed protein; usual condiment amounts contribute little.', 'Seed oil and any added oil vary with recipe.', 'May contain added sugar or starch; use the actual ingredient list and nutrition label.', 'Varies with seed content and preparation; usual portions contribute limited fibre.', 'Usually a small carbohydrate contribution at condiment portions; sweetened recipes and amount used matter.', 'Pungency or acidity can trigger symptoms in some people with reflux; not a generic digestive treatment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MUSTARD. Some prepared mustards also contain WHEAT or other allergens; check the complete recipe.', 'People with mustard allergy; those checking additional allergens, salt/sugar content or personal reflux triggers.', 'Table condiments, sandwiches, dressings, marinades, mayonnaise and prepared sauces.', 'Mustard; Prepared mustard; mustard condiment; mustard paste', 'A suitable mustard-free flavouring for mustard allergy, or a recipe with less salt/sugar where desired; allergen suitability is recipe-specific.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'Mustard seed has no inherent gluten, but prepared mustard can contain wheat flour or other gluten-containing ingredients.', 'Context dependent', 'Mustard condiment — mustard allergen and recipe matter', 'Moderate', 'MUSTARD must be declared and emphasised where required; additional allergens such as WHEAT need their own declaration.', 'Prepared mustard adds strong flavour, but recipes differ in salt, sugar and other ingredients. Mustard is a regulated allergen, and some products also contain wheat.', 'mustard|prepared mustard|mustard condiment|mustard paste', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Mustard Powder (UIL-0377); Mustard Seed; Dijon Mustard; Wholegrain Mustard; English Mustard', 'Prepared products may use acids, thickeners or preservatives; none should be assumed for every mustard.', 'https://www.colmans.co.uk/p/english-squeezable-mustard.html/00000096107775 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.uhsussex.nhs.uk/resources/advice-on-management-of-gastro-oesophageal-reflux/ | https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('wheat-rusk', 'UIL-0371', 'Wheat Rusk', 'Wheat-based rusk; wheat rusks; wheat rusk crumb', 'Bakery and cereal bases', 'Wheat flour / rusk', 'A dried, baked wheat-flour product, usually gristed into crumbs for binding and texture.', 'Wheat flour, commonly with salt and a raising agent; the complete recipe varies.', 'Absorbs water, binds ingredients and controls texture in meat and other prepared foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Primarily starch/carbohydrate, with some wheat protein; salt and fibre depend on recipe/flour.', 'Some wheat protein, but usually used for binding rather than protein enrichment.', 'Often limited in a basic rusk; richer recipes can contain added fat.', 'Mainly digestible wheat starch; quantity in the food matters.', 'Variable and generally lower with refined flour; not equivalent to wheat bran.', 'Digestible starch contributes carbohydrate; no fixed GI assigned to rusk or the finished food.', 'No established special gut benefit; wheat allergy, coeliac disease and individual tolerance matter.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains WHEAT; recipe additions may introduce EGG, MILK or other allergens.', 'People with wheat allergy or coeliac disease; those checking carbohydrate and salt content.', 'Sausages, burgers, stuffing, coatings, meat-free binding mixes and bakery ingredients.', 'Wheat Rusk; Wheat-based rusk; wheat rusks; wheat rusk crumb', 'Verified gluten-free rusk/breadcrumbs if needed, or another binder chosen for the recipe; nutrient/allergen profiles differ.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'Wheat rusk normally contains gluten and is unsuitable for coeliac disease unless a specifically compliant preparation is established.', 'Context dependent', 'Wheat cereal binder — starch, wheat allergen and recipe matter', 'Moderate', 'WHEAT must be declared and emphasised; composite recipe allergens need assessment. Its presence does 