  ('starter-culture', 'UIL-0372', 'Starter Culture', 'Starter cultures; food starter culture; fermentation starter culture', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Food fermentation microorganisms', 'A selected microorganism or mixture used to initiate controlled food fermentation; organisms and carriers depend on the application.', 'Cultivated food-fermentation bacteria, yeasts and/or moulds, supplied in a preparation with possible carriers.', 'Fermentation, acidification, flavour development and food-specific texture or preservation functions.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Usually little direct nutrient contribution at inoculation amounts; carriers and fermentation change the final food.', 'Usually negligible direct contribution; milk/protein carriers can be present.', 'Usually negligible directly; the culture preparation and final food need assessment.', 'Carriers may contain sugars or starch; fermentation changes substrates in a process-dependent way.', 'No automatic dietary-fibre or prebiotic contribution.', 'A starter-culture name does not establish a low-sugar product or a blood-sugar benefit.', 'Not automatically probiotic. Health effects require appropriate evidence for defined organisms, amounts and the finished food.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Culture preparations may contain MILK, SOYA or cereal-based carriers; microbial identity alone does not determine allergen status.', 'People checking allergens, vegan suitability or claims about live organisms; product/strain details are needed.', 'Yoghurt, cheese, fermented milk, plant ferments, sourdough and other controlled fermentation processes.', 'Starter Culture; Starter cultures; food starter culture; fermentation starter culture', 'An application-appropriate food culture with verified strain, carrier and dietary specifications.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Organisms do not inherently provide gluten; cereal-based starters and carriers may contain it and need verification.', 'Context dependent', 'Fermentation ingredient — organism, carrier and finished food matter', 'Moderate', 'Use food-appropriate strains and assess declared carriers/allergens. A starter designation does not establish an authorised probiotic or health claim.', 'Starter cultures drive fermentation, but the generic name does not identify their organisms, carriers or health effects. Check the exact preparation and whether organisms remain alive in the finished food.', 'starter culture|starter cultures|food starter culture|fermentation starter culture', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Yoghurt Culture (UIL-0268); Kefir Culture (UIL-0294); Cheese Culture (UIL-0320); Sourdough Culture (UIL-0346); Probiotic Culture', 'Carriers or stabilising ingredients may be present; a culture should not be conflated with rennet or a single food-additive identity.', 'https://www.iff.com/food-beverage/food-bioscience/cultures/ | https://doi.org/10.1038/s41575-020-00390-5 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('vitamin-d3', 'UIL-0373', 'Vitamin D3', 'Cholecalciferol; colecalciferol; vitamin D 3', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Vitamin D', 'The D3 form of vitamin D, a fat-soluble micronutrient used in fortification and supplements.', 'Manufactured cholecalciferol, commonly lanolin-derived; verified animal-free routes include lichen and pine-derived material. Premix carriers vary.', 'Adds vitamin D activity to foods or supplements.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Vitamin D activity; the amount delivered depends on potency, inclusion and serving.', 'No protein contribution from the D3 molecule.', 'Fat-soluble vitamin, not a meaningful source of dietary fat at nutrient doses; carrier oil may contribute.', 'No carbohydrate from D3 itself; premix carriers may contain sugar/starch.', 'None from D3 itself.', 'No direct carbohydrate contribution; no generic glucose-lowering claim assigned.', 'Supports normal calcium handling, but is not a generic digestive or gut-healing ingredient.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'D3 itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; carriers, coatings and animal-derived preparations need checking.', 'People combining fortified foods and supplements, or requiring verified vegan sourcing; medical dosing needs individual guidance.', 'Fortified drinks, spreads, cereals, nutrition products and supplements.', 'Vitamin D3; Cholecalciferol; colecalciferol; vitamin D 3', 'A verified animal-free D3 preparation or suitable D2 for the intended application; dose and formulation require their own assessment.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'D3 itself has no gluten; premix carriers and the finished product require separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Vitamin fortificant — dose and sourcing matter', 'High', 'Cholecalciferol is listed as a permitted vitamin form for food fortification in GB; product restrictions and claim conditions still apply.', 'Vitamin D3 supplies vitamin D, which supports normal calcium/phosphate regulation. Its vegan suitability depends on its source and carriers, while the total dose matters when combining products.', 'vitamin d3|vitamin d 3|cholecalciferol|colecalciferol', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Vitamin D2 (UIL-0347); Cholecalciferol (UIL-0399); Calcium Ingredients', 'Nutrient fortificant rather than an assumed E-number additive; carriers or premix additives need separate review.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-d/ | https://theghtcompanies.com/vitashine/ | https://www.innobioglobal.com/Vitamin-D3.html | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('calcium-gluconate', 'UIL-0374', 'Calcium Gluconate', 'Calcium D-gluconate; E578; E 578', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Calcium / gluconic acid', 'A calcium salt of gluconic acid, used as a calcium source and in some food-additive applications.', 'Manufactured calcium gluconate; feedstock and processing aids are supplier-specific.', 'Calcium fortification/supplementation; permitted technological functions depend on the food application.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Calcium; the elemental calcium dose is not equal to the total weight of the gluconate salt.', 'None from plain calcium gluconate.', 'None from the mineral salt itself.', 'Not a sugar ingredient; the gluconate salt must not be treated as equivalent to free glucose. Carriers may differ.', 'None from the mineral salt.', 'No established generic blood-sugar-lowering effect; the complete product determines carbohydrate exposure.', 'No fibre or prebiotic role. High supplemental calcium intake can cause digestive symptoms.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Calcium gluconate itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens and is not inherently milk; carriers may contain allergens.', 'People combining calcium supplements/fortified foods or with clinician-managed calcium/kidney conditions; use product-specific guidance.', 'Fortified foods and drinks, supplements and permitted food-additive applications.', 'Calcium Gluconate; Calcium D-gluconate; E578; E 578', 'Calcium-containing foods or another permitted calcium source selected for the formulation and individual need; compare elemental calcium.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'Plain calcium gluconate has no inherent gluten; carriers and blends require separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Calcium ingredient — elemental dose and function matter', 'High', 'Listed as a permitted calcium source for fortification in GB. E578 food-additive use is a separate matter subject to applicable categories/conditions.', 'Calcium gluconate can supply calcium and has a food-additive identity, E578. The calcium dose, purpose and finished formulation matter; it should not be confused with milk or glucose.', 'calcium gluconate|calcium d-gluconate|e578|e 578', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Calcium Carbonate (UIL-0244); Calcium Citrate (UIL-0270); Calcium Lactate (UIL-0348); Gluconic Acid', 'Calcium gluconate E578; nutrient-source and technological-additive uses should be distinguished.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/calcium/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods | https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/id/food-additives/authorisation/e-578 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('l-valine', 'UIL-0375', 'L-Valine', 'L valine; valine (L-form)', 'Amino acids and functional nutrition', 'Valine / essential amino acids', 'The L-form of valine, one of the essential branched-chain amino acids, supplied as an isolated ingredient.', 'Manufactured amino acid; the production route, feedstock and processing aids need supplier confirmation.', 'Adds valine to amino-acid blends, sports nutrition or specialist nutrition formulations.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'One essential amino acid; not a complete protein or a balanced source of all essential amino acids.', 'Valine is a building block of protein, but isolated L-valine does not supply all the amino acids in complete dietary protein.', 'None in the pure amino acid.', 'Not a sugar or starch; carriers and flavoured blends may add carbohydrate.', 'None in the pure amino acid.', 'No generic blood-sugar benefit assigned; metabolic effects cannot be inferred from the ingredient name.', 'No established special digestive benefit for a generic L-valine ingredient.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'L-valine itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; production-derived residues and blend ingredients need assessment.', 'People considering concentrated amino-acid supplements or using medically supervised specialist nutrition; origin and dose require checking.', 'BCAA/amino-acid blends, sports nutrition and specialist nutrition products.', 'L-Valine; L valine; valine (L-form)', 'Varied protein foods supplying all essential amino acids; specialist nutrition should follow individual guidance.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Pure L-valine has no gluten; source residues, carriers and the finished blend require separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Isolated essential amino acid — dose, origin and purpose matter', 'Moderate', 'Nutrition/supplement and health-claim rules depend on product and