  ('rice-vinegar', 'UIL-0379', 'Rice Vinegar', 'Rice wine vinegar; vinegar from rice', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Rice fermentation', 'Vinegar produced from a rice-derived fermentation base; plain and seasoned preparations have different recipes.', 'Fermented rice-derived liquid, water and optional recipe ingredients.', 'Acidity and flavour in dressings, marinades, pickling and rice seasoning.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually a small nutrient contribution at condiment amounts; seasoned products may add sugar and salt.', 'Usually negligible at condiment portions.', 'Usually negligible in plain rice vinegar.', 'Plain products can contain little carbohydrate; seasoned rice vinegar may contain added sugar.', 'No meaningful fibre contribution from plain vinegar.', 'Assess added sugars and portion; no generic diabetes-treatment or guaranteed glucose-lowering claim.', 'Acidity may trigger reflux symptoms in some people; vinegar is not automatically probiotic.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Rice itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens, but mixed-grain vinegars, blends and other recipe ingredients require checks.', 'People checking added sugar/salt, cereal allergens or personal reflux triggers.', 'Dressings, pickles, sushi-rice seasonings, marinades, sauces and prepared dishes.', 'Rice Vinegar; Rice wine vinegar; vinegar from rice', 'A suitable unsweetened vinegar or other tolerated acidic ingredient for the recipe; compare flavour, acidity and allergens.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'Rice-only vinegar has no inherent gluten source; mixed grains, blends and cross-contact need verification. Do not assume every product is rice-only.', 'Context dependent', 'Fermented acidic condiment — recipe and tolerance matter', 'Moderate', 'Use an accurate vinegar/seasoning description and declare compound ingredients/allergens as required; verify any glute