  ('sweet-potato-puree', 'UIL-0381', 'Sweet Potato Puree', 'Sweet potato purée; sweet-potato puree; pureed sweet potato', 'Vegetable ingredients', 'Sweet potato', 'A smooth preparation made by breaking down sweet potato flesh, often followed by heat treatment; added ingredients depend on the product.', 'Sweet potato roots (Ipomoea batatas); variety, peeling, water content and heat treatment vary.', 'Vegetable flavour, colour, body, moisture and a carbohydrate-containing base.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Starch/carbohydrate, some fibre and micronutrients; composition varies with cultivar and dilution.', 'A small contribution compared with protein foods.', 'Little inherent fat; oil, cream or butter additions change the recipe.', 'Contains starch and naturally occurring sugars; not a carbohydrate-free vegetable preparation.', 'Can retain root fibre; peeling, sieving and dilution change the amount.', 'Contributes carbohydrate; serving, cooking, dilution and the complete food affect the response. No fixed GI assigned.', 'Fibre and portion may affect tolerance; no generic gut-healing or prebiotic claim.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Sweet potato is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; compound puree ingredients and cross-contact require checks.', 'People monitoring carbohydrate or checking added milk, fats, salt or other recipe ingredients.', 'Soups, sauces, baby-food formulations, bakery products, prepared meals and vegetable blends.', 'Sweet Potato Puree; Sweet potato purée; sweet-potato puree; pureed sweet potato', 'Whole cooked sweet potato when the recipe permits; no general need to replace a plain puree.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Vegetable preparation with starch and fibre', 'Moderate', 'Assess the actual ingredient list and preparati