  ('groundnut-oil', 'UIL-0387', 'Groundnut Oil', 'Peanut oil; arachis oil; ground nut oil', 'Oils and fats', 'Peanuts', 'Edible oil extracted from peanuts, also called groundnuts; refined and unrefined forms have different properties.', 'Peanut seeds (Arachis hypogaea); extraction and refining method vary.', 'Cooking, frying, flavour and fat in food formulations.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Energy and fat, mainly unsaturated; fatty-acid profile varies with cultivar and processing.', 'No meaningful protein nutrition in oil, but residual allergenic protein can matter.', 'Main contribution; predominantly unsaturated with some saturated fat. High-oleic varieties have a different profile.', 'No carbohydrate or sugar in plain oil.', 'None in plain oil.', 'No carbohydrate contribution from plain oil; the whole meal determines the response.', 'No fibre or established special digestive benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'PEANUT-derived. Refining removes most allergenic protein; unrefined oils retain more. The generic name does not establish suitability for peanut allergy.', 'People with peanut allergy need clear refining/source information and their allergy team''s advice.', 'Cooking/frying oils, dressings, sauces, snacks and prepared foods.', 'Groundnut Oil; Peanut oil; arachis oil; ground nut oil', 'Another suitable culinary oil when avoiding peanuts, with appropriate ingredient and cross-contact checks.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Culinary oil requiring peanut-source and refining context', 'Moderate', 'Peanut-origin oil remains subject to relevant PEANUT allergen labelling; do not apply the refined-soya-oil exemption to peanut oil.', 'Groundnut oil is peanut oil. It supplies mainly fat, and its refining status is particularly relevant for peanut-al