  ('egg-albumen', 'UIL-0389', 'Egg Albumen', 'Egg white; hen egg albumen; egg albumen liquid; dried egg albumen', 'Egg ingredients', 'Egg white', 'The white of an egg, predominantly water and proteins; it may be supplied liquid, frozen or dried.', 'Hen eggs in typical food use; separation, pasteurisation and drying depend on preparation.', 'Foaming, binding, structure and protein in foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Egg-white protein and water in liquid form; drying concentrates the protein and other solids.', 'Supplies essential amino acids; amount depends on liquid/dried form and processing.', 'Little inherent fat compared with whole egg or yolk.', 'Usually a small contribution in plain albumen; sugar/starch-containing blends differ.', 'No inherent dietary fibre.', 'Plain albumen usually contributes little carbohydrate; recipe ingredients determine the complete food''s response.', 'No established special digestive benefit; egg allergy can involve digestive symptoms.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains EGG. Drying or pasteurisation does not remove its egg-allergy relevance.', 'People with egg allergy; those checking a verified pasteurised product and appropriate storage/handling.', 'Bakery products, meringues, icing, binding/foaming mixes, egg products and protein formulations.', 'Egg Albumen; Egg white; hen egg albumen; egg albumen liquid; dried egg albumen', 'A suitable plant protein or recipe-specific egg-free foaming/binding preparation when avoiding egg.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Egg-white ingredient with egg-allergen relevance', 'High', 'EGG must be declared and emphasised where required; safe handling and any added ingredients require preparation-specific assessment.', 'Egg albumen means egg white. Its protein and low