  ('cod', 'UIL-0391', 'Cod', 'Cod fish; Atlantic cod; Pacific cod', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'White fish', 'An edible white fish commonly referring to Atlantic or Pacific cod; species and preparation should be identified.', 'Cod species such as Gadus morhua or Gadus macrocephalus; fishery and cut vary.', 'Protein, mild fish flavour and texture.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Protein and micronutrients; plain cod flesh is relatively lean.', 'Provides complete animal protein.', 'Low in fat when plain; batter, frying oil or sauces change the profile. Cod flesh is distinct from cod liver oil.', 'No inherent carbohydrate in plain fish; coatings and sauces can add it.', 'None in plain fish.', 'Plain cod contributes no carbohydrate; assess the meal, coating and sauce.', 'No established special digestive benefit; appropriate fish storage and preparation remain important.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains FISH; plain cod and cod-derived food ingredients retain fish-allergy relevance.', 'People with fish allergy, or checking coatings, salt and preparation.', 'Fresh/frozen fish, fish fingers, fish-and-chips, fish pies, salted fish and prepared meals.', 'Cod; Cod fish; Atlantic cod; Pacific cod', 'Other suitable fish or protein foods; oily fish can supply more long-chain omega-3, subject to dietary guidance.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Lean fish protein with fish-allergen relevance', 'High', 'FISH must be declared where required; species descriptions, safe handling and compound ingredients need assessment.', 'Plain cod is a lean protein food. Its fish allergen remains relevant, while batter, oil, salt and sauces can substantially change a cod product''s composition.', 'cod|cod fish|atlantic cod|pacific cod', 'None specifically val