  ('dijon-mustard', 'UIL-0396', 'Dijon Mustard', 'Dijon-style mustard; French Dijon mustard', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Prepared mustard', 'A smooth Dijon-style mustard condiment, typically based on mustard seeds with an acidic liquid, salt and other recipe ingredients.', 'Mustard seeds, commonly brown/oriental mustard, with water, vinegar and/or wine and product-specific ingredients.', 'Pungent flavour and emulsification/texture in condiments, dressings, marinades and sauces.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually a small contribution at condiment amounts; salt, sugar, seed fat and carbohydrate vary.', 'Some mustard-seed protein; ordinary condiment portions contribute little.', 'Seed fat and any added oil vary by recipe.', 'Added sugar or other carbohydrate varies; honey/flavoured versions differ from plain Dijon.', 'Limited at usual condiment portions; seed proportion and processing affect content.', 'Usually a small contribution at condiment amounts; assess added sugar and portion.', 'Pungency/acidity can aggravate reflux symptoms in some people; no generic digestive-treatment claim.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MUSTARD. Some recipes contain SULPHITES from wine or preservatives; other added allergens must be checked.', 'People with mustard allergy or sulphite sensitivity, and those checking salt, sugar or personal reflux triggers.', 'Table mustard, dressings, mayonnaise, marinades, sauces and prepared meals.', 'Dijon Mustard; Dijon-style mustard; French Dijon mustard', 'A suitable mustard-free flavouring if avoiding mustard, or a recipe meeting the intended salt/sugar needs.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'Mustard seeds have no inherent gluten; check the complete Dijon recipe, vinegar source, blends and cross-contact.', 'Context dependent', 'Mustard condiment with mustard and recipe-dependent sulphite relevance', 'Moderate', 'MUSTARD