  ('cholecalciferol', 'UIL-0399', 'Cholecalciferol', 'Vitamin D3; colecalciferol; vitamin D 3', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Vitamin D', 'The D3 form of vitamin D, a fat-soluble micronutrient used in fortification and supplements.', 'Manufactured cholecalciferol, commonly lanolin-derived; verified animal-free routes include lichen and pine-derived material. Premix carriers vary.', 'Adds vitamin D activity to foods or supplements.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Vitamin D activity; the amount delivered depends on potency, inclusion and serving.', 'No protein contribution from the D3 molecule.', 'Fat-soluble vitamin, not a meaningful source of dietary fat at nutrient doses; carrier oil may contribute.', 'No carbohydrate from D3 itself; premix carriers may contain sugar/starch.', 'None from D3 itself.', 'No direct carbohydrate contribution; no generic glucose-lowering claim assigned.', 'Supports normal calcium handling, but is not a generic digestive or gut-healing ingredient.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'D3 itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; carriers, coatings and animal-derived preparations need checking.', 'People combining fortified foods and supplements, or requiring verified vegan sourcing; medical dosing needs individual guidance.', 'Fortified drinks, spreads, cereals, nutrition products and supplements.', 'Cholecalciferol; Vitamin D3; colecalciferol; vitamin D 3', 'A verified animal-free D3 preparation or suitable D2 for the intended application; dose and formulation require their own assessment.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'D3 itself has no gluten; premix carriers and the finished product require separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Vitamin fortificant — dose and sourcing matter', 'High', 'Cholecalciferol is listed as a permitted vitamin form for food fortification in GB; product restrictions and claim conditions still ap