  ('mustard-seed', 'UIL-0403', 'Mustard Seed', 'Mustard seeds; yellow mustard seed; white mustard seed; brown mustard seed; black mustard seed', 'Herbs, spices and seasonings', 'Mustard', 'Seeds of mustard plants used whole or ground as a pungent seasoning.', 'Yellow/white, brown or black mustard plants; seed type and preparation vary.', 'Flavour in pickles, curries, sauces, seasoning blends and prepared mustard.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'At usual seasoning portions, mainly flavour; the seeds also contain fat, protein and fibre.', 'Some seed protein, generally a small contribution at seasoning amounts.', 'Contains seed fat; this is not the same ingredient as extracted mustard oil.', 'Some carbohydrate; plain seed is not added sugar.', 'Contains seed fibre; contribution depends on portion and preparation.', 'No established generic glucose-treatment effect assigned at culinary exposure.', 'No gut-treatment claim assigned; tolerance to pungent foods varies.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MUSTARD, a regulated allergen. Whole seeds, ground seeds and prepared mustard require the same allergen awareness.', 'People with mustard allergy; evaluate seasoning blends for additional allergens.', 'Pickles, chutneys, curries, mustard condiments and spice blends.', 'Mustard Seed; Mustard seeds; yellow mustard seed; white mustard seed; brown mustard seed; black mustard seed', 'No reason to replace for most people; a mustard-free seasoning is needed for mustard allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Culinary seed with mandatory mustard-allergen awareness', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise mustard when used as an allergenic ingredient; a generic ''spices'' term must not hide it.', 'Mustard seed adds pungent flavour. Its main ingredient-specific concern