  ('modified-pea-starch', 'UIL-0409', 'Modified Pea Starch', 'Modified pea-derived starch', 'Starches and carbohydrate ingredients', 'Pea starch', 'Pea starch altered to change its texture or performance. The name alone does not identify the modification chemistry or additive number.', 'Starch separated from peas and modified by a specified process; supplier documentation is needed to identify the grade.', 'Thickening, gelling, texture, stability and processing performance in formulated foods.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Mainly starch carbohydrate; do not copy the protein or fibre profile of whole peas.', 'Not a pea-protein ingredient; residual protein may remain.', 'Usually little inherent fat in the starch; check the preparation.', 'Mainly starch; digestibility depends on the modification and cooking. It is not automatically resistant starch.', 'Do not assign fibre content without grade-specific analysis; ''modified'' does not establish dietary fibre.', 'Carbohydrate contribution and response depend on grade, amount and preparation; no fixed glycaemic index assigned.', 'No generic prebiotic or gut-treatment effect established by the word ''modified''.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pea is outside the 14 regulated allergens, but pea allergy can occur; residual protein and blends require assessment.', 'People with pea allergy or needing verified starch, fibre or additive information.', 'Noodles, soups, sauces, bakery, meat or seafood formulations and other texture-controlled foods.', 'Modified Pea Starch; Modified pea-derived starch', 'Native starch or another thickener only if it meets the recipe''s technical needs; no general reason to replace an authorised suitable grade.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Functional starch requiring exact modification and grade context', 'Moderate', 'Confirm additive status and applicable category/use conditions for the precise modification. E1420 is one documented modified-pea-starch form, not all forms.', 'Modified pea starch changes food texture and stability. Its name does not show an E-number, resistance to digestion, genetic-modification status or a gut-health benefit.', 'modified pea starch|modified pea-derived starch', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pea Starch (UIL-0383); Resistant Starch; Modified Starch', 'Acetylated starch (E1420) is a documented pea-starch example. Do not infer E1420, or pea origin from E1420 alone, without the exact specification.', 'https://www.roquette.com/food-nutrition/product-catalog/clearam-lg-00-20 | https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/food_authorisations/e-1420 | https://allergynorthwest.nhs.uk/home-patient/managing-allergies/patient-leaflets/legume-allergy-2/', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('fondant-sugar', 'UIL-0410', 'Fondant Sugar', 'Dry fondant sugar; powdered fondant; fondant icing sugar', 'Sugars, syrups and sweetening ingredients', 'Sugar', 'A sugar-based confectionery ingredient for fondant fillings or icing. It can be a fine dry sugar/glucose blend or a prepared fondant paste; recipes differ.', 'Refined sucrose, commonly combined with glucose syrup or dried glucose; prepared icing can contain further ingredients.', 'Sweetness and a fine, smooth crystalline texture in icing, confectionery and fillings.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Primarily free sugars and energy; not a significant protein or fibre ingredient.', 'Negligible in a simple sugar-based preparation; other ingredients can change this.', 'Little in a simple sugar/glucose fondant; ready-to-roll recipes can contain fat.', 'Mainly sucrose and/or glucose-based sugars, which count as free sugars when added to foods.', 'No meaningful fibre in a simple sugar preparation.', 'Sugar amount, portion and the complete food affect glucose response; no low-GI advantage assumed over other sugars.', 'Not a meaningful fibre ingredient; added polyols or other ingredients need their own assessment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Sugar itself is not a regulated allergen; fondant recipes and finished confections can include allergenic ingredients.', 'People monitoring sugar/carbohydrate intake or requiring exact dietary and allergen information for an icing recipe.', 'Confectionery centres, glazes, cake icing, bakery fillings and fondant preparations.', 'Fondant Sugar; Dry fondant sugar; powdered fondant; fondant icing sugar', 'Use less icing or a less-sweet recipe if reducing free sugars; replacing it with another sugar does not remove free sugars.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Confectionery sugar ingredient requiring portion and recipe context', 'Moderate', 'Declare the actual preparation and its components. A fondant name alone does not establish vegan, allergen-free or reduced-sugar suitability.', 'Fondant sugar mainly supplies sweetness and smooth icing texture. The precise recipe matters, but its sugars still contribute to free-sugar intake.', 'fondant sugar|dry fondant sugar|powdered fondant|fondant icing sugar', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Icing Sugar (UIL-0384); Glucose Syrup (UIL-0002); Sucrose', 'Prepared fondant recipes may include emulsifiers, humectants, stabilisers, colours or preservatives; identify the actual label, not a generic list.', 'https://www.nordzucker.com/en/sugar-expertise-products/sugar-for-the-food-industry/fondant | https://fleminghowden.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/FH-Insert_Fondants-Icings_WEB.pdf | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('lentil-protein', 'UIL-0411', 'Lentil Protein', 'Lentil protein concentrate; lentil protein isolate (specified preparations)', 'Legumes and pulse derivatives', 'Lentils', 'A protein-enriched fraction of lentil seeds, sold as concentrates or isolates rather than whole lentil flour.', 'Lentils (Lens culinaris), fractionated to separate a protein-rich ingredient; dry and wet processing routes can produce different compositions.', 'Protein enrichment, binding, emulsification and structure in plant-based formulations.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Primarily protein; starch, fibre, fat and micronutrient contents differ between preparations.', 'A plant-protein ingredient; amino-acid composition, digestibility and usable protein quality require grade- and recipe-specific data.', 'Variable residual fat; no single value applies to all concentrates or isolates.', 'Residual starch and other carbohydrate vary; not equivalent to whole lentils or lentil flour.', 'Concentrates may retain some fibre; isolates need separate assessment. A high-fibre claim cannot be assumed.', 'No glucose-treatment effect inferred from the name; evaluate carbohydrate and the overall food.', 'Tolerance depends on the preparation and serving; whole-lentil digestive effects cannot automatically be transferred to a protein fraction.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Lentil allergy can occur despite lentil not being one of the 14 regulated allergens. Allergy to one legume does not prove allergy to every legume.', 'People with lentil/legume allergy or seeking verified protein, fibre and amino-acid information.', 'Plant-based meat or dairy alternatives, protein beverages, bakery products, pasta and nutritional blends.', 'Lentil Protein; Lentil protein concentrate; lentil protein isolate (specified preparations)', 'Whole lentils for a whole-food protein/fibre combination, or another suitable protein for a specific allergy or formulation requirement.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Plant protein requiring grade, composition and allergy context', 'Moderate', 'Declare the lentil-derived preparation accurately; protein and other nutrition claims require the finished food to meet their conditions.', 'Lentil protein supplies plant protein, but it is not nutritionally identical to lentil flour or whole lentils. Concentration, processing and the complete recipe determine its role.', 'lentil protein|lentil protein concentrate|lentil protein isolate|red lentil protein|green lentil protein', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Lentil Flour (UIL-0333); Red Lentil Flour (UIL-0359); Green Lentil Flour (UIL-0385); Red Lentils (UIL-0133); Green Lentils (UIL-0134)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.agtfoods.com/ingredients/pulseplus-ingredients/protein | https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6769807/ | https://allergynorthwest.nhs.uk/home-patient/managing-allergies/patient-leaflets/legume-allergy-2/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/great-britain-nutrition-and-health-claims-nhc-register', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('hazelnut-butter', 'UIL-0412', 'Hazelnut Butter', 'Pure hazelnut butter; hazelnut paste (where the same nut-only preparation is meant)', 'Nut and seed derivatives', 'Hazelnuts', 'Hazelnuts ground into a spreadable butter, often after roasting. The plain nut preparation is different from a sweetened chocolate-hazelnut spread.', 'Ground hazelnuts; sugar, oils, cocoa, dairy or other additions depend on the product.', 'Nut flavour, fat, texture and some protein in spreads, fillings, sauces, desserts and bakery.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Fat, including predominantly unsaturated fats, with some protein and fibre in the nut-only preparation.', 'Provides nut protein; actual contribution depends on portion and hazelnut content.', 'Naturally fat-rich; added oils alter the composition, and portion still affects energy intake.', 'Some natural hazelnut carbohydrate and sugars; sweetened spreads can add substantial free sugars.', 'Nut-only butter retains hazelnut fibre; dilution with other ingredients changes the amount.', 'No generic glucose-lowering treatment claim assigned; sweetened spreads require separate sugar assessment.', 'Can contribute dietary fibre in the nut-only preparation; no ingredient-specific gut-treatment claim assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains HAZELNUT, a regulated nut allergen. Added milk and other allergens require separate checking.', 'People with hazelnut/nut allergy or comparing nut-only butter with sweetened spreads.', 'Nut-butter jars, confectionery, fillings, desserts, sauces and bakery formulations.', 'Hazelnut Butter; Pure hazelnut butter; hazelnut paste (where the same nut-only preparation is meant)', 'No general reason to replace plain hazelnut butter; use an appropriate hazelnut-free option for allergy or a less-sweet recipe if added sugar is the concern.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Nut-derived spread with hazelnut-allergen and recipe context', 'Moderate', 'Declare and emphasise hazelnut; use actual hazelnut content and the complete recipe for nutrition and dietary claims.', 'Plain hazelnut butter is ground hazelnuts and supplies fat, some protein and fibre. It should not be treated as the same recipe as a sweetened chocolate spread.', 'hazelnut butter|pure hazelnut butter', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Hazelnuts (UIL-0145); Hazelnut Paste (UIL-0386); Hazelnut Meal (UIL-0360); Hazelnut Praline (UIL-0438)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.bulk.com/uk/products/hazelnut-butter/bpf-hbut | https://en.deanocciola.com/product/100-roasted-hazelnut-butter/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('toasted-sesame-oil', 'UIL-0413', 'Toasted Sesame Oil', 'Roasted sesame oil; sesame oil from toasted seeds', 'Oils and fats', 'Sesame seeds', 'Oil extracted from toasted or roasted sesame seeds, giving a pronounced nutty aroma.', 'Sesame seeds roasted before oil extraction; pure oils and blended products should be distinguished.', 'Flavour and fat in dressings, marinades, sauces and finishing or seasoning applications.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Fat and energy; the oil does not retain the protein and fibre profile of whole sesame seeds.', 'Essentially none in the oil; this does not establish allergy safety.', 'Mainly unsaturated fats with some saturated fat; all oils are energy-dense.', 'No meaningful carbohydrate or sugars in pure oil.', 'None in pure oil.', 'Pure oil contributes no meaningful carbohydrate, but this does not establish a glucose-treatment benefit.', 'No established generic gut-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains SESAME, a regulated allergen. Do not assume that roasting or oil extraction makes it safe for sesame allergy.', 'People with sesame allergy or checking the composition and intended cooking use of an oil blend.', 'Asian-style dressings, sauces, marinades, soups and seasoned dishes.', 'Toasted Sesame Oil; Roasted sesame oil; sesame oil from toasted seeds', 'Another suitable sesame-free oil for allergy; no general reason to replace it when sesame flavour is wanted.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Flavouring oil with sesame-allergen and portion context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise sesame; any blended oils or other ingredients need their own declaration.', 'Toasted sesame oil supplies aromatic flavour and fat. It is different from whole sesame seeds, and sesame allergy remains relevant.', 'toasted sesame oil|roasted sesame oil|sesame oil from toasted seeds', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Sesame Oil (UIL-0045); Sesame Seeds (UIL-0151); Sesame Paste (UIL-0871)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.kikkoman.co.uk/products/detail/kikkoman-toasted-sesame-oil | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.fao.org/4/Y2774E/y2774e04.htm', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cream', 'UIL-0414', 'Cream', 'Dairy cream; milk cream', 'Dairy ingredients', 'Milk', 'The milk-fat-rich fraction separated from milk, usually heat-treated for food use. The generic name covers different fat levels and preparations.', 'Dairy milk, commonly cows'' milk; species, fat level, heat treatment and additions require product-specific confirmation.', 'Richness, creamy texture, fat and, in suitable grades, whipping or emulsification in recipes.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Mainly milk fat and energy; it should not be treated as a concentrated protein or universally high-calcium ingredient.', 'Contains some milk protein; its amount varies with the preparation and portion.', 'Fat-rich, including saturated fat; single, double and whipping creams have different compositions.', 'Plain dairy cream can contain lactose; lactose-free and sweetened preparations differ.', 'None inherent in plain dairy cream.', 'The complete recipe matters; plain cream is not a glucose-treatment ingredient, and sweetened cream-based foods differ.', 'Lactose may cause symptoms in people with lactose intolerance, depending on product and portion; this is distinct from milk allergy.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MILK, a regulated allergen. Lactose-free dairy cream still contains milk protein.', 'People with milk allergy or lactose intolerance, those reducing saturated fat, and people needing pasteurised foods.', 'Sauces, soups, desserts, bakery, confectionery, ice cream and cream-based dishes.', 'Cream; Dairy cream; milk cream', 'Lower-fat plain yoghurt or another suitable lower-fat preparation where the recipe allows; a verified milk-free option is needed for milk allergy.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Dairy fat ingredient requiring milk-allergen, fat-level and recipe context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise milk; preparation names, nutrition and any lactose-free claim must describe the actual product.', 'Cream adds milk fat and texture. Fat level, lactose and added ingredients vary, and lactose-free cream remains unsuitable for milk allergy.', 'cream|dairy cream|milk cream', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Double Cream (UIL-0440); Single Cream (UIL-0466); Whipping Cream (UIL-0492); Cream Powder (UIL-0570); Soured Cream (UIL-0518)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/milk-and-dairy-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.arlafoods.co.uk/brands/lactofree/whipping-and-cooking-cream-200ml/', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('egg-yolk', 'UIL-0415', 'Egg Yolk', 'Egg yolks; hen egg yolk', 'Egg ingredients', 'Egg', 'The yellow central part of an egg, separated from the white; usually hens'' eggs in commercial foods.', 'Egg yolks from a verified bird species; liquid, dried, salted and sugared preparations have different compositions.', 'Emulsification, colour, richness, binding and texture in foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Fat, protein and choline, with other micronutrients; composition depends on preparation and portion.', 'Contains egg protein but is not equivalent to egg white or isolated egg-white protein.', 'Contains substantial egg fat, including phospholipids, and dietary cholesterol.', 'Plain yolk has little carbohydrate; sugared preparations and compound recipes differ.', 'None in plain egg yolk.', 'No generic glucose-lowering benefit assigned; carbohydrate in the complete food matters.', 'No established gut-treatment claim assigned to an egg-yolk ingredient mention.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains EGG, a regulated allergen. Separated yolk must not be assumed safe for someone with egg allergy.', 'People with egg allergy; anyone using raw or lightly cooked yolks should follow applicable egg-safety guidance.', 'Mayonnaise, custards, pasta, bakery, sauces, desserts and emulsified formulations.', 'Egg Yolk; Egg yolks; hen egg yolk', 'An appropriate egg-free emulsifier or recipe for egg allergy; no general reason to replace yolk where its function is wanted.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Egg-derived nutrient and functional ingredient with egg-allergen context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise egg; separated yolks and egg preparations require appropriate hygiene, storage and handling.', 'Egg yolk supplies fat, protein and choline and helps emulsify foods. It is a separate preparation from egg white, and egg allergy remains relevant.', 'egg yolk|egg yolks|hen egg yolk|hen''s egg yolk', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Egg Yolk Powder (UIL-0072); Liquid Egg Yolk (UIL-0441); Salted Egg Yolk (UIL-0467); Sugared Egg Yolk (UIL-0493); Egg White (UIL-0311)', 'Egg yolk contains natural phospholipids; isolated lecithin (E322) is a distinct additive preparation, not an automatic alias for yolk.', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Choline-HealthProfessional/ | https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9385935/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-on-safe-storage-handling-and-use-of-eggs-for-catering', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('pork', 'UIL-0416', 'Pork', 'Pig meat; pork meat', 'Meat and poultry ingredients', 'Pig', 'Meat from pigs. Pork is classified as red meat in dietary guidance, even when cooked meat looks pale.', 'Pig muscle meat; cut, trimming, fat content, cooking and preservation vary.', 'Protein, flavour and texture in meat dishes and prepared foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Protein and micronutrients such as B vitamins, iron and zinc; fat varies greatly by cut and trimming.', 'A substantial source of animal protein in plain meat; contribution depends on portion.', 'Cut-dependent, with both saturated and unsaturated fats; lean cuts differ from belly and added pork fat.', 'Little inherent carbohydrate in plain meat; coatings, sauces and marinades can add carbohydrate or sugars.', 'None inherent in pork muscle meat.', 'Plain pork supplies little carbohydrate; this does not establish a glucose-treatment or unrestricted-intake benefit.', 'No gut-treatment claim assigned. Assess red/processed-meat intake in the context of overall diet.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pork is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; individual meat allergy and allergens in coatings or processed recipes require separate assessment.', 'People moderating red/processed-meat or saturated-fat intake, avoiding pork for dietary/religious reasons, or preparing meat safely.', 'Fresh meat dishes, ready meals, fillings and meat-based products; cured products require separate assessment.', 'Pork; Pig meat; pork meat', 'Lean cuts, smaller portions or some replacement with pulses, fish or other suitable proteins according to the person''s dietary needs.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Red-meat protein requiring cut, frequency and preservation context', 'High', 'Food-safety and accurate meat-ingredient information apply; plain pork is different from cured or preserved pork products.', 'Pork supplies protein and micronutrients, with fat varying by cut. It counts as red meat, while curing or other preservation creates a separate processed-meat context.', 'pork|pork meat|pig meat', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pork Mince (UIL-0442); Pork Protein (UIL-0468); Pork Stock Concentrate (UIL-0494); Pork Gelatine (UIL-0520); Pork Fat (UIL-0947)', 'None inherent in plain pork; cured, seasoned or formulated products may contain additives that need separate identification.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/meat-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://doi.org/10.1017/S1368980018003762', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('haddock', 'UIL-0417', 'Haddock', 'Melanogrammus aeglefinus', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'White fish', 'An edible North Atlantic fish species, Melanogrammus aeglefinus, commonly sold as a white-fish fillet.', 'Haddock flesh; catch area, preparation, preservation and added ingredients vary.', 'Fish protein, flavour and texture in meals and prepared foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Primarily protein in plain flesh; generally low in fat, with composition affected by preparation.', 'A substantial animal-protein source in plain fish; contribution depends on portion.', 'Plain haddock is a lean white fish, not an oily-fish equivalent; frying or added oils increase fat.', 'Little inherent carbohydrate in plain fish; batter, breadcrumbs and sauces add carbohydrate.', 'None in plain fish flesh.', 'Plain fish has little carbohydrate; the finished recipe and portion determine meal-level glucose response.', 'No established generic gut-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains FISH, a regulated allergen. Cooking does not make haddock safe for fish allergy; fish and shellfish are separate allergen categories.', 'People with fish allergy; smoked products and ready meals require preparation, salt and food-safety checks.', 'Fish fillets, fishcakes, pies, ready meals and smoked or breaded preparations.', 'Haddock; Melanogrammus aeglefinus', 'No automatic replacement needed; another suitable protein for fish allergy, or a different fish species for a specific nutrition or sourcing goal.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Lean fish protein with fish-allergen and preparation context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise fish; accurate species, ingredient and food-safety information are required.', 'Haddock is a lean white fish that supplies protein. Smoked, battered or sauce-based products have additional salt, fat, carbohydrate and ingredient considerations.', 'haddock|melanogrammus aeglefinus', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cod (UIL-0391); Smoked Haddock; Fish', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/fish-and-shellfish-nutrition/ | https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/haddock | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('rapeseed-protein', 'UIL-0418', 'Rapeseed Protein', 'Rapeseed protein isolate; rapeseed protein concentrate (specified preparation); canola protein (source-qualified)', 'Plant proteins and meat alternatives', 'Rapeseed', 'A protein-rich food ingredient separated from rapeseed. It is distinct from rapeseed oil and feed-grade rapeseed meal.', 'Suitable rapeseed material, including press cake from specified low-erucic-acid/low-glucosinolate varieties; species and extraction process must match the food-grade specification.', 'Plant-protein enrichment and functional structure, emulsification or texture in suitable formulations.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Primarily protein; fat, fibre and carbohydrate contents vary with the precise preparation.', 'Plant protein; no universal protein percentage, digestibility score or amino-acid-quality claim assigned to the generic name.', 'Residual oil varies; the oil profile of rapeseed oil must not be copied to the protein ingredient.', 'Residual carbohydrate depends on the grade and recipe.', 'Variable residual fibre; it is not automatically a high-fibre ingredient.', 'No generic glucose-treatment benefit inferred from a rapeseed-protein mention.', 'No established ingredient-specific gut-treatment benefit assigned; product and portion determine tolerance.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Rapeseed protein can be relevant to MUSTARD allergy. The registered GB preparation requires a warning about possible reactions in mustard-allergic consumers.', 'People with mustard or rapeseed allergy, and formulators checking exact novel-food authorisation and product specifications.', 'Some plant-based foods, protein-enriched products and other authorised food formulations.', 'Rapeseed Protein; Rapeseed protein isolate; rapeseed protein concentrate (specified preparation); canola protein (source-qualified)', 'Another appropriate verified protein if allergy or formulation requires it; no generic reason to replace a suitable authorised preparation.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Plant protein requiring precise authorisation and mustard-allergy context', 'Moderate', 'GB NOVEL-121 specifies the designation ''Rapeseed protein'' and a mustard-allergy warning near the ingredients where relevant. Identity, specifications and use conditions must match; this is not blanket permission for every isolate.', 'Rapeseed protein can supply plant protein, but it is a different ingredient from rapeseed oil. Exact food-grade authorisation and the mustard-allergy warning are essential checks.', 'rapeseed protein|rapeseed protein isolate|rapeseed protein concentrate|canola protein', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Canola Protein (UIL-0392); Rapeseed Oil (UIL-0009); Cold-Pressed Rapeseed Oil (UIL-0231)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/novel_authorisations/novel-121 | https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2013.3420 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/great-britain-nutrition-and-health-claims-nhc-register', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('sugar-beet-fibre', 'UIL-0419', 'Sugar Beet Fibre', 'Sugar beet fiber; sugar-beet fibre; sugar-beet fiber', 'Fibres and prebiotic ingredients', 'Sugar beet', 'A human-food-grade fibre-rich ingredient made from sugar beet pulp after much of the sucrose has been extracted.', 'Processed sugar beet root pulp, prepared and dried to a food-grade specification; feed-grade beet pulp is a different suitability context.', 'Fibre enrichment, water binding, bulk and texture in formulated foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly dietary fibre, with some residual sugar, protein and minerals depending on grade.', 'May contain residual protein; not primarily a protein ingredient.', 'Usually little residual fat; no fixed composition assigned.', 'Mostly fibre polysaccharides with possible residual digestible sugars; not equivalent to beet sugar or a zero-carbohydrate ingredient.', 'Contains soluble and insoluble fibre, including pectin, cellulose and hemicellulose; amounts vary by preparation.', 'No generic glucose-lowering benefit assigned at an unspecified serving; fibre and any residual sugars need actual product data.', 'Human evidence assessed by EFSA supports increased stool bulk under studied conditions. An ingredient-list mention does not establish the amount needed or treatment of bowel disease.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Sugar beet itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; verify processing aids, blends and supplier allergen information.', 'People adjusting fibre intake or needing a confirmed food-grade preparation and tolerable serving amount.', 'Fibre-enriched breads, bakery, cereals, meat formulations and other texture-controlled foods.', 'Sugar Beet Fibre; Sugar beet fiber; sugar-beet fibre; sugar-beet fiber', 'Fibre-containing whole foods for broader dietary variety, or another suitable fibre if a particular recipe or tolerance requires it.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Added fibre ingredient with supported stool-bulk evidence and dose context', 'Moderate', 'EFSA''s stool-bulk assessment has specific food/claim conditions. Any commercial GB claim must use the authorised wording and conditions in the GB register; US technical descriptions are not GB authorisation.', 'Sugar beet fibre is mostly the fibrous material left after sugar extraction, rather than beet sugar. It can increase stool bulk in suitable amounts, but generic glucose-control or disease-treatment claims are not assigned.', 'sugar beet fibre|sugar beet fiber|sugar-beet fibre|sugar-beet fiber', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Beetroot; Pectin; Cellulose; Dietary Fibre', 'The mixed plant fibre is not automatically isolated pectin (E440) or cellulose (E460); assess any separately added additives.', 'https://www.ams.usda.gov/sites/default/files/media/Sugar%20beet%20fibers%20report%202012.pdf | https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2011.2468 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/great-britain-nutrition-and-health-claims-nhc-register', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cocoa-juice-concentrate', 'UIL-0420', 'Cocoa Juice Concentrate', 'Cacao juice concentrate; cacaofruit juice concentrate; cocoa fruit juice concentrate; concentrated cocoa pulp juice', 'Cocoa, coffee and tea derivatives', 'Cocoa fruit pulp', 'Concentrated juice from the white pulp surrounding cacao beans in the cocoa fruit, rather than a concentrate of cocoa bean powder.', 'Theobroma cacao fruit-pulp juice, separated and concentrated with appropriate food-grade processing; the exact preparation must be verified.', 'Fruit flavour, acidity, sweetness and juice solids in beverages, desserts and other formulations.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly naturally occurring fruit-juice sugars; minerals and retained pulp solids vary with concentration and process.', 'Not a substantial protein ingredient; do not copy the protein profile of cocoa beans.', 'Normally little fat; not cocoa butter or a cocoa-bean fat concentrate.', 'Fruit-juice sugars become concentrated as water is removed and contribute to free-sugar intake even without added sugar.', 'Usually limited compared with the pulp itself; cloudy and filtered grades can differ.', 'Sugar amount, dilution, portion and food matrix affect response; no fixed low-GI or glucose-lowering benefit assigned.', 'No generic probiotic, prebiotic or gut-treatment claim assigned to this juice concentrate.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Cocoa fruit pulp is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; any additives, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'People managing free sugars or carbohydrate intake, and formulators confirming exact cocoa-fruit preparation and authorisation.', 'Fruit-based drinks, sorbets, ice cream, dairy/plant desserts, jams and confectionery formulations.', 'Cocoa Juice Concentrate; Cacao juice concentrate; cacaofruit juice concentrate; cocoa fruit juice concentrate; concentrated cocoa pulp juice', 'A lower-sugar formulation where reducing free sugars is the goal; no automatically healthier sugar substitute is implied.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Cocoa-fruit juice concentrate requiring identity and free-sugar context', 'Moderate', 'GB NOVEL-62 covers specified cocoa fruit pulp, pulp juice and concentrated pulp juice as traditional food preparations. Verify identity/specification; separately extracted cocoa-pulp sugars have a different entry.', 'Cocoa juice concentrate comes from the fruit pulp around cacao beans. It adds fruity sweetness and acidity, and its sugars remain free sugars even when no sugar has been added.', 'cocoa juice concentrate|cacao juice concentrate|cacaofruit juice concentrate|cocoa fruit juice concentrate|concentrated cocoa pulp juice|concentrated cacao pulp juice', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cocoa Fruit Pulp (UIL-0394); Cocoa Powder; Cocoa Butter; Cocoa-Pulp Sugars (distinct preparation)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.barry-callebaut.com/sites/default/files/2021-09/Tech%20sheet%20CF%20juice%20concentrate.pdf | https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/novel_authorisations/novel-62 | https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/novel_authorisations/novel-133 | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/', '2026-10-14', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('orange-extract', 'UIL-0421', 'Orange Extract', 'Pure orange extract; orange flavour extract; orange flavor extract', 'Flavouring food ingredients', 'Orange', 'A concentrated orange-flavour preparation, commonly made with orange oil in a carrier. It is different from orange juice or whole fruit.', 'Orange-derived flavour components with a supplier-specific carrier such as alcohol and water; composition varies between preparations and markets.', 'Orange aroma and flavour in small amounts in bakery, desserts, confectionery, drinks and sauces.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Primarily flavour at usual use levels; it is not a dependable source of orange fibre or vitamin C.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at flavouring amounts.', 'May contain orange oil, but usual flavouring portions are not a substantial source of dietary fat.', 'Sugar and carbohydrate depend on the carrier and any additions; the name does not establish a sugar-free preparation.', 'No meaningful fruit fibre in a typical liquid flavour extract.', 'No generic glucose-lowering effect or fixed glycaemic response assigned; carrier and finished recipe matter.', 'No established generic gut-treatment benefit assigned to an orange-extract ingredient mention.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Orange itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; individual citrus allergy and allergens in the preparation require separate assessment.', 'People with citrus allergy or needing to avoid alcohol or particular carriers should check the exact extract.', 'Cakes, biscuits, desserts, confectionery, flavoured drinks and some savoury recipes.', 'Orange Extract; Pure orange extract; orange flavour extract; orange flavor extract', 'Orange zest where suitable for the recipe, or another appropriate orange flavour preparation; not a direct nutritional substitute for fruit.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Concentrated flavouring requiring carrier and recipe context', 'Moderate', 'Flavouring rules depend on the actual preparation and constituents; use the correct description and verify any natural-flavouring claim.', 'Orange extract supplies orange flavour in small amounts. Its carrier can vary, and the name does not establish the nutrition of an orange or a health benefit.', 'orange extract|pure orange extract|orange flavour extract|orange flavor extract', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Orange Juice Concentrate (UIL-0167); Orange Oil; Orange Zest; Lemon Extract (UIL-0395)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://nielsenmassey.com/products/pure-orange-extract/ | https://nielsenmassey.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/435972996-nmvi-product-catalog-intl-2021-english-compressed.pdf | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/flavourings-authorisation-guidance', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('wholegrain-mustard', 'UIL-0422', 'Wholegrain Mustard', 'Whole-grain mustard; whole grain mustard; grainy mustard; coarse-grain mustard', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Mustard condiment', 'A prepared mustard condiment retaining whole or coarsely broken mustard seeds in an acidic base.', 'Mustard seeds with water, vinegar and salt; wine, sugar, spices, preservatives and other ingredients vary by recipe.', 'Pungent flavour and seed texture in dressings, sauces, marinades, sandwiches and prepared foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly a flavouring condiment at usual portions; seeds contribute some fat and protein, while salt and added sugar vary.', 'Some seed protein, usually a small contribution at condiment portions.', 'Some natural seed fat; added oils or other ingredients change the recipe.', 'Seed carbohydrate and any added sugars depend on the formulation.', 'Seeds can contribute fibre, but typical condiment portions do not establish a high-fibre food.', 'No generic glucose-treatment benefit assigned; added sugar and the finished food need separate assessment.', 'No probiotic or gut-treatment benefit established by the seed texture or condiment name.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MUSTARD, a regulated allergen. Some recipes also contain sulphites; check the full label.', 'People with mustard allergy or sulphite sensitivity, and people monitoring salt or checking wine-derived ingredients.', 'Mustard jars, dressings, sauces, marinades, sandwiches, glazes and ready meals.', 'Wholegrain Mustard; Whole-grain mustard; whole grain mustard; grainy mustard; coarse-grain mustard', 'A mustard-free recipe for mustard allergy, or a verified lower-salt condiment if reducing salt; no general reason to replace it for most people.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Mustard condiment requiring allergen, salt and recipe context', 'Moderate', 'Declare and emphasise mustard and any other declarable allergens; sulphite declaration depends on the ready-to-consume concentration.', 'Wholegrain mustard adds mustard flavour and seed texture. Mustard allergy remains relevant, while salt, sugar, wine and sulphites depend on the recipe.', 'wholegrain mustard|whole-grain mustard|whole grain mustard|grainy mustard|coarse-grain mustard', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Mustard (UIL-0370); Mustard Seed (UIL-0403); Mustard Powder (UIL-0377); Dijon Mustard (UIL-0396)', 'Some recipes contain sulphite preservatives or acidity regulators; identify those on the actual label.', 'https://uk.maille.com/collections/price-asc-mustards/products/wholegrain-chardonnay-mustard-served-in-a-stoneware-jar | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/salt-in-your-diet/', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cookie-crumb', 'UIL-0423', 'Cookie Crumb', 'Cookie crumbs; crushed cookies; biscuit crumbs (overlapping term)', 'Bakery and cereal bases', 'Cookies or biscuits', 'Baked cookies broken or milled into crumbs for use in another food. This is a compound ingredient whose recipe determines its composition.', 'Cookies made from their own flour, sugar, fat and other ingredients; recipe and crumb size vary.', 'Crunch, flavour, decoration, inclusions, coatings or dessert bases.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Commonly carbohydrate from flour and sugars plus fat; protein, fibre and salt vary by cookie recipe.', 'Recipe-dependent; not automatically a protein ingredient.', 'Depends on the fats, butter, chocolate or nuts in the cookie.', 'Often includes flour starch and free sugars; use the actual cookie composition and portion.', 'Depends on flour and other ingredients; crumbs are not automatically high in fibre.', 'Carbohydrate, added sugar, portion and the complete dessert determine response; no fixed glycaemic index assigned.', 'No generic gut-treatment benefit assigned; assess any relevant allergens, intolerances or added polyols from the recipe.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Often contains WHEAT; milk, egg, soya, nuts or other allergens are recipe-dependent. A verified gluten-free cookie is a different formulation.', 'People with food allergy or coeliac disease, and those checking sugar, fat or dietary suitability in dessert ingredients.', 'Cheesecakes, ice cream, desserts, confectionery, toppings, bakery fillings and coatings.', 'Cookie Crumb; Cookie crumbs; crushed cookies; biscuit crumbs (overlapping term)', 'A suitable allergen-free or less-sweet crumb where needed; changing to another cookie crumb alone does not establish a nutritional improvement.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Recipe-dependent: conventional wheat-cookie crumbs contain gluten; gluten-free status requires a verified recipe and cross-contact controls.', 'Context dependent', 'Compound bakery ingredient requiring the original cookie recipe', 'Moderate', 'The compound ingredient''s components and relevant allergens must be assessed for the finished food; ''cookie crumb'' does not establish its full composition.', 'Cookie crumb is a recipe ingredient, not a single raw material. Its sugar, fat, allergens and dietary suitability come from the cookies used to make it.', 'cookie crumb|cookie crumbs|crushed cookies', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Biscuit Crumb (UIL-0397); Wheat Rusk (UIL-0371); Rusk (UIL-0345); Icing Sugar (UIL-0384)', 'Any raising agents, emulsifiers, flavourings, colours or preservatives depend on the original cookie recipe.', 'https://www.lotusbiscoff.com/en-gb/foodprofessionals/products/biscoff-cookie-crumbs-750-g | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('lactobacillus-acidophilus', 'UIL-0424', 'Lactobacillus Acidophilus', 'Lactobacillus acidophilus culture; L. acidophilus; L acidophilus', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Lactic acid bacteria', 'A bacterial species used in some food cultures and probiotic preparations. A species name does not identify the particular strain or viable dose.', 'Cultivated Lactobacillus acidophilus strains; growth medium, drying method, carriers and viable counts vary.', 'Microbial culture in some fermented foods or a specified live strain in a formulated supplement.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Not a meaningful source of protein, fat, carbohydrate, fibre or vitamins at typical culture-use levels; carriers and the food supply these separately.', 'No meaningful protein contribution from typical culture quantities; a dairy carrier can contain milk protein.', 'No meaningful dietary-fat contribution from typical culture quantities.', 'Carbohydrate carriers or the fermented food need their own assessment.', 'Bacteria are not dietary fibre; added prebiotic fibres are separate ingredients.', 'No generic glucose-lowering effect assigned without strain-, dose- and outcome-specific human evidence.', 'Potential effects are strain-, dose-, formulation- and condition-specific. The species name alone is insufficient to assign an IBS, diarrhoea or general gut-health benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The bacterium is not itself one of the 14 regulated allergens; milk or other allergens can be introduced by the commercial preparation.', 'People with severe illness or impaired immunity should seek clinical advice before probiotic supplementation; allergen-sensitive users need the exact carrier information.', 'Some fermented dairy foods, culture blends, probiotic supplements and other specified microbial preparations.', 'Lactobacillus Acidophilus; Lactobacillus acidophilus culture; L. acidophilus; L acidophilus', 'No generic replacement needed for fermentation; for a claimed clinical benefit, assess the exact studied strain and product rather than another generic culture.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Depends on the culture medium, carriers and finished product; the species name does not verify gluten-free status.', 'Context dependent', 'Culture species requiring strain, viability and product-specific evidence', 'Insufficient', 'A named culture does not establish an authorised GB health claim. Probiotic and other health-related commercial claims require the applicable evidence and claims conditions.', 'Lactobacillus acidophilus identifies a bacterial species. Meaningful health assessment needs the strain, viable count, dose and product evidence; the name alone cannot supply those details.', 'lactobacillus acidophilus|lactobacillus acidophilus culture|l. acidophilus|l acidophilus', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Probiotic Culture (UIL-0398); Lactic Acid Bacteria Culture (UIL-0242); Starter Culture (UIL-0372); Yoghurt Culture (UIL-0268)', 'Carriers, stabilisers and protective ingredients may be present; assess the supplied culture preparation.', 'https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/probiotics-usefulness-and-safety | https://www.nhs.uk/tests-and-treatments/probiotics/ | https://www.iff.com/health-sciences/our-products/howaru-ncfm/ | https://www.asa.org.uk/advice-online/food-probiotic-claims.html', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('ergocalciferol', 'UIL-0425', 'Ergocalciferol', 'Vitamin D2; vitamin D 2', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Vitamin D', 'Vitamin D2, a form of vitamin D used in foods and supplements, commonly produced from irradiated ergosterol.', 'Usually fungal or yeast-derived starting material; commercial premix carriers and capsule ingredients vary.', 'Vitamin D fortification and supplementation.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Vitamin D activity, supporting normal calcium/phosphate regulation and bone and muscle health; negligible food energy at nutritional use levels.', 'None from the vitamin compound.', 'Fat-soluble vitamin, not a meaningful source of dietary fat.', 'None from the compound itself; premix carriers can add carbohydrate.', 'None from the compound.', 'No direct carbohydrate contribution or generic diabetes-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No direct fibre or established generic microbiome benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Ergocalciferol itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; carriers and encapsulation can introduce allergens.', 'People combining vitamin D products or using prescribed vitamin D should check the total dose; excessive vitamin D can be harmful.', 'Fortified foods, plant-based drinks, cereals, spreads, supplements and some licensed medicines.', 'Ergocalciferol; Vitamin D2; vitamin D 2', 'An appropriate vitamin D source according to dietary needs and UK guidance; no universal reason to reject D2.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Essential vitamin source requiring dose and formulation context', 'High', 'Ergocalciferol is a listed GB vitamin-D form for food fortification; product, dose, supplement, medicines and claims requirements depend on the use.', 'Ergocalciferol is vitamin D2. It can contribute use