  ('magnesium-citrate', 'UIL-0426', 'Magnesium Citrate', 'Magnesium salts of citric acid; citrate of magnesium', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Magnesium', 'Magnesium salt forms of citric acid used to supply magnesium. Hydration state and formulation affect the amount of elemental magnesium per gram.', 'Manufactured food-grade magnesium citrate; exact salt composition, water content and carriers vary by grade.', 'Magnesium fortification or supplementation; medicinal laxative preparations are a separate use context.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Magnesium; the total citrate-salt weight is not the same as the elemental magnesium delivered.', 'None from the pure salt.', 'None from the pure salt.', 'Not a meaningful sugar or starch ingredient; carriers and the finished food may add carbohydrate.', 'None from the pure salt.', 'No generic glucose-lowering benefit assigned from an ingredient-list mention.', 'Supplemental magnesium can loosen stools or cause diarrhoea at sufficient doses; medicinal laxative use is not equivalent to an ingredient amount in food.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The citrate salt itself is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; premix and capsule ingredients require separate assessment.', 'People with impaired kidney function, combining magnesium products, or taking medicines affected by magnesium should check product-specific professional advice.', 'Magnesium supplements, mineral blends, fortified products and specified medicinal preparations.', 'Magnesium Citrate; Magnesium salts of citric acid; citrate of magnesium', 'Magnesium-containing foods for ordinary dietary needs, or another appropriate magnesium preparation if clinically or technically indicated.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Magnesium source requiring elemental-dose and 