  ('l-lysine-hydrochloride', 'UIL-0427', 'L-Lysine Hydrochloride', 'L-lysine HCl; L lysine hydrochloride; lysine hydrochloride; L-lysine monohydrochloride', 'Amino acids and functional nutrition', 'L-Lysine', 'The hydrochloride salt form of the essential amino acid L-lysine, supplied as an isolated nutrition ingredient.', 'Food-grade L-lysine hydrochloride. Fermentation-derived lysine is commercially produced; actual manufacturing inputs and preparation require supplier confirmation.', 'To supply lysine in supplements, amino-acid blends and suitable formulated nutritional products.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Lysine; the weight of its hydrochloride salt is not identical to the amount of lysine base.', 'Supplies one essential amino acid, not all essential amino acids or a complete dietary protein.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'None in the pure salt; carriers and blends may contain carbohydrate.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'No generic glucose-lowering effect assigned from the name alone.', 'No established generic gut-treatment benefit assigned; concentrated-product dose and formulation affect tolerance.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The pure lysine salt is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; carriers, processing inputs and blends need separate assessment.', 'People using concentrated amino-acid products should assess actual lysine dose, dietary needs and the complete formulation.', 'Amino-acid supplements, sports-nutrition products and some formulated nutritional blends.', 'L-Lysine Hydrochloride; L-lysine HCl; L lysine hydrochloride; lysine hydrochloride; L-lysine monohydrochloride', 'Protein-containing foods for general protein needs; an isolated lysine salt has a different formulation purpose.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Isolated amino-acid salt requiring lysine-dose and source context', 'Moderate', 'Use an appropriate human-food-grade preparation and assess food/supplement and claims requirements. An animal-feed approval does not establish human-food suitability.', 'L-lysine hydrochloride supplies the essential amino acid lysine in a salt form. It does not provide a complete protein or establish a treatment or performance benefit.', 'l-lysine hydrochloride|l lysine hydrochloride|lysine hydrochloride|l-lysine hcl|l lysine hcl|l-lysine monohydrochloride', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'L-Lysine (UIL-0401); L-Valine (UIL-0375); Other Essential Amino Acids', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/ExerciseAndAthleticPerformance-HealthProfessional/ | https://dsld.od.nih.gov/label/36938 | https://www.kyowahakko-bio.co.jp/english/corporate/history/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/great-britain-nutrition-and-health-claims-nhc-register', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('fruit-infused-water', 'UIL-0428', 'Fruit-Infused Water', 'Fruit infused water; water infused with fruit', 'Water and liquid bases', 'Water and fruit', 'Drinking water flavoured by contact with fruit pieces or peel. Commercial products using the same description can include juice, extracts, sugar or other ingredients.', 'Safe drinking water and fruit; fruit type, contact time, additions and removal of the fruit vary.', 'Hydration with a light fruit flavour.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Mainly water in a simple infusion; do not assume a meaningful fruit, fibre, vitamin or electrolyte serving.', 'Normally negligible in the water portion.', 'Normally negligible in a simple fruit infusion.', 'Depends on fruit contact and any juice, sugar or syrup added; a commercial label is needed to establish sugar content.', 'Little fibre in strained water; eating the fruit is different from drinking the infusion.', 'A simple unsweetened infusion differs from a juice/syrup drink; assess actual carbohydrate instead of assuming a treatment benefit.', 'No established detox, probiotic or gut-treatment benefit assigned to fruit-infused water.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Depends on the fruit and any added ingredients; water itself is not an allergen.', 'People with a relevant fruit allergy or prescribed fluid restriction, and anyone checking sugars in a commercial drink.', 'Homemade infused water, hospitality drinks and some bottled or flavoured-water products.', 'Fruit-Infused Water; Fruit infused water; water infused with fruit', 'Plain water if fruit flavour is unnecessary; whole fruit separately if fruit fibre and nutrients are the goal.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Hydration base requiring fruit, sugar and formulation context', 'Moderate', 'The description does not establish a sugar-free, fruit-serving, vitamin or health claim; assess the actual bottled formulation.', 'Simple fruit-infused water can add flavour to hydration. It is not nutritionally equivalent to eating fruit, and commercial versions need their own ingredient and sugar checks.', 'fruit-infused water|fruit infused water|water infused with fruit', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Water (UIL-0246); Filtered Water (UIL-0324); Sparkling Water (UIL-0376); Fruit Juice', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-guidelines-and-food-labels/water-drinks-nutrition/ | https://www.uhsussex.nhs.uk/resources/healthy-eating-with-gestational-diabetes/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('celery-seed', 'UIL-0429', 'Celery Seed', 'Celery seeds; Apium graveolens seed; ground celery seed (specified form)', 'Herbs, spices and seasonings', 'Celery', 'The small dried aromatic seed/fruit commonly sold as celery seed for seasoning.', 'Celery plant, Apium graveolens; supplied whole or ground.', 'Celery-like aroma and flavour in pickles, sauces, spice blends, rubs and celery salt.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'At ordinary seasoning portions, mainly flavour; seeds contain some fat, protein and fibre.', 'Some seed protein; usually a small contribution at spice portions.', 'Contains seed fat; not equivalent to extracted celery-seed oil.', 'Some seed carbohydrate; plain seed is not added sugar.', 'Contains seed fibre; contribution depends on the portion.', 'No established generic glucose-treatment benefit assigned at culinary exposure.', 'No gut-treatment effect assigned from seasoning use; concentrated extracts require a separate assessment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains CELERY, a regulated allergen, including celery seeds and their derivatives.', 'People with celery allergy; check spice blends and sauces for celery even when the amount is small.', 'Pickles, spice mixes, savoury sauces, rubs, celery salt and some prepared foods.', 'Celery Seed; Celery seeds; Apium graveolens seed; ground celery seed (specified form)', 'No general reason to replace for most people; choose a celery-free seasoning for celery allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Culinary spice requiring celery-allergen awareness', 'High', 'Celery must be declared and emphasised when present as an allergenic ingredient; a generic spice description must not hide it.', 'Celery seed adds concentrated celery flavour. Its main specific concern at seasoning use is celery allergy; medicinal benefits cannot be inferred from the spice name.', 'celery seed|celery seeds|ground celery seed|apium graveolens seed', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Celery Salt (UIL-0430); Celery Juice (UIL-0558); Celery; Celeriac', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.tunaspice.com/seeds-whole-spices/celery-seeds | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('celery-salt', 'UIL-0430', 'Celery Salt', 'Celery salt seasoning', 'Salt and savoury bases', 'Salt and celery seed', 'A seasoning blend of salt and ground celery seed; some recipes include anti-caking agents or other ingredients.', 'Food-grade salt blended with celery seed or another specified celery preparation.', 'Combined salty and celery flavour in savoury foods and drinks.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Mainly sodium from salt at usual use levels; celery does not remove the sodium contribution.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at seasoning portions.', 'Usually a small contribution from the celery material; recipe-dependent.', 'Some carbohydrate from celery or additions, generally small at seasoning portions.', 'Not a meaningful fibre source at typical seasoning amounts.', 'No generic glucose-lowering effect assigned; evaluate the complete food.', 'No established generic gut-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains CELERY, a regulated allergen. Additional allergens depend on the full seasoning recipe.', 'People with celery allergy or reducing salt intake, including those following blood-pressure advice.', 'Seasoning jars, spice blends, sauces, dressings, savoury snacks, rubs and Bloody Mary recipes.', 'Celery Salt; Celery salt seasoning', 'Celery-free seasoning for celery allergy; salt-free herbs or spices when the goal is reducing sodium.', 'Usually vegan', 'Usually vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Salt-containing seasoning with celery-allergen context', 'Moderate', 'Declare and emphasise celery; use the actual blend and portion for nutrition and any reduced-salt claim.', 'Celery salt supplies both salt and celery flavour. It is not inherently a low-sodium alternative to salt, and celery allergy remains relevant.', 