  ('cider-vinegar-powder', 'UIL-0431', 'Cider Vinegar Powder', 'Apple cider vinegar powder; powdered cider vinegar; apple-cider-vinegar powder', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Apple cider vinegar', 'A dried cider-vinegar preparation, commonly spray-dried with a carrier so that vinegar flavour can be used in dry foods.', 'Apple cider vinegar combined with a supplier-specific drying carrier, commonly maltodextrin; acidity and extra ingredients vary.', 'Vinegar flavour and acidity in dry seasonings, snacks, sauces and some supplements.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Carrier-dependent carbohydrate and organic acids; the powder is not nutritionally identical to an equal weight of liquid vinegar.', 'Usually little in maltodextrin-based grades; other carriers require checking.', 'Usually little in simple grades; assess any blend.', 'Maltodextrin or other carriers can add digestible carbohydrate; a vinegar name does not establish sugar-free or carbohydrate-free status.', 'No meaningful apple fibre should be assumed from a vinegar-derived powder.', 'No diabetes-treatment or fixed glucose-response claim assigned; actual acid dose, carriers and food matrix differ from liquid-vinegar studies.', 'Drying or a vinegar origin does not establish live probiotic organisms or a gut-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Depends on vinegar processing, carriers and additions; check any milk-derived carrier, sulphites or other declared allergens.', 'People requiring carrier/allergen information or managing carbohydrate intake; supplement users need the actual formulation and dose.', 'Salt-and-vinegar seasonings, crisps/snacks, dry sauces, seasoning blends and some food supplements.', 'Cider Vinegar Powder; Apple cider vinegar powder; powdered cider vinegar; apple-cider-vinegar powder', 'Liquid cider vinegar where the recipe permits; choose a verified carrier formulation where a dry ingredient is needed.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Cider vinegar itself is not malt vinegar; gluten status of the carrier and full preparation requires verification.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Vinegar-derived powder requiring carrier and acidity context', 'Moderate', 'Assess the actual compound ingredient and any claims. A dried vinegar powder does not establish an authorised weight-loss, detox or probiotic claim.', 'Cider vinegar powder makes vinegar flavour usable in dry foods, often with a carbohydrate carrier. Its name does not establish the acid dose or the effects of drinking liquid vinegar.', 'cider vinegar powder|apple cider vinegar powder|powdered cider vinegar|apple-cider-vinegar powder', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Apple Cider Vinegar (UIL-0275); Maltodextrin (UIL-0001); Rice Vinegar (UIL-0379)', 'Carriers, acidity regulators or anti-caking ingredients depend on the supplier; no universal E-number assigned.', 'https://www.camstar.co.uk/en/products/vinegarpowders | https://www.drbehr.com/en/produkt/apple-cider-vinegar-powder/ | https://www.asa.org.uk/advice-online/food-probiotic-claims.html | https://www.gov.uk/food-labelling-and-packaging/ingredients-list', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('dried-pear', 'UIL-0432', 'Dried Pear', 'Dried pears; dehydrated pear; dried pear halves; dried pear pieces', 'Fruit ingredients', 'Pear', 'Pear fruit preserved by removal of water, supplied as halves, slices or pieces; soft, rehydrated and preserved versions differ.', 'Pear fruit, usually dried; some products include sulphite preservatives, oils, sweeteners or other additions.', 'Fruit flavour, sweetness and texture in snacks, bakery, cereals, desserts and fruit blends.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Carbohydrate and natural fruit sugars with fibre; water removal concentrates solids per gram compared with fresh pear.', 'Usually a small contribution; not a protein ingredient.', 'Low in plain dried pear; added oils or coatings change the composition.', 'Naturally occurring fruit sugars are concentrated per gram. Added sweeteners, if present, require separate assessment.', 'Retains some pear fibre; amount depends on peeling, drying and the actual product.', 'Can contribute appreciable carbohydrate in a small weight; portion and the complete meal matter. No fixed glycaemic index assigned.', 'Can contribute fibre; individual tolerance and portion vary, and no generic IBS-treatment claim is assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pear allergy can occur. Some dried pears contain SULPHITES, which require assessment separately from pear allergy.', 'People with pear allergy or sulphite sensitivity, and those monitoring portions and carbohydrate intake.', 'Dried-fruit snacks, fruit-and-nut mixes, cereals, granola, bakery, desserts and sauces.', 'Dried Pear; Dried pears; dehydrated pear; dried pear halves; dried pear pieces', 'Fresh pear where a higher-water fruit or larger-volume portion is wanted; no general reason to replace an appropriate unsweetened dried-fruit portion.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-