  ('pea-flour', 'UIL-0437', 'Pea Flour', 'Milled peas; dried pea flour; pea seed flour', 'Legumes and pulse derivatives', 'Peas', 'Flour made by milling dried peas, whole or dehulled. It is distinct from isolated pea starch or pea protein.', 'Dried peas (Pisum sativum), milled to a food-grade flour; variety, dehulling and heat treatment vary.', 'Pulse flavour, starch, protein, binding and texture in bakery, snacks, batters, sauces and other foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'A combination of starch carbohydrate, plant protein and fibre; exact amounts vary by flour grade.', 'Contributes pea protein; it is not the same protein concentration or composition as a pea-protein isolate.', 'Generally little inherent fat; the finished recipe can add oils or other fats.', 'Contains appreciable starch; it is not a carbohydrate-free ingredient.', 'Can contribute fibre, with dehulling and fractionation affecting the amount; use the actual specification for claims.', 'No fixed glycaemic index or glucose-lowering benefit assigned; preparation, portion and the complete food matter.', 'Pulse carbohydrate and fibre can affect tolerance in a portion- and preparation-dependent way; no generic gut-treatment claim assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pea allergy can occur despite pea being outside the 14 regulated allergens. Allergy to one legume does not establish allergy to all legumes.', 'People with pea/legume allergy or needing verified gluten-free, protein or fibre information.', 'Bakery, snacks, batters, breadings, soups, sauces and some plant-based formulations.', 'Pea Flour; Milled peas; dried pea flour; pea seed flour', 'Whole cooked peas where a flour is unnecessary, or another suitable flour for a specific allergy or technical requirement.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.