  ('hazelnut-oil', 'UIL-0439', 'Hazelnut Oil', 'Hazelnut kernel oil; roasted hazelnut oil (specified preparation)', 'Oils and fats', 'Hazelnuts', 'Oil extracted from hazelnut kernels, sold in different grades including roasted-nut preparations.', 'Hazelnut kernels; roasting, extraction, refining and blending vary by supplier.', 'Nutty flavour and fat in dressings, bakery, sauces, confectionery and other culinary applications.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Fat and energy; it does not retain the protein and fibre profile of whole hazelnuts.', 'No meaningful dietary protein contribution from pure oil; this does not establish allergy safety.', 'A fat-rich nut oil containing unsaturated and saturated fatty acids; use the supplied grade for the precise fatty-acid profile.', 'No meaningful carbohydrate or sugars in pure oil.', 'None in pure oil.', 'Pure oil supplies no meaningful carbohydrate; this does not establish a glucose-treatment benefit.', 'No established generic gut-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Derived from HAZELNUT, a regulated nut allergen. Roasting, pressing or a refined-oil description must not be assumed to establish safety for hazelnut allergy.', 'People with hazelnut/nut allergy; check blended oils and the grade''s intended cooking and storage instructions.', 'Salad dressings, bakery, sauces, desserts, confectionery and flavoured oil preparations.', 'Hazelnut Oil; Hazelnut kernel oil; roasted hazelnut oil (specified preparation)', 'A suitable hazelnut-free oil for allergy; no general reason to replace the oil when its flavour and function are wanted.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Nut-derived culinary oil with hazelnut-allergen context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise hazelnut origin; hazelnut oil is not covered by the specific fully refined soya-oil allergen exemption.', 'Hazelnut oil supplies fat and nut flavour rather than whole-nut protein or fibre. Hazelnut allergy remains relevant, and grade matters for cooking and storage.', 'hazelnut oil|hazelnut kernel oil|roasted hazelnut oil', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Hazelnuts (UIL-0145); Hazelnut Paste (UIL-0386); Hazelnut Butter (UIL-0412); Hazelnut Praline (UIL-0438)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://latourangelle.com/products/roasted-hazelnut-oil | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://latourangelle.com/pages/roasted-oils', '2026-10-15', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('double-cream', 'UIL-0440', 'Double Cream', 'Dairy double cream; double dairy cream', 'Dairy ingredients', 'Dairy cream', 'A high-milk-fat dairy cream. The Dairy UK/PTF industry code specifies at least 48% milk fat for standard double cream.', 'The milk-fat-rich fraction separated from dairy milk, commonly cows'' milk; heat treatment and added ingredients depend on the product.', 'Richness, fat, creamy texture, pouring, whipping and culinary structure in desserts and savoury recipes.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Mainly milk fat and energy, including saturated fat; not a concentrated protein or universally high-calcium ingredient.', 'Contains some milk protein; amount varies with preparation and portion.', 'Fat-rich and a source of saturated fat. The 48% industry-code minimum is a compositional standard, not a recommended serving.', 'Plain double cream can contain lactose; sweetened and lactose-free preparations differ.', 'None in plain dairy double cream.', 'The complete recipe matters; low carbohydrate relative to sweet desserts does not establish a glucose-treatment or unrestricted-intake benefit.', 'Lactose can affect people with lactose intolerance depending on product and portion; lactose intolerance is distinct from milk allergy.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MILK, a regulated allergen. Lactose-free dairy double cream still contains milk protein.', 'People with milk allergy or lactose intolerance, those reducing saturated fat, and people needing to avoid unpasteurised dairy.', 'Desserts, sauces, soups, ganache, bakery, ice cream, whipped cream and rich savoury dishes.', 'Double Cream; Dairy double cream; double dairy cream', 'A suitable lower-fat dairy preparation where the recipe permits; a verified milk-free option is needed for milk allergy.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; carriers, blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'High-fat dairy ingredient requiring milk-allergen and portion context', 'High', 'The Dairy UK/PTF code retains a 48% milk-fat standard for double cream as an industry compositional designation. The former statutory fat limits were revoked in December 2018; general food-information and milk-allergen requirements still apply.', 'Double cream is a high-fat dairy ingredient that adds richness and texture. Portion, saturated fat, lactose and milk allergy all need the actual product and recipe context.', 'double cream|dairy double cream|double dairy cream', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cream (UIL-0414); Single Cream (UIL-0466); Whipping Cream (UIL-0492); Soured Cream (UIL-0518); Cream Powder (UIL-0570)', 'None inherent; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.dairyuk.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/FINAL-Compositional-Standards-Cream.pdf | https://www.provtrade.co.uk/technical-and-legislation/labelling-and-standards.aspx | https://riverforddairy.co.uk/portfolio/organic-double-cream/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/milk-and-dairy-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('liquid-egg-yolk', 'UIL-0441', 'Liquid Egg Yolk', 'Liquid egg yolks; pasteurised liquid egg yolk; pasteurized liquid egg yolk', 'Egg ingredients', 'Egg yolk', 'Separated egg yolk supplied in liquid form, commonly pasteurised for commercial use. Salted, sugared and other formulated grades differ from plain yolk.', 'Egg yolks, usually from hens; bird species, pasteurisation, additives and storage requirements depend on the supplied preparation.', 'Emulsification, richness, colour and texture without cracking and separating shell eggs.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Plain liquid yolk supplies fat, protein and choline; added salt, sugar or water changes the composition.', 'Contains egg protein; not equivalent to egg white or isolated egg-white protein.', 'Contains egg fat, phospholipids and dietary cholesterol; the complete recipe and portion matter.', 'Little carbohydrate in plain yolk; sugared preparations need separate assessment.', 'None in plain liquid egg yolk.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; assess carbohydrate in the finished food.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned to a liquid egg-yolk ingredient.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains EGG, a regulated allergen. Separation and pasteurisation do not make it suitable for egg allergy.', 'People with egg allergy and anyone preparing raw or lightly cooked foods; verify pasteurisation and follow storage and use instructions.', 'Mayonnaise, hollandaise, custard, ice cream, bakery, pasta and other emulsified foods.', 'Liquid Egg Yolk; Liquid egg yolks; pasteurised liquid egg yolk; pasteurized liquid egg yolk', 'An appropriate egg-free recipe or emulsifier for egg allergy; no general reason to replace yolk where its function is wanted.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Egg preparation requiring allergen, formulation and handling context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise egg. Pasteurised egg products can reduce risks in uncooked or lightly cooked dishes; hygiene and product instructions still apply.', 'Liquid egg yolk provides yolk nutrients and emulsifying properties in a convenient form. Check whether it is plain, pasteurised, salted or sugared, and retain egg-allergen information.', 'liquid egg yolk|liquid egg yolks|pasteurised liquid egg yolk|pasteurized liquid egg yolk', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Egg Yolk (UIL-0415); Egg Yolk Powder (UIL-0072); Salted Egg Yolk (UIL-0467); Sugared Egg Yolk (UIL-0493); Liquid Whole Egg (UIL-0259)', 'Some grades contain acidity regulators or preservatives; these are not inherent to every liquid egg-yolk product. Egg phospholipids are not automatically isolated lecithin (E322).', 'https://www.egginfo.co.uk/british-lion-egg/products/guide/liquid-egg-yolk | https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-on-safe-storage-handling-and-use-of-eggs-for-catering | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Choline-HealthProfessional/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('pork-mince', 'UIL-0442', 'Pork Mince', 'Minced pork; ground pork', 'Meat and poultry ingredients', 'Pork', 'Pork muscle meat chopped or ground into small particles. Fat content depends on the cuts and trimming.', 'Pig meat, supplied fresh, chilled or frozen; added seasoning, water or preservatives create a different preparation.', 'Protein, flavour, texture and a form suitable for fillings, patties and mixed dishes.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Animal protein and meat micronutrients; fat and energy vary substantially between products.', 'A substantial protein source; contribution depends on the meat proportion and serving.', 'Variable, including saturated and unsaturated fat. ''Mince'' does not specify a lean percentage.', 'Little inherent carbohydrate in plain mince; fillers, breadcrumbs, sauces and seasoning can add carbohydrate.', 'None in plain pork muscle meat.', 'No glucose-lowering benefit assigned; sauces, fillers and the complete meal need assessment.', 'No gut-treatment claim assigned. Consider red- and processed-meat intake within the overall diet.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Plain pork is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; individual meat allergy and allergens added to preparations need separate checks.', 'People moderating red-meat or saturated-fat intake, avoiding pork for dietary reasons, or handling and cooking raw mince.', 'Meatballs, dumpling and pie fillings, burgers, sauces, ready meals and other pork dishes.', 'Pork Mince; Minced pork; ground pork', 'A verified leaner mince, smaller portions or a suitable pulse, fish or other protein preparation where the recipe and dietary needs permit.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Red-meat protein requiring fat-content and food-safety context', 'High', 'Pork mince should be cooked thoroughly throughout. Appropriate chilling and prevention of raw-to-ready-to-eat cross-contamination remain necessary.', 'Pork mince supplies protein, with fat depending on the cut and recipe. Mincing is different from curing or preservation, but it increases the importance of thorough cooking.', 'pork mince|minced pork|ground pork', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pork (UIL-0416); Pork Protein (UIL-0468); Pork Fat (UIL-0947); Pork Stock Concentrate (UIL-0494)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/meat-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cooking-your-food/cooking-your-food | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('pollock', 'UIL-0443', 'Pollock', 'Pollack; lythe; Pollachius pollachius (UK commercial designation)', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'White fish', 'An edible white-fish name. The UK commercial designation Pollock/Pollack/Lythe refers to Pollachius pollachius; other markets and qualified names can refer to different species.', 'Fish flesh from the declared species and fishery; retain the scientific name, catch information and actual preparation when available.', 'Protein, mild fish flavour and flaky texture in fish dishes and manufactured fish products.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Protein with relatively little fat in plain white-fish flesh; coatings, sauces and processing change the contribution.', 'A source of fish protein; the fish proportion matters in coated and formed products.', 'Plain pollock is a low-fat white fish, not nutritionally interchangeable with oily fish.', 'Little inherent carbohydrate in plain fish; batter, breadcrumbs and sauces can add starch and sugar.', 'None in plain fish flesh.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; assess coatings, starches, sauces and the full meal.', 'No established ingredient-specific gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains FISH, a regulated allergen. Fish allergy is distinct from crustacean or mollusc allergy.', 'People with fish allergy; check bones, cooking instructions and the composition of coated or formed products.', 'Fish fillets, fish fingers, fish cakes, pies, breaded products and prepared fish dishes.', 'Pollock; Pollack; Lythe; Pollachius pollachius', 'No general reason to replace suitable plain fish. For fish allergy use a verified fish-free recipe; oily fish has a different nutritional role.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'White-fish protein requiring species and fish-allergen context', 'Moderate', 'Use the appropriate UK commercial designation and fish-allergen declaration for the actual species and product; species-specific labelling requirements depend on the marketed form.', 'Pollock is a white-fish ingredient that supplies protein. Confirm the species and recipe, especially where the label specifies Alaska or Pacific pollock, and retain the fish-allergen flag.', 'pollock|pollack|lythe|pollachius pollachius', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Alaska Pollock (UIL-0469); Cod (UIL-0391); Haddock (UIL-0417); Fish', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/commercial-designations-of-fish-united-kingdom/commercial-designations-of-fish | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/fish-and-shellfish-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('wheat-protein-isolate', 'UIL-0444', 'Wheat Protein Isolate', 'Isolated wheat protein; wheat-protein isolate', 'Plant proteins and meat alternatives', 'Wheat protein', 'A concentrated wheat-protein preparation separated from much of the grain''s other material; functional properties depend on the exact grade.', 'Wheat proteins, including gluten fractions; isolation, modification and any processing aids or carriers vary by supplier.', 'Protein enrichment, dough structure, elasticity, binding and texture in bakery and other formulated foods.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Concentrated wheat protein, without the full starch, fibre and micronutrient profile of whole wheat.', 'High protein concentration by design; purity and amino-acid balance require the actual specification. It is not a complete meal or all-purpose protein replacement.', 'Usually little fat in a simple isolate; assess the grade and finished recipe.', 'Starch and sugars are reduced relative to wheat flour, but the name does not guarantee zero carbohydrate.', 'Not equivalent to wholegrain fibre; no high-fibre content should be assumed.', 'No glucose-lowering benefit assigned from protein isolation; assess the complete formulation.', 'Contains wheat gluten; unsuitable for routine coeliac avoidance. No generic gut-health benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains WHEAT. Some grades use sulphite processing, so sulphite content and any declaration requirement need the current specification.', 'People with wheat allergy or coeliac disease, sulphite-sensitive users when relevant, and anyone relying on a defined protein or gluten specification.', 'Bread, bakery, pasta, protein-enriched foods, bars and some plant-based meat preparations.', 'Wheat Protein Isolate; Isolated wheat protein; wheat-protein isolate', 'A verified wheat-free protein for wheat allergy or coeliac needs, matched to the recipe''s nutritional and structural requirements.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'Contains wheat gluten; isolation does not establish gluten-free status or suitability for coeliac disease.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Concentrated wheat protein requiring gluten, allergen and grade context', 'Moderate', 'Declare and emphasise wheat. Assess sulphites and nutrition claims using the actual supplied grade and finished-food conditions.', 'Wheat protein isolate adds concentrated protein and structure. It still requires a wheat/gluten assessment, and commercial grades differ in processing, purity and functionality.', 'wheat protein isolate|isolated wheat protein|wheat-protein isolate', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Wheat Protein (UIL-0356); Hydrolysed Wheat Protein (UIL-0470); Textured Wheat Protein (UIL-0626); Wheat Gluten (UIL-0078); Vital Wheat Gluten', 'Processing aids or additives can vary by grade. Do not assign sulphites or a universal E-number to all wheat protein isolates.', 'https://mgpingredients.com/food-ingredients/products/line/arise | https://new.mgpingredients.com/sites/default/files/2018-03/Wheat_Protein_Isolates_Properties_and_Functionality.pdf | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('bamboo-fibre', 'UIL-0445', 'Bamboo Fibre', 'Bamboo fiber; bamboo dietary fibre; bamboo dietary fiber', 'Fibres and prebiotic ingredients', 'Bamboo', 'An isolated plant-fibre ingredient derived from bamboo stalk material, commonly rich in insoluble cellulose and hemicellulose.', 'Food-grade bamboo stalk fibre, refined and milled into supplier-specific particle sizes and grades.', 'Fibre enrichment, texture, water management and reformulation in manufactured foods.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Mainly insoluble dietary fibre in the defined food-grade preparation; it does not reproduce the nutrient profile of a whole vegetable.', 'Not a meaningful protein ingredient in a purified fibre grade.', 'Normally little dietary fat; assess the specification and added ingredients.', 'Mainly non-digestible fibre rather than sugar; do not infer a finished-food low-carbohydrate or calorie claim.', 'An insoluble fibre source; the amount and analytical specification determine the actual fibre contribution.', 'No fixed glycaemic or glucose-treatment effect established from the generic name.', 'Tolerance depends on fibre amount and the complete diet. Insoluble bamboo fibre is not automatically an evidence-backed prebiotic or an IBS treatment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Bamboo is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; individual allergy, added ingredients and cross-contact require separate assessment.', 'People sensitive to changes in fibre intake and anyone needing verified gluten-free, food-grade or compositional information.', 'Fibre-enriched bakery, tortillas, meat preparations, plant-based foods and other texture-controlled formulations.', 'Bamboo Fibre; Bamboo fiber; bamboo dietary fibre; bamboo dietary fiber', 'A suitable whole-food fibre source where the nutritional aim permits, or another verified fibre matched to the technical need; no universal substitute.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Isolated insoluble fibre requiring dose and grade context', 'Moderate', 'Verify food-grade identity, permitted intended use and any applicable novel-food requirements for the exact material. A generic bamboo name does not establish these for every extract or manufacturing process.', 'Bamboo fibre is a concentrated fibre and texture ingredient. Assess the grade and amount used rather than treating it as a whole vegetable or assigning a general prebiotic benefit.', 'bamboo fibre|bamboo fiber|bamboo dietary fibre|bamboo dietary fiber', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cellulose (UIL-0039); Powdered Cellulose; Wheat Fibre (UIL-0382); Oat fibre (UIL-0038)', 'No E-number is assigned from the name alone. A supplied cellulose additive grade requires its own identity and specification.', 'https://www.jrs.eu/en/food-ingredients/products/vitacel-bamboo-fiber.php | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/novel-foods-authorisation-guidance/novel-foods-authorisation-guidance | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.asa.org.uk/advice-online/food-probiotic-claims.html', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('chocolate-liquor', 'UIL-0446', 'Chocolate Liquor', 'Cocoa liquor; cocoa mass; cacao mass; cocoa paste; unsweetened chocolate', 'Cocoa, coffee and tea derivatives', 'Cocoa mass', 'Finely ground cocoa-nib material containing cocoa solids and cocoa butter. The term liquor describes the cocoa preparation rather than an alcoholic drink.', 'Cocoa beans processed into nibs and ground into a paste; roasting, alkalisation and permitted additions vary by grade.', 'Cocoa flavour, colour, fat and solids in chocolate and related foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Energy-dense cocoa material containing cocoa fat and other cocoa solids, including fibre; it is different from defatted cocoa powder.', 'Contains some cocoa protein but is not primarily a protein ingredient.', 'Contains substantial cocoa butter. Do not apply one fixed fat percentage to every international grade.', 'Plain unsweetened cocoa mass has no added sugar; the finished chocolate or dessert can contain substantial added sugars.', 'Contains cocoa fibre; contribution depends on the actual grade and use level.', 'An unsweetened ingredient does not make the finished food sugar-free or establish a glucose-treatment benefit.', 'No ingredient-specific gut-treatment benefit assigned; assess the cocoa amount and complete formulation.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Cocoa is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; added milk, soya and other ingredients or cross-contact need separate checks.', 'People with cocoa allergy or product-specific sensitivities, and anyone needing to check added sugar or milk in the finished food.', 'Chocolate, coatings, fillings, bakery, ice cream and cocoa-based desserts.', 'Chocolate Liquor; Cocoa liquor; cocoa mass; cacao mass; cocoa paste; unsweetened chocolate', 'No general reason to replace suitable cocoa mass. Assess the full recipe and added sugar; cocoa powder has a different fat content and function.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Cocoa ingredient requiring unsweetened-grade and recipe context', 'High', 'Cocoa/chocolate composition rules depend on the jurisdiction and finished product. The US chocolate-liquor definition is a terminology/composition reference, not a GB labelling authorisation.', 'Chocolate liquor is ground cocoa material, also called cocoa mass. It supplies cocoa solids and fat; its name does not mean an alcoholic beverage or a sweetened chocolate recipe.', 'chocolate liquor|cocoa liquor|cocoa mass|cacao mass|cocoa paste|unsweetened chocolate', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cocoa Mass (UIL-0182); Cocoa Nibs (UIL-0183); Cocoa Powder (UIL-0181); Cocoa Butter (UIL-0057); Dark Chocolate (UIL-0185)', 'Some grades permit alkali treatment or other additions. Do not infer an alkali, emulsifier or E-number from the name alone.', 'https://www.cargill.com/food-bev/emea/cocoa-chocolate/cocoa-liquor | https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-21/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-163/subpart-B/section-163.111 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('lime-extract', 'UIL-0447', 'Lime Extract', 'Pure lime extract; lime flavour extract; lime flavor extract', 'Flavouring food ingredients', 'Lime', 'A concentrated culinary lime-flavour preparation, often made with lime oil in a carrier. It is different from lime juice, whole fruit and medicinal botanical extracts.', 'Lime-derived flavour material with supplier-specific carriers such as alcohol and water; formulation and extraction vary.', 'Lime aroma and flavour in small amounts in foods and drinks.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Primarily a flavour ingredient at usual use levels; it is not a meaningful whole-fruit, fibre or vitamin-C serving.', 'Usually negligible at flavouring use levels; carriers and the finished recipe need separate assessment.', 'Can contain lime oil, but ordinary flavouring quantities are not a meaningful dietary-fat source.', 'Carriers differ; the generic name does not verify sugar-free or carbohydrate-free status.', 'Not a meaningful fibre ingredient.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; the carrier and finished food determine carbohydrate relevance.', 'No established detox, probiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned to culinary lime extract.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Lime is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; citrus allergy, carriers and any added ingredients need their own assessment.', 'People with citrus allergy or sensitivity, those avoiding alcohol, and anyone needing exact carrier or allergen information.', 'Bakery, ice cream, desserts, confectionery, sauces, beverages and flavour blends.', 'Lime Extract; Pure lime extract; lime flavour extract; lime flavor extract', 'Lime zest or juice where the recipe permits; these differ in acidity, water content and flavour strength.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Concentrated citrus flavour requiring carrier and use-level context', 'Moderate', 'Assess the actual flavouring declaration and formulation. ''Natural'' or ''pure'' wording does not establish nutritional equivalence to fruit or a health benefit.', 'Lime extract supplies concentrated flavour rather than a serving of lime. Carrier, alcohol content and recipe details matter more than the extract name alone.', 'lime extract|pure lime extract|lime flavour extract|lime flavor extract', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Orange Extract (UIL-0421); Lemon Extract (UIL-0395); Lime Juice; Lime Oil; Lime Juice Concentrate', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://cooksvanilla.com/products/pure-lime-extract | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('english-mustard', 'UIL-0448', 'English Mustard', 'Prepared English mustard; English-style mustard', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Mustard condiment', 'A pungent prepared mustard condiment commonly made from mustard flour, water and seasoning. Recipes vary, and some include wheat flour.', 'Mustard seed flour with water, salt and recipe-dependent sugar, acids, spices, thickeners or other ingredients.', 'Pungency, savoury flavour and seasoning in condiments, sauces and prepared dishes.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly flavour and seasoning at usual portions; salt and added sugars depend on the recipe.', 'Some seed/flour protein, generally a small contribution at condiment portions.', 'Some mustard-seed fat; added oils and the amount used change the contribution.', 'Mustard/wheat flour and any added sugar contribute carbohydrate; do not assume a sugar-free formulation.', 'Some seed material may remain, but a small condiment portion is not a major fibre source.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; assess added sugar, flour, portion and the finished food.', 'No established ingredient-specific gut-treatment or probiotic benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MUSTARD. Some products also contain WHEAT; check the full preparation for other allergens.', 'People with mustard allergy, wheat allergy or coeliac disease when wheat is used, and those monitoring salt intake.', 'Sandwiches, sauces, dressings, gravies, meat dishes, ready meals and condiments.', 'English Mustard; Prepared English mustard; English-style mustard', 'For mustard allergy use a verified mustard-free recipe. For coeliac needs, a specifically verified gluten-free mustard preparation may be required.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Some English mustard contains wheat flour, as in Colman''s example. Do not assign gluten-free status from the condiment name.', 'Context dependent', 'Mustard condiment requiring mustard, wheat and recipe context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise mustard and any wheat or other regulated allergens actually present. Assess the complete recipe rather than copying one brand''s specification.', 'English mustard adds strong flavour in small amounts. Mustard allergy is inherent, while wheat, salt, sugar and other additions depend on the preparation.', 'english mustard|prepared english mustard|english-style mustard', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Mustard (UIL-0370); Mustard Powder (UIL-0377); Mustard Seed (UIL-0403); Dijon Mustard (UIL-0396); Wholegrain Mustard (UIL-0422)', 'Acids, thickeners or preservatives may be present. Colman''s lists citric acid and xanthan gum; these are examples rather than universal English-mustard ingredients.', 'https://www.colmans.co.uk/p/english-mustard.html/00000050147311 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cake-crumb', 'UIL-0449', 'Cake Crumb', 'Cake crumbs; crumbled cake', 'Bakery and cereal bases', 'Baked cake', 'Baked cake broken or manufactured into small crumbs for use as another food ingredient. The original cake recipe determines its composition.', 'A baked recipe containing flour or other starch, sweeteners, fats and optional egg, dairy, cocoa or other components.', 'Cake flavour, texture, inclusions, layers and toppings in desserts and bakery.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually carbohydrate with variable sugar and fat; the recipe and crumb portion determine nutrition.', 'Recipe-dependent; do not treat cake crumb as a concentrated protein ingredient.', 'Depends on the cake''s fats, oils, dairy, coating and filling.', 'Typically includes flour starch and added sugars, but no universal sugar or carbohydrate value is assigned.', 'Depends on flour, fruit, nuts and other recipe ingredients; wholegrain/high-fibre status cannot be inferred.', 'The amount, recipe and meal context determine glucose relevance; no fixed glycaemic index or treatment claim.', 'Tolerance depends on the full recipe, including any milk, wheat or other individually relevant components.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Common recipes contain WHEAT, EGG and/or MILK; SOYA, nuts or other allergens can also occur. The name alone does not specify a universal allergen list.', 'People with food allergy or coeliac disease, those avoiding animal ingredients, and anyone assessing sugar, fat or the full compound recipe.', 'Ice cream, layered desserts, cake pops, bakery fillings, dessert toppings and confectionery.', 'Cake Crumb; Cake crumbs; crumbled cake', 'A verified allergen-free or differently formulated crumb matched to the recipe; a smaller topping portion may suit sugar or energy goals.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Usually relevant when wheat flour is used, but verified gluten-free recipes exist. Obtain the full cake formulation.', 'Context dependent', 'Compound baked ingredient requiring full recipe and allergen details', 'Moderate', 'Assess the component ingredients and allergens of the actual compound preparation. ''Cake crumb'' is not a sufficient specification for dietary or nutrition claims.', 'Cake crumb is a small form of a complete baked recipe. Its sugar, fat, allergens and dietary suitability must come from that recipe rather than the crumb name.', 'cake crumb|cake crumbs|crumbled cake', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cookie Crumb (UIL-0423); Biscuit Crumb (UIL-0397); Chocolate Crumb (UIL-0472); Milk Chocolate Crumb (UIL-0498); Breadcrumbs (UIL-0241)', 'Raising agents, emulsifiers, colours, flavourings or preservatives may be present according to the cake recipe; no universal list.', 'https://www.parkerfoodgroup.com/cookie-crumbs | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('lactobacillus-rhamnosus', 'UIL-0450', 'Lactobacillus Rhamnosus', 'Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus; Lactobacillus rhamnosus culture; L. rhamnosus', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Lactic acid bacteria', 'A bacterial species now named Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus, also labelled under its older Lactobacillus name. The species name does not identify a particular strain.', 'Cultivated bacteria in a product-specific culture preparation; strain, medium, carrier, drying, viable count and storage vary.', 'Microbial culture in selected foods or as a defined live strain in a probiotic supplement.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Usually little direct macronutrient contribution at culture-use levels; carriers and the food supply nutrients separately.', 'No meaningful protein contribution from typical culture quantities; protein-containing carriers may be present.', 'Usually negligible from the culture quantity; assess the supplied preparation.', 'Sugars or starch may occur in carriers or the food; the species does not define these.', 'Bacteria are not dietary fibre; any added prebiotic is a separate ingredient.', 'No generic glucose-treatment effect assigned without strain-, dose- and outcome-specific human evidence.', 'Effects depend on the exact strain, viable amount, product, condition and population. The species name alone does not establish a clinical gut-health benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The bacterium is not itself one of the 14 regulated allergens; milk or other allergens may occur in the commercial preparation.', 'People with serious illness or impaired immunity should seek clinical advice before probiotic supplementation; check carriers and product suitability.', 'Some fermented foods, culture blends, probiotic supplements and other specified microbial preparations.', 'Lactobacillus Rhamnosus; Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus; Lactobacillus rhamnosus culture; L. rhamnosus', 'No generic replacement needed for fermentation. For a claimed benefit, assess the exact studied strain and product rather than substituting a species name.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Culture medium, carrier ingredients and relevant residues require checks; the species name does not verify gluten-free status.', 'Context dependent', 'Culture species requiring strain, viability and product-specific evidence', 'Insufficient', 'A named bacterium does not establish an authorised GB health claim. Probiotic and health-related commercial wording must meet the relevant claims conditions.', 'Lactobacillus rhamnosus and Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus name the same species. A health assessment still needs its exact strain, viable amount, use and human evidence.', 'lactobacillus rhamnosus|lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus|lactobacillus rhamnosus culture|l. rhamnosus|l rhamnosus', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Probiotic Culture (UIL-0398); Lactic Acid Bacteria Culture (UIL-0242); Starter Culture (UIL-0372); Lactobacillus Acidophilus (UIL-0424); Yoghurt Culture (UIL-0268)', 'Carriers, stabilisers and protective ingredients may be present; assess the actual culture preparation.', 'https://lpsn.dsmz.de/species/lacticaseibacillus-rhamnosus | https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/probiotics-usefulness-and-safety | https://www.asa.org.uk/advice-online/food-probiotic-claims.html', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('vitamin-e', 'UIL-0451', 'Vitamin E', 'Vitamin-E; vitamin E family', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Vitamin E family', 'A family of fat-soluble compounds. Alpha-tocopherol is the form recognised for meeting human vitamin E requirements; labels may specify different tocopherols or esters.', 'Vitamin preparations from plant-derived material and/or chemical manufacture; exact form, potency, carriers and capsule ingredients require the supplier specification.', 'Vitamin fortification or supplementation; specified tocopherol preparations can also protect food fats from oxidation.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Provides vitamin E, involved in antioxidant protection and normal immune function; contribution depends on form and dose.', 'Not a protein ingredient; any protein carrier is separate.', 'Fat-soluble does not mean it supplies a meaningful amount of dietary fat; oil carriers require their own assessment.', 'The vitamin itself is not sugar or starch; powders, carriers and supplements can contain carbohydrate.', 'Not dietary fibre.', 'No generic glucose-lowering or diabetes-treatment effect assigned.', 'Absorption and the preparation matter, but vitamin E is not a probiotic or a generic gut treatment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Check the preparation''s carriers and any applicable allergen exemptions. Specified soybean-derived natural tocopherols/esters are exempt from mandatory soya declaration; do not infer soya allergy from ''vitamin E'' alone.', 'People considering high-dose supplements, especially those taking anticoagulant or antiplatelet medicines; product carriers also matter for allergies and dietary requirements.', 'Fortified foods, nutrition products, supplements, oils and foods using specified antioxidant preparations.', 'Vitamin E; Vitamin-E', 'A varied diet can provide vitamin E. When supplementation is needed, use an appropriate verified form and dose; no universal advantage follows from ''natural'' or ''synthetic'' wording.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Essential vitamin requiring exact form, purpose and dose context', 'High', 'Permitted vitamin forms and fortification conditions differ from food-antioxidant additive rules. E306 and E307 are defined preparations, not automatic codes for every vitamin-E ingredient.', 'Vitamin E has an established nutritional role, but the exact form and dose matter. Trace antioxidant use in food is different from high-dose supplementation.', 'vitamin e|vitamin-e', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'D-Alpha-Tocopherol (UIL-0503); DL-Alpha-Tocopheryl Acetate (UIL-0477); Tocopherols; Tocotrienols', 'Related antioxidant preparations include tocopherol-rich extract (E306) and alpha-tocopherol (E307); confirm identity and function before mapping. An acetate vitamin preparation is not automatically E307.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-e/ | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/VitaminE-HealthProfessional/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods | https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/food_authorisations/e-306 | https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/food_authorisations/e-307 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('magnesium-carbonate', 'UIL-0452', 'Magnesium Carbonate', 'Carbonate of magnesium; MgCO3 (anhydrous chemical formula)', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Magnesium mineral salts', 'A magnesium-containing inorganic carbonate used as a mineral source and in specified food-additive preparations. Hydrated and basic carbonate grades need their own specifications.', 'Manufactured and purified food-grade magnesium carbonate; hydration, basic-carbonate composition, purity and carriers vary.', 'Magnesium fortification/supplementation and anticaking or other permitted technological functions in specified foods.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Can provide magnesium; meaningful contribution depends on elemental magnesium amount and use level, not the total salt mass alone.', 'None in the pure mineral preparation.', 'None in the pure mineral preparation.', 'Carbonate is an inorganic ion, not dietary carbohydrate or sugar; carriers may add carbohydrate.', 'None in the pure mineral preparation.', 'An essential mineral role does not establish a glucose-treatment benefit from this ingredient mention.', 'High supplemental or medicinal magnesium doses can cause diarrhoea and abdominal symptoms; this is different from ordinary low-level technological use.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The pure mineral is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; check excipients, carriers and the complete preparation.', 'People with impaired kidney function or using substantial magnesium supplements, laxatives or interacting medicines should obtain appropriate clinical advice.', 'Mineral supplements, fortified nutrition products and foods using a permitted magnesium-carbonate anticaking preparation.', 'Magnesium Carbonate; carbonate of magnesium', 'Food sources can supply magnesium. A different supplement salt requires an appropriate elemental dose and suitability assessment; no universal best salt is established here.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Mineral source or functional ingredient requiring form and dose context', 'High', 'Magnesium carbonate is listed as a GB mineral source. Magnesium carbonates are covered by E504 additive authorisation with applicable specifications and use conditions; authorisation is not unrestricted use.', 'Magnesium carbonate can supply magnesium or serve a technical food function. Identify the exact grade and elemental dose, and keep supplement effects separate from small additive amounts.', 'magnesium carbonate|carbonate of magnesium|mgco3', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Magnesium Citrate (UIL-0426); Magnesium Oxide (UIL-0400); Magnesium Chloride (UIL-0478); Magnesium Sulphate (UIL-0504)', 'E504 is the magnesium-carbonates group. Normal magnesium carbonate and magnesium hydroxide carbonate/basic grades require their correct identities; do not infer subtype from E504 alone.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods | https://data.food.gov.uk/regulated-products/food_authorisations/e-504 | https://www.fao.org/fileadmin/user_upload/jecfa_additives/docs/Monograph1/Additive-257.pdf | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Magnesium-HealthProfessional/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('l-methionine', 'UIL-0453', 'L-Methionine', 'L methionine', 'Amino acids and functional nutrition', 'Methionine', 'The L-form of methionine, an essential sulphur-containing amino acid used to build proteins. The isolated ingredient supplies one amino acid rather than a complete protein.', 'Manufactured and purified L-methionine for the stated food or nutrition use; manufacturing route, grade and added carriers require verification.', 'Amino-acid provision in selected supplements, nutrition preparations and foods for defined nutritional purposes.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'One essential amino acid; it does not provide all essential amino acids or the nutrients of a whole protein food.', 'Contributes methionine to amino-acid intake. A free amino acid is not a complete dietary protein.', 'None in pure L-methionine; oil carriers or other ingredients are separate.', 'Not sugar or starch; a formulated powder or capsule may contain carbohydrate ingredients.', 'None in pure L-methionine.', 'No generic glucose-lowering or diabetes-treatment effect assigned.', 'No established generic gut-treatment benefit assigned to the isolated ingredient; formulation and concentrated dose affect suitability.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pure L-methionine is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; the source preparation and excipients require separate checks.', 'People using concentrated amino-acid supplements or following a prescribed amino-acid/protein diet need the actual dose, formulation and relevant clinical advice.', 'Amino-acid blends, selected supplements, clinical nutrition and specified formulated foods.', 'L-Methionine; L methionine', 'Suitable protein foods normally supply methionine within a varied diet. Isolated supplementation needs a defined purpose; other amino acids are not direct substitutes.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Isolated essential amino acid requiring grade, dose and diet context', 'High', 'Verify food-grade suitability and the rules for the intended product. A feed, laboratory or pharmaceutical grade and a non-GB listing do not establish permission for general GB food use.', 'L-methionine supplies one essential amino acid used in proteins. It is different from a complete protein food and does not establish a detox, mood or general health treatment.', 'l-methionine|l methionine', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Methionine; Selenomethionine (UIL-0909); L-Lysine (UIL-0401); L-Lysine Hydrochloride (UIL-0427); L-Cysteine (UIL-0760)', 'No universal E-number assigned. L-methionine is not the same ingredient as L-cysteine or selenomethionine.', 'https://www.ajihealthandnutrition.com/product/l-methionine/ | https://lambertshealthcare.co.uk/products/l-methionine-500mg | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('vegetable-juice', 'UIL-0454', 'Vegetable Juice', 'Vegetable juices; mixed vegetable juice; mixed-vegetable juice', 'Water and liquid bases', 'Vegetables', 'Liquid extracted from one or more vegetables, with composition depending on the vegetables, pulp retained and any added ingredients.', 'Vegetable juice supplied fresh, heat-treated, frozen or reconstituted; it may be a single vegetable or a blend.', 'Vegetable flavour, colour, moisture and liquid content in drinks, soups, sauces and prepared foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Mainly water with variable vegetable sugars and micronutrients; it is not nutritionally identical to whole vegetables.', 'Usually a small contribution; exact vegetables, concentration and portion determine the amount.', 'Usually little fat in plain juice; oils or other additions require separate assessment.', 'Naturally occurring juice sugars count as free sugars. Concentration, blending and any added sugar change the amount.', 'Straining removes much of the insoluble fibre; retained pulp varies. Do not equate it with a whole-vegetable fibre portion.', 'Juice carbohydrate and portion matter; an unsweetened or vegetable label does not establish a glucose-lowering effect.', 'No detox or probiotic benefit inferred. Fibre and individual tolerance depend on the vegetables, pulp and processing.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Can contain CELERY or other relevant vegetable allergens; the exact vegetable list is essential. Not every vegetable juice has the same allergen profile.', 'People with relevant vegetable allergies, those monitoring free sugars or salt, and anyone on a prescribed fluid, potassium or other dietary restriction.', 'Vegetable drinks, blended juices, soups, sauces, savoury foods and ingredient mixes.', 'Vegetable Juice; Vegetable juices; mixed vegetable juice; mixed-vegetable juice', 'Whole vegetables provide a different food structure and usually more retained fibre; water is a simpler hydration option where juice flavour/nutrients are not required.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Vegetable liquid requiring source, pulp and sugar context', 'Moderate', 'Declare the actual composition and any regulated allergens. Nutrition and no-added-sugar claims require the finished formulation to meet the relevant conditions.', 'Vegetable juice can supply fluid and vegetable nutrients, but it differs from whole vegetables. Check the exact blend, pulp, sugars, salt and allergens.', 'vegetable juice|vegetable juices|mixed vegetable juice|mixed-vegetable juice', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Vegetable Juice Concentrate (UIL-0480); Fruit-Infused Water (UIL-0428); Tomato Juice; Carrot Juice (UIL-0506); Beetroot Juice (UIL-0532)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.nhs.uk/Live-well/eat-well/how-to-eat-a-balanced-diet/how-to-cut-down-on-sugar-in-your-diet/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('fennel-seed', 'UIL-0455', 'Fennel Seed', 'Fennel seeds; whole fennel seed; ground fennel seed', 'Herbs, spices and seasonings', 'Fennel', 'The dried aromatic fruits commonly called seeds of fennel, used whole or ground as a culinary spice.', 'Dried fennel seed material; variety, cleaning, milling and any seasoning additions vary.', 'Anise-like aroma and savoury or sweet flavour in small culinary amounts.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Primarily flavour at ordinary spice portions; any seed fibre, fat and protein contribution depends on the small amount used.', 'Small contribution at usual seasoning quantities; not a protein substitute.', 'Contains seed constituents, but usual spice portions provide little dietary fat.', 'Some seed carbohydrate; a pure spice is different from a sweetened fennel preparation.', 'Contains plant fibre; the amount contributed depends on the serving.', 'No generic glucose-treatment effect assigned from culinary fennel use.', 'A traditional digestive use does not establish a treatment benefit for this culinary ingredient; concentrated products require a separate assessment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Fennel is not one of the 14 regulated allergens, though individual spice allergy can occur; check blends for added allergens.', 'People with known fennel/spice allergy or sensitivity, and anyone considering concentrated extracts rather than ordinary seasoning.', 'Spice mixes, curries, sausages, bread, fish and vegetable dishes, sauces and some desserts.', 'Fennel Seed; Fennel seeds; whole fennel seed; ground fennel seed', 'No general reason to replace suitable fennel seasoning; another tolerated spice may suit the recipe but will taste different.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Culinary spice requiring portion and individual-allergy context', 'Moderate', 'Use an accurate ingredient description and assess allergens in spice blends. Medicinal or concentrated-product claims require separate evidence and rules.', 'Fennel seed is mainly a flavouring spice at normal culinary amounts. It does not automatically provide a significant nutrient dose or an established gut-treatment effect.', 'fennel seed|fennel seeds|whole fennel seed|ground fennel seed', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Fennel; Aniseed; Celery Seed (UIL-0429); Cumin Seed; Coriander Seed (UIL-0214)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.schwartz.co.uk/products/schwartz-fennel-seeds | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('onion-salt', 'UIL-0456', 'Onion Salt', 'Onion seasoning salt; onion-flavoured salt; onion flavored salt', 'Salt and savoury bases', 'Seasoned salt', 'A seasoning blend of salt and dried onion, with optional anticaking ingredients or other recipe additions.', 'Salt with dried onion powder or pieces; proportions and added ingredients depend on the manufacturer.', 'Saltiness and onion flavour in a convenient dry seasoning.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Mainly sodium-containing salt at usual use levels; dried onion does not remove the sodium contribution.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at ordinary seasoning portions.', 'Usually little fat; some preparations include a small amount of oil.', 'Onion and any added carriers contribute some carbohydrate; the actual seasoning quantity matters.', 'Usually a small contribution from the onion material at seasoning portions.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; onion flavour does not establish a blood-sugar effect.', 'Onion-sensitive individuals may need the actual onion amount and preparation. No generic gut-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Salt and onion are not among the 14 regulated allergens; individual onion allergy and allergens in compound blends require separate assessment.', 'People reducing salt, those with known onion allergy or sensitivity, and anyone following a prescribed diet that limits onion.', 'Seasoning mixes, soups, gravies, sauces, savoury snacks, meat dishes and prepared foods.', 'Onion Salt; Onion seasoning salt; onion-flavoured salt; onion flavored salt', 'Plain onion or onion powder with less added salt where suitable; these still contain onion and are not alternatives for onion allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Salt-based seasoning requiring sodium and recipe context', 'High', 'Check the full ingredient declaration, allergens and any salt/nutrition claims for the actual blend.', 'Onion salt combines onion flavour with salt. It is different from plain onion powder, and the sodium amount still matters.', 'onion salt|onion seasoning salt|onion-flavoured salt|onion flavored salt', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Onion Powder (UIL-0206); Dried Onion; Salt; Garlic Salt (UIL-0404); Celery Salt (UIL-0430)', 'Anticaking agents and small oil additions may be present; no single agent or formula applies to all onion salts.', 'https://www.schwartz.co.uk/products/schwartz-onion-salt | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('vinegar-powder', 'UIL-0457', 'Vinegar Powder', 'Powdered vinegar; dried vinegar; dry vinegar', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Vinegar', 'A dried vinegar preparation, commonly produced with a carbohydrate carrier so that vinegar flavour can be used in a dry ingredient.', 'A specified vinegar, such as spirit, cider or malt vinegar, dried with supplier-specific carriers and processing.', 'Dry acidity and vinegar flavour in seasonings, coatings and prepared foods; preservation performance requires a validated formulation.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Carrier-dependent carbohydrate and organic acids; it is not nutritionally equivalent to the same weight of liquid vinegar.', 'Usually little in simple carbohydrate-carrier grades; assess other carriers and additions.', 'Usually little in a simple powder; blends need their own assessment.', 'Maltodextrin or other starch-based carriers can supply digestible carbohydrate; do not assume sugar-free or carbohydrate-free status.', 'A dried vinegar name does not establish a meaningful fibre or prebiotic contribution.', 'No fixed glucose-response or diabetes-treatment claim assigned; acid content, carrier, dose and food matrix differ from liquid-vinegar preparations.', 'Drying or a vinegar origin does not establish live probiotic organisms or a gut-treatment effect.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Allergens depend on the source vinegar and carrier. Malt-vinegar preparations may contain BARLEY; milk or other carriers must be checked separately.', 'People requiring gluten/allergen information, monitoring carbohydrate intake, or using a powder for a defined acid or preservation function.', 'Salt-and-vinegar seasonings, crisps, snacks, dry coatings, sauces, marinades and foodservice powder blends.', 'Vinegar Powder; Powdered vinegar; dried vinegar; dry vinegar', 'A suitable liquid vinegar where the recipe permits, or a verified carrier/formulation appropriate to the dietary and technical requirement.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Source vinegar, malt/cereal ingredients and carriers determine gluten relevance. Distilled spirit vinegar and malt vinegar must not be treated as the same source.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Dried vinegar preparation requiring source, carrier and acidity context', 'Moderate', 'Declare the actual preparation and any allergens. A vinegar powder does not establish an authorised health claim or a safe preservation level in every recipe.', 'Vinegar powder provides dry vinegar flavour, often with a substantial carrier contribution. Check the vinegar source, carrier and acid strength rather than treating it as dried pure acetic acid.', 'vinegar powder|powdered vinegar|dried vinegar|dry vinegar', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cider Vinegar Powder (UIL-0431); Spirit Vinegar (UIL-0223); Malt Vinegar (UIL-0249); Apple Cider Vinegar (UIL-0275); Maltodextrin (UIL-0001)', 'Carriers, starches and other ingredients vary. Do not assign an acetic-acid additive code or modified-starch E-number without the specified ingredient.', 'https://www.camstar.co.uk/en/products/vinegarpowders | https://www.amtechingredients.com/vinegar-powders | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('peach-puree', 'UIL-0458', 'Peach Puree', 'Peach purée; peach purée preparation; pureed peach; puréed peach', 'Fruit ingredients', 'Peach', 'Peach flesh reduced to a smooth pulp, often sieved and heat-treated. Commercial preparations may include sugar, water, acids or other ingredients.', 'Peaches with product-dependent peeling, pulping, sieving and preservation; plain, concentrated and sweetened preparations differ.', 'Peach flavour, fruit solids, colour, moisture and texture in foods and drinks.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Mainly peach carbohydrate and water, with some retained fruit fibre and variable micronutrients; additions change the profile.', 'Usually a small contribution; not a protein ingredient.', 'Little fat in a plain peach puree; the final recipe may contain fats.', 'Peach sugars contribute carbohydrate and count as free sugars in purée under UK guidance; added sugar or syrup increases the amount.', 'Retains some fruit fibre, depending on peeling and sieving; it differs from strained juice and intact fruit.', 'Portion, sugar content and the complete recipe matter. No fixed glycaemic index or glucose-lowering effect assigned.', 'Some fibre is retained, but individual fruit tolerance and portion matter; no generic gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Peach allergy can occur even though peach is not one of the 14 regulated allergens. Added ingredients and cross-contact require separate checks.', 'People with peach allergy or sensitivity and those monitoring free sugars or the composition of sweetened fruit preparations.', 'Yoghurt, desserts, bakery, smoothies, cocktails, fruit preparations, sauces and baby-food recipes.', 'Peach Puree; Peach purée; peach purée preparation; pureed peach; puréed peach', 'Whole peach where texture permits, or an unsweetened plain preparation when reducing added sugar; this does not remove naturally occurring puree sugars.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Fruit pulp requiring retained-fibre and sugar context', 'High', 'Use the actual ingredient/fruit description and assess added sugars, allergens and nutrition claims. ''No added sugar'' is different from sugar-free.', 'Peach puree keeps some fruit solids but changes the fruit''s structure. Check added sugar and the actual preparation; plain puree is different from juice concentrate or a sweetened cocktail mix.', 'peach puree|peach purée|pureed peach|puréed peach', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Peach Juice Concentrate (UIL-0484); Peach Powder (UIL-0510); Dried Peach (UIL-0536); Fruit Juice Concentrate (UIL-0006)', 'Some preparations contain antioxidants such as ascorbic acid (E300), acids or other additions; none should be assumed universal.', 'https://www.kiril-mischeff.com/product/peach-puree/ | https://www.dirafrost.com/product/fruit-puree/foodservice/peach-puree/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cassava-flour', 'UIL-0459', 'Cassava Flour', 'Cassava root flour; yuca flour; manioc flour', 'Vegetable ingredients', 'Cassava root', 'Flour made from appropriately processed, dried and milled cassava root. It is different from isolated cassava/tapioca starch.', 'Cassava roots processed for food use; variety, detoxification, fermentation, drying and milling affect the final preparation.', 'Starch-rich flour for baking, flatbreads, coatings, thickening and other food preparations.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Mainly carbohydrate as starch, with some root material and variable fibre; not a concentrated protein or complete-grain substitute.', 'Usually low in protein compared with many grain or pulse flours; it is not a protein replacement.', 'Little fat in a plain root flour; added oils in recipes change the contribution.', 'Starch-rich; grain-free or gluten-free does not mean low carbohydrate or a guaranteed lower glucose response.', 'Can retain more root material than isolated tapioca starch; amount depends on processing and cannot be assumed high.', 'Available carbohydrate, preparation, portion and the meal determine the response; no universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No generic gut-treatment claim assigned. Cyanogenic-compound control is a food-safety issue, separate from food allergy.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Cassava is not one of the 14 regulated allergens; individual allergy, blends and cross-contact need their own assessment.', 'Anyone choosing or preparing cassava flour should use a verified food-grade product made with appropriate processing and follow its preparation instructions.', 'Gluten-free bakery, flatbreads, tortillas, coatings, pancakes and cassava-based foods.', 'Cassava Flour; Cassava root flour; yuca flour; manioc flour', 'Another appropriately prepared flour matched to the recipe and dietary requirements; no general reason to reject properly processed food-grade cassava flour.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Starch-rich root flour requiring verified processing and preparation', 'High', 'Food safety depends on the verified cassava preparation and control of cyanogenic compounds. FSANZ guidance supports the hazard assessment; its local labelling rules are not stated as GB law.', 'Cassava flour is a carbohydrate-rich root flour rather than isolated tapioca starch. Use properly processed food-grade flour and follow its preparation instructions; the name alone does not prove safe processing.', 'cassava flour|cassava root flour|yuca flour|manioc flour', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cassava (UIL-0433); Cassava Starch (UIL-0539); Tapioca starch (UIL-0032); Tapioca Pearls (UIL-0485)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.ottosnaturals.com/ | https://www.foodstandards.gov.au/consumer/prevention-of-foodborne-illness/cassava | https://www.foodstandards.gov.au/sites/default/files/publications/Documents/28_Cyanogenic_glycosides.pdf | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('wheat-malt', 'UIL-0460', 'Wheat Malt', 'Malted wheat; wheat malt grain; malted wheat grain', 'Cereal and grain derivatives', 'Wheat', 'Wheat grain germinated under controlled conditions and dried during malting. It may be supplied whole or milled, with enzyme activity depending on the grade.', 'Wheat processed by steeping, germination and drying/kilning; whole grain, flour, flakes and extracts are different preparations.', 'Malty flavour, colour, cereal solids and, in appropriate grades, enzymes for brewing or food manufacture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly cereal carbohydrate with wheat protein and variable grain fibre; milling, mashing or extraction changes the composition.', 'Contains wheat protein, including gluten. Its role is not equivalent to an isolated wheat-protein ingredient.', 'Usually a modest contribution from grain; assess grade and recipe.', 'Contains starch and some sugars. Malting and subsequent processing can convert starch to fermentable sugars; it is not identical to a malt syrup.', 'Grain fibre contribution depends on the retained material and milling; an extract or syrup has a different profile.', 'No generic glucose-lowering effect assigned; grade, starch conversion, use level and finished product matter.', 'Wheat gluten remains relevant. Malting does not establish suitability for coeliac disease or a generic digestive benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains WHEAT, a regulated allergen. Barley or other cereals can be present in blends or through relevant cross-contact.', 'People with wheat allergy or coeliac disease, and anyone needing to distinguish whole malt from an extract, flour or syrup.', 'Wheat beers, brewing grists, malted bakery and cereal preparations, and specified food-manufacturing ingredients.', 'Wheat Malt; Malted wheat; wheat malt grain; malted wheat grain', 'A verified gluten-free or wheat-free ingredient matched to the technical need; another malt is not automatically suitable for coeliac disease.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'Contains wheat gluten; germination/malting does not make wheat gluten-free.', 'Context dependent', 'Malted cereal requiring wheat, gluten and preparation context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise wheat as appropriate to the product. The cereal source must be clear; generic ''malt'' must not be assumed to mean barley or wheat without evidence.', 'Wheat malt is germinated and dried wheat used for flavour and manufacturing functions. It still contains wheat/gluten and is different from malt extract, syrup or a finished beer.', 'wheat malt|malted wheat|wheat malt grain|malted wheat grain', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Malted Wheat Flour (UIL-0486); Malted Wheat Flakes (UIL-0631); Malted Barley (UIL-0564); Barley malt extract (UIL-0026); Barley Malt Flour (UIL-0512)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://crispmalt.com/malts/wheat-malt/ | https://crispmalt.com/making-malt/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('sago-starch', 'UIL-0461', 'Sago Starch', 'Palm sago starch; sago palm starch; Metroxylon sago starch', 'Starches and carbohydrate ingredients', 'Palm starch', 'Food-grade starch extracted from the pith of sago palms, principally Metroxylon species. Some products called sago are made from tapioca, so confirm the botanical source.', 'Palm stem pith is processed with water to separate starch, which is recovered and dried. Tapioca-based sago comes from cassava roots instead.', 'Thickening, gelling and providing starch solids in foods.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Mainly starch; not nutritionally equivalent to whole plant tissue.', 'Usually little protein in purified starch.', 'Usually little fat.', 'Predominantly starch; cooking, portion and recipe affect its digestion.', 'Usually little fibre; do not assume it is resistant starch.', 'No universal glycaemic index or glucose-lowering effect assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned to generic sago starch.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in plain palm starch; assess actual source and blends.', 'Anyone distinguishing palm sago from tapioca, or assessing a blended starch preparation.', 'Puddings, sago pearls, desserts, thickened sauces and regional starch-based foods.', 'Sago Starch; Palm sago starch; sago palm starch; Metroxylon sago starch', 'Tapioca, potato or maize starch matched to the required texture; they have separate source identities.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Purified plant starch requiring botanical-source context', 'Moderate', 'Identify the actual starch source accurately. The word sago does not establish chemical modification, an E-number or a resistant-starch claim.', 'Sago starch is mainly carbohydrate used for texture. Confirm whether a product is palm starch or tapioca-based sago before assigning its source.', 'sago starch|palm sago starch|sago palm starch|metroxylon sago starch', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Tapioca starch (UIL-0032); Cassava Starch (UIL-0539); Potato starch (UIL-0031); Maize Starch (UIL-0008); Resistant starch (UIL-0034)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.fao.org/4/x5045e/x5045E08.HTM | https://ecocrop.apps.fao.org/ecocrop/srv/en/cropView?id=1466 | https://www.ctcri.org/public/publications/2025-05/tf-15_detailed-manufacturing-process-of.pdf', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('molasses', 'UIL-0462', 'Molasses', 'Molasses syrup; cane molasses; blackstrap molasses', 'Sugars, syrups and sweetening ingredients', 'Sugar-production syrup', 'A dark syrup remaining during sugar manufacture. Source and extraction stage distinguish grades, including cane blackstrap molasses.', 'Sugar-processing streams, commonly from sugar cane; verify cane/beet origin and the supplied grade.', 'Sweetness, dark colour, characteristic flavour and moisture.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'A sugar-containing syrup with variable mineral content; dark colour does not prove a meaningful iron contribution per serving.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at typical use levels.', 'Usually little fat in plain syrup.', 'Contains free sugars; quantities depend on grade and use level.', 'Not equivalent to a fibre-rich whole plant food.', 'Treat its sugars as part of the finished food''s carbohydrate; no diabetes-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in plain molasses. Supplier precautionary warnings and added ingredients are product-specific.', 'People monitoring free sugars, and anyone distinguishing blackstrap, sulphured or blended syrups.', 'Baking, gingerbread, sauces, marinades, confectionery and dark syrup blends.', 'Molasses; Molasses syrup; cane molasses; blackstrap molasses', 'A different syrup or a lower-sugar recipe where appropriate; replacing one sugar syrup does not automatically reduce free sugars.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Sugar-containing culinary syrup with grade-dependent minerals', 'Moderate', 'Use an accurate ingredient description. Nutrition and mineral claims require the actual product composition; molasses is not automatically a caramel-colour additive.', 'Molasses adds sweetness and dark flavour. Mineral levels vary, and it remains a source of free sugars.', 'molasses|molasses syrup|cane molasses|blackstrap molasses', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cane Sugar (UIL-0228); Beet Sugar (UIL-0254); Brown Sugar (UIL-0358); Golden syrup (UIL-0024)', 'Unsulphured and sulphured grades differ. Assess sulphites and any additives from the actual specification; do not assign E150 from the dark colour.', 'https://shop.meridianfoods.co.uk/collections/all-products/products/meridian-org-blackstrap-molasses-350-g | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses?c=Linux', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('yellow-pea-flour', 'UIL-0463', 'Yellow Pea Flour', 'Yellow pea flour; split yellow pea flour; yellow split pea flour', 'Legumes and pulse derivatives', 'Pea flour', 'Flour milled from dried yellow peas, including split or dehulled grades. It retains a broader mix of pea components than isolated pea protein or starch.', 'Dried yellow peas; dehulling and milling influence the composition.', 'Pulse flavour, flour solids, thickening and protein contribution.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Supplies starch, plant protein and fibre in amounts that depend on the milling grade.', 'Contains pea protein; not a protein isolate.', 'Usually relatively low in fat compared with nut flours.', 'Contains substantial starch; it is not carbohydrate-free.', 'Contributes pulse fibre; dehulling changes the amount.', 'No fixed glycaemic index or glucose-treatment effect assigned to the flour.', 'Pulse components can affect individual digestive tolerance; no general prebiotic or treatment claim assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pea allergy is possible although pea is outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Allergy to one legume does not establish allergy to all legumes.', 'People with pea allergy or individual pulse intolerance; coeliac suitability also requires control of cross-contact.', 'Pulse baking, pancakes, batters, sauces, snacks and plant-based recipes.', 'Yellow Pea Flour; Yellow pea flour; split yellow pea flour; yellow split pea flour', 'Another tolerated flour matched to recipe needs; allergy and gluten suitability require separate checks.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Milled pulse ingredient retaining starch and protein', 'High', 'Describe the pulse accurately. A supplier''s gluten-free result supports that product, not every yellow pea flour.', 'Yellow pea flour provides pulse protein, starch and fibre. It differs from pea starch and isolated pea protein.', 'yellow pea flour|split yellow pea flour|yellow split pea flour', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pea Flour (UIL-0437); Pea Starch (UIL-0383); Pea Protein Isolate (UIL-0016); Pea Protein Concentrate (UIL-0489)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://hodmedods.co.uk/products/yellow-pea-flour | https://allergynorthwest.nhs.uk/home-patient/managing-allergies/patient-leaflets/legume-allergy-2/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('walnut-meal', 'UIL-0464', 'Walnut Meal', 'Ground walnuts; walnut flour; ground walnut meal', 'Nut and seed derivatives', 'Walnut kernel', 'Ground walnut material used as meal or flour. It may be ground whole kernels or material with some oil removed.', 'Walnut kernels; grinding and any oil extraction determine the grade.', 'Nut flavour, texture and solids in baking and other foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Whole-kernel meal retains substantial walnut fat; partly defatted meal has a different protein, fat and fibre balance.', 'Contains walnut protein; concentration depends on oil removal.', 'Whole-kernel meal is fat-rich, with predominantly unsaturated fats; defatted grades contain less.', 'Not equivalent to cereal starch; exact carbohydrate content varies.', 'Contains walnut fibre, with concentration depending on grade.', 'No generic glucose-lowering effect assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned to walnut meal.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains WALNUT, a regulated tree-nut allergen. Grinding or removing some oil does not remove walnut-allergen relevance.', 'People with walnut allergy and anyone comparing whole-kernel and partly defatted meals.', 'Cakes, biscuits, pastry, fillings, bread and nut-based foods.', 'Walnut Meal; Ground walnuts; walnut flour; ground walnut meal', 'A tolerated nut-free or seed-based recipe where suitable; another tree nut is not automatically appropriate for nut allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Ground tree-nut ingredient with variable defatting', 'Moderate', 'Declare and emphasise walnut. The term meal or flour alone does not specify the fat content.', 'Walnut meal adds walnut flavour and nutrients, but its composition changes when oil is removed. It remains a walnut allergen.', 'walnut meal|walnut flour|ground walnut meal|ground walnuts', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Walnuts (UIL-0143); Walnut Oil (UIL-0050); Walnut Paste (UIL-0490); Almond Meal (UIL-0230)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://naturalchoice.co.uk/products/walnut-meal-flour | https://www.stoll-walnussprodukte.com/en/walnut-flours/ | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses?c=Linux', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('almond-oil', 'UIL-0465', 'Almond Oil', 'Edible almond oil; sweet almond oil; food-grade almond oil', 'Oils and fats', 'Almond-derived oil', 'Edible oil obtained from sweet almonds. Culinary grades differ from cosmetic oils and bitter-almond flavouring or essential-oil products.', 'Sweet almond kernels; extraction, roasting and refining vary by grade.', 'Culinary fat, almond flavour where retained, and a carrier in suitable food preparations.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'A concentrated fat and energy source; it does not retain the protein and fibre profile of whole almonds.', 'Not a meaningful protein source; residual allergenic protein depends on processing.', 'Predominantly unsaturated fat in typical edible almond oils; do not assign a universal fatty-acid percentage.', 'Little carbohydrate in plain oil.', 'None in plain oil.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Almond-derived: retain ALMOND allergen information. Do not assume a blanket allergen exemption for refined almond oil.', 'People with almond allergy; anyone checking whether the supplied oil is food-grade and suitable for the intended cooking method.', 'Dressings, finishing oils, bakery, confectionery and culinary oil blends.', 'Almond Oil; Edible almond oil; sweet almond oil; food-grade almond oil', 'A tolerated food-grade oil matched to cooking needs; another nut oil is not automatically suitable for almond allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Culinary nut oil requiring allergen and grade context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise almond as required. The refined-soya-oil exemption must not be transferred to almond oil.', 'Almond oil is a culinary fat rather than a substitute for whole-almond protein or fibre. Check food grade and almond-allergen information.', 'almond oil|edible almond oil|sweet almond oil|food-grade almond oil', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Almonds (UIL-0142); Almond Meal (UIL-0230); Almond Flour (UIL-0098); Almond Extract (UIL-0525)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.latourangelle.fr/en/oils-of-dried-fruits/3023-huile-amande-3245270000559.html | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('single-cream', 'UIL-0466', 'Single Cream', 'Dairy single cream; single dairy cream', 'Dairy ingredients', 'Dairy cream', 'A dairy cream with less milk fat than standard double cream. The Dairy UK/PTF industry code specifies at least 18% milk fat for non-sterilised single cream.', 'The milk-fat-rich fraction of dairy milk; heat treatment and formulation depend on the product.', 'Creaminess, richness and dairy flavour in foods.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Provides milk fat, including saturated fat, with some milk protein and lactose; assess the serving and formulation.', 'Contains milk protein; not a concentrated protein ingredient.', 'Fat-rich, though less concentrated than standard double cream. The industry-code fat standard is not a recommended serving.', 'Contains lactose unless specifically reduced; sweetened preparations differ.', 'None inherent in plain dairy cream.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; consider lactose and added sugars in the finished food.', 'Lactose tolerance varies. Lactose-free dairy cream still requires milk-allergen assessment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MILK, a regulated allergen. Heat treatment does not make ordinary cream suitable for milk allergy.', 'People with milk allergy or lactose intolerance; also assess saturated fat and portion in the overall diet.', 'Sauces, soups, desserts, pouring cream and dairy-based recipes.', 'Single Cream; Dairy single cream; single dairy cream', 'A suitable milk-free culinary preparation for milk allergy; check its own allergens and recipe performance.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Dairy cream with milk-allergen and industry-standard context', 'High', 'The Dairy UK/PTF code retains customary cream fat standards; the former statutory limits were revoked in December 2018. Milk-allergen and general food-information requirements still apply.', 'Single cream adds dairy richness and contains milk. Its customary fat standard comes from an industry code, and the actual product specification remains relevant.', 'single cream|dairy single cream|single dairy cream', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cream (UIL-0414); Double Cream (UIL-0440); Whipping Cream (UIL-0492); Cream Powder (UIL-0570)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.dairyuk.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/FINAL-Compositional-Standards-Cream.pdf | https://www.provtrade.co.uk/technical-and-legislation/labelling-and-standards.aspx | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/milk-and-dairy-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('salted-egg-yolk', 'UIL-0467', 'Salted Egg Yolk', 'Salted egg yolks; salted liquid egg yolk; salted liquid egg yolks', 'Egg ingredients', 'Egg yolk preparation', 'Egg yolk prepared with salt. The name can describe salted liquid yolk or cured and dried yolk preparations with different specifications.', 'Egg yolks, from hens or other specified birds, combined or treated with salt.', 'Emulsification, richness, colour and a salty egg-yolk flavour.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Contains yolk fat and protein plus added salt; water content and salt level vary substantially.', 'Contains egg protein.', 'Contains yolk fat, phospholipids and cholesterol; amounts depend on the preparation.', 'Usually little inherent carbohydrate; added sugars or other ingredients change the profile.', 'None inherent in egg yolk and salt.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains EGG, a regulated allergen. Salting does not remove egg-allergen relevance.', 'People with egg allergy, those monitoring salt intake, and anyone preparing uncooked foods.', 'Mayonnaise, sauces, bakery, salted-yolk fillings, toppings and savoury snacks.', 'Salted Egg Yolk; Salted egg yolks; salted liquid egg yolk; salted liquid egg yolks', 'A suitable egg-free recipe for egg allergy; unsalted yolk can change both salt balance and processing requirements.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Salted egg preparation requiring grade and handling context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise egg. Salting alone does not establish pasteurisation, shelf stability or suitability for raw consumption; follow the supplied product''s handling instructions.', 'Salted egg yolk adds egg-yolk functionality and salt. Confirm whether it is liquid, cured or dried, and retain egg-allergen information.', 'salted egg yolk|salted egg yolks|salted liquid egg yolk|salted liquid egg yolks', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Egg Yolk (UIL-0415); Liquid Egg Yolk (UIL-0441); Egg Yolk Powder (UIL-0072); Sugared Egg Yolk (UIL-0493)', 'Salt is part of this preparation. Preservatives or other additions vary by grade; no additive code is inherent in the name.', 'https://www.bouwhuis-enthoven.com/our-products-and-solutions/emulsification/salted-liquid-egg-yolk/ | https://www.incredibleegg.org/professionals/manufacturers/technical-resources/egg-products-and-specifications/egg-yolk-types/ | https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-on-safe-storage-handling-and-use-of-eggs-for-catering | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('pork-protein', 'UIL-0468', 'Pork Protein', 'Porcine protein; pork-derived protein', 'Meat and poultry ingredients', 'Porcine protein ingredient', 'A protein ingredient derived from pigs. Grades can come from muscle, collagen-rich tissues or blood components and need different nutritional descriptions.', 'Porcine tissues or blood fractions processed to produce functional protein; extraction and hydrolysis vary.', 'Protein addition, water binding, emulsification, gel formation and texture.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Provides porcine protein, but amino-acid balance and other nutrients depend on the actual fraction and processing.', 'May be muscle, collagen, plasma or another fraction. Do not assume every grade has the amino-acid profile of lean pork.', 'Variable residual fat; not automatically the fat profile of whole pork.', 'Usually limited in a pure protein fraction; carriers and blends can contribute carbohydrate.', 'None inherent in the animal protein.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Hydrolysis or animal origin alone does not establish improved tolerance or a gut-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pork is outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens, but individual meat allergy is possible. Assess added ingredients and relevant cross-contact.', 'People avoiding porcine ingredients for dietary or religious reasons, people with relevant meat allergy, and formulators comparing muscle and collagen grades.', 'Processed meat, sausages, meat preparations and specified functional protein blends.', 'Pork Protein; Porcine protein; pork-derived protein', 'A suitable non-porcine protein matched to the technical and dietary need; amino-acid quality and allergens may differ.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Animal protein fraction requiring tissue and processing context', 'Moderate', 'Identify the animal source accurately. The broad name does not establish a particular protein-quality claim, tissue fraction or hydrolysis method.', 'Pork protein is a broad family of porcine functional ingredients. The specification is needed to distinguish muscle, collagen and blood-derived proteins.', 'pork protein|porcine protein|pork-derived protein', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pork (UIL-0416); Pork Mince (UIL-0442); Pork Gelatine (UIL-0520); Collagen Peptides (UIL-0075)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.vepro.biz/products-pork/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/ExerciseAndAthleticPerformance-HealthProfessional/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('alaska-pollock', 'UIL-0469', 'Alaska Pollock', 'Alaska pollack; walleye pollock; Pacific pollock; Pacific pollack; Gadus chalcogrammus; Theragra chalcogramma', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'White fish', 'A North Pacific white-fish species, Gadus chalcogrammus, historically named Theragra chalcogramma. It differs from Pollachius pollachius, also sold as pollock or pollack.', 'Fish of the specified species; catch area, fishery and product form need separate confirmation.', 'White-fish protein, flesh and texture in seafood products.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Plain flesh provides protein and is relatively low in fat; coatings, surimi recipes and added ingredients change the profile.', 'Provides fish protein.', 'Plain flesh is low-fat white fish; do not assign the omega-3 profile of an oily fish.', 'Little inherent carbohydrate in plain fish; coatings and binders can add substantial starch.', 'None in plain fish.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains FISH, a regulated allergen. Processing does not establish suitability for fish allergy.', 'People with fish allergy and anyone checking the species, catch origin or a formulated seafood recipe.', 'Fish fillets, fish fingers, coated fish, surimi and seafood preparations.', 'Alaska Pollock; Alaska pollack; walleye pollock; Pacific pollock; Pacific pollack; Gadus chalcogrammus; Theragra chalcogramma', 'Another tolerated fish or a suitable fish-free recipe; another fish species is not automatically safe for fish allergy.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'White-fish species requiring exact species and product matching', 'High', 'Use the appropriate commercial and scientific designation and any origin information required for the product. Alaska in the species name does not itself prove an Alaskan catch.', 'Alaska pollock is a lean white fish and a fish allergen. Match the full species name and assess coatings or surimi ingredients separately.', 'alaska pollock|alaska pollack|walleye pollock|pacific pollock|pacific pollack|gadus chalcogrammus|theragra chalcogramma', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pollock (UIL-0443)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/alaska-pollock | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/commercial-designations-of-fish-united-kingdom/commercial-designations-of-fish | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/fish-and-shellfish-nutrition/ | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses?c=Linux', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('hydrolysed-wheat-protein', 'UIL-0470', 'Hydrolysed Wheat Protein', 'Hydrolyzed wheat protein; wheat protein hydrolysate; hydrolysed wheat proteins; hydrolyzed wheat proteins', 'Plant proteins and meat alternatives', 'Wheat protein hydrolysate', 'Wheat protein broken into smaller peptides and amino acids by controlled hydrolysis. The extent and method vary by food-grade product.', 'Wheat-derived protein treated enzymatically or by another specified hydrolysis process.', 'Protein contribution, solubility, flavour and other formulation functions depending on the grade.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'A wheat-protein-derived ingredient; amino-acid balance, peptide sizes and sodium depend on the specification.', 'Provides wheat-derived amino acids and peptides; not identical to intact wheat protein isolate.', 'Usually little fat in a purified grade; check carriers.', 'Residual carbohydrate and carriers vary.', 'Not inherently a meaningful fibre source.', 'No generic glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Hydrolysis does not by itself prove easier digestion, hypoallergenicity or coeliac suitability.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'WHEAT-derived and subject to relevant wheat-allergen declaration. Do not infer that hydrolysis removes allergen risk.', 'People with wheat allergy or coeliac disease, and anyone comparing food-grade hydrolysates with cosmetic products.', 'Protein drinks, bars, savoury preparations and specified food-manufacturing blends.', 'Hydrolysed Wheat Protein; Hydrolyzed wheat protein; wheat protein hydrolysate; hydrolysed wheat proteins; hydrolyzed wheat proteins', 'A verified suitable non-wheat protein matched to the recipe; alternative proteins bring their own allergen considerations.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'Wheat-derived; hydrolysis does not itself establish gluten-free suitability. Require product-specific evidence and compliant labelling.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Hydrolysed cereal protein requiring wheat and grade context', 'Moderate', 'The allergen exemptions for certain wheat glucose syrups or maltodextrins must not be transferred to wheat protein hydrolysates. Any gluten-free claim needs specific compliance evidence.', 'Hydrolysed wheat protein supplies wheat-derived peptides for food formulation. It is not automatically gluten-free or suitable for wheat allergy.', 'hydrolysed wheat protein|hydrolyzed wheat protein|wheat protein hydrolysate|hydrolysed wheat proteins|hydrolyzed wheat proteins', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Wheat Protein (UIL-0356); Wheat Protein Isolate (UIL-0444); Hydrolysed Pea Protein (UIL-0496)', 'No fixed MSG content or E621 identity follows from hydrolysis. Assess salts, carriers and other declared ingredients.', 'https://www.mgpingredients.com/more-information/news-press/news-releases/mgp-ingredients-introduces-optein-new-wheat-protein | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/ExerciseAndAthleticPerformance-HealthProfessional/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cocoa-fibre', 'UIL-0471', 'Cocoa Fibre', 'Cocoa fiber; cocoa shell fibre; cocoa shell fiber', 'Fibres and prebiotic ingredients', 'Cocoa shell fibre ingredient', 'A food-grade fibre ingredient commonly made from cleaned, processed cocoa bean shells. It differs from cocoa powder made from the bean material.', 'Selected cocoa bean shells, processed and milled to the supplier''s food-grade specification.', 'Fibre enrichment, water binding, colour, cocoa notes and texture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'A concentrated fibre ingredient with grade-dependent residual protein, fat and carbohydrate.', 'May contain residual protein; not a standard protein isolate.', 'Variable residual cocoa fat; not equivalent to cocoa butter.', 'Digestible carbohydrate depends on grade; fibre content must come from the specification.', 'Typically fibre-rich, but do not assign one supplier''s percentage to all cocoa fibre.', 'No established glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Fibre can affect stool characteristics and tolerance; the generic name does not establish a prebiotic or gut-treatment claim.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Cocoa allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Milk, soya and other allergens depend on formulation and relevant cross-contact.', 'People with cocoa allergy or sensitivity to concentrated fibre, and formulators needing to distinguish shell fibre from cocoa powder.', 'Fibre-enriched bakery, biscuits, snacks and cocoa-flavoured formulations.', 'Cocoa Fibre; Cocoa fiber; cocoa shell fibre; cocoa shell fiber', 'Another fibre matched to texture and tolerance; cocoa powder has a different composition and technical role.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Processed cocoa-shell fibre requiring food-grade and composition context', 'Moderate', 'Use the correct ingredient description. Cocoa shell fibre is not automatically cocoa powder or countable cocoa solids under chocolate composition standards.', 'Cocoa fibre adds fibre, texture and cocoa-like colour or flavour. Its shell-based origin and specification distinguish it from cocoa powder.', 'cocoa fibre|cocoa fiber|cocoa shell fibre|cocoa shell fiber', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cocoa Shell Powder (UIL-0368); Cocoa Powder (UIL-0181); Cocoa Solids (UIL-0184); Cocoa Extract (UIL-0342)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://interfiber.com/en/products/cocoa-fiber | https://greenfield.eu.com/cocoa-fibre/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('chocolate-crumb', 'UIL-0472', 'Chocolate Crumb', 'Chocolate manufacturing crumb; chocolate crumb powder', 'Cocoa, coffee and tea derivatives', 'Compound chocolate-manufacturing ingredient', 'In chocolate manufacture, a dried compound commonly produced from milk, sugar and cocoa liquor. The same wording can be used loosely for crumbled chocolate or baked toppings, which need recipe confirmation.', 'For the industrial baseline, milk, sugar and cocoa liquor are cooked under vacuum, dried and milled.', 'Chocolate flavour, dairy notes and solids in chocolate production.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Sugar, milk solids and cocoa-derived components contribute nutrients in recipe-dependent proportions.', 'Milk-based grades supply milk protein; other recipes differ.', 'Milk and cocoa can contribute fat, including saturated fat; amounts vary.', 'Typically contains added sugar; baked crumb variants may also contain cereal starch.', 'Depends on cocoa and any other ingredients; no generic fibre claim.', 'Assess actual sugars, starch and portion in the finished food; no glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned; lactose may be relevant in milk-based grades.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The conventional milk-chocolate manufacturing grade contains MILK. Ambiguous topping or baked-crumb uses require the actual recipe; wheat, egg, soya or nuts may be present.', 'People with milk or other relevant food allergies, and anyone determining whether the term means industrial crumb or a baked topping.', 'Milk-chocolate manufacture, chocolate-flavoured products and, under looser usage, dessert toppings.', 'Chocolate Crumb; Chocolate manufacturing crumb; chocolate crumb powder', 'A specified milk-free or allergen-appropriate chocolate ingredient; substitution must match the manufacturing function.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'The milk/sugar/cocoa manufacturing baseline has no inherent gluten, but baked variants and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Compound ingredient with an industrial baseline and ambiguous culinary usage', 'Moderate', 'Compound-ingredient and allergen requirements depend on the actual recipe. Do not interpret every crumb as wheat-based or every chocolate term as milk-free.', 'Chocolate crumb usually refers here to a milk, sugar and cocoa manufacturing intermediate. Confirm the recipe before assigning allergens or dietary suitability.', 'chocolate crumb|chocolate manufacturing crumb|chocolate crumb powder', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Milk Chocolate Crumb (UIL-0498); Cocoa Mass (UIL-0182); Biscuit Crumb (UIL-0397); Cake Crumb (UIL-0449)', 'Emulsifiers, flavourings and other additives depend on the recipe; no additive is established by crumb alone.', 'https://meadowfoods.co.uk/products/meadow-confectionery/ | https://www.delica.com/media/wnvdoofr/enflyerchocoblondcrumbhighres.pdf | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses?c=Linux | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('peppermint-extract', 'UIL-0473', 'Peppermint Extract', 'Peppermint flavour extract; peppermint flavor extract; pure peppermint extract', 'Flavouring food ingredients', 'Botanical flavour extract', 'A concentrated culinary peppermint flavour preparation, often made with peppermint oil and an alcohol carrier.', 'Peppermint-derived flavour components with product-specific carriers; alcohol, water and other ingredients vary.', 'Mint flavour in small quantities.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Used primarily for flavour; carrier and dose determine any sugar, alcohol or energy contribution.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at flavouring levels.', 'May contain peppermint oil, but is not a meaningful dietary-fat serving.', 'Sugar or syrup carriers may contribute carbohydrate; check the product.', 'Not equivalent to peppermint leaf fibre.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Culinary extract is not equivalent to studied medicinal peppermint-oil preparations; no IBS or digestive-treatment claim assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Peppermint allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check carriers and the complete preparation.', 'People with peppermint allergy or carrier restrictions, including those avoiding alcohol.', 'Confectionery, chocolate, baking, desserts and flavoured drinks.', 'Peppermint Extract; Peppermint flavour extract; peppermint flavor extract; pure peppermint extract', 'Another appropriate flavour preparation or peppermint leaf where the recipe permits; strengths and carriers differ.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Concentrated flavour preparation requiring carrier and dose context', 'Moderate', 'Use an accurate flavouring description and assess any claims for the actual food. A culinary extract does not establish a medicinal dose or indication.', 'Peppermint extract adds concentrated mint flavour. Check carriers and distinguish culinary use from medicinal peppermint-oil products.', 'peppermint extract|peppermint flavour extract|peppermint flavor extract|pure peppermint extract', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Mint Extract (UIL-0499); Peppermint Leaf (UIL-0662); Orange Extract (UIL-0421); Lime Extract (UIL-0447)', 'Carriers and any preservatives or emulsifiers are preparation-specific; no E-number follows from the word extract.', 'https://nielsenmassey.com/products/pure-peppermint-extract-2/ | https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/peppermint-oil/about-peppermint-oil/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('horseradish-sauce', 'UIL-0474', 'Horseradish Sauce', 'Prepared horseradish sauce; creamy horseradish sauce', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Compound horseradish condiment', 'A prepared condiment containing horseradish with other ingredients such as vinegar, oil, water or cream. Recipes differ substantially.', 'Horseradish root combined with the specified sauce ingredients.', 'Pungent flavour, acidity and a creamy or spoonable condiment texture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Fat, sugar, salt and other nutrients depend on the recipe; it is not nutritionally equivalent to plain root.', 'Usually limited at condiment portions; egg or dairy ingredients may contribute.', 'Oil or cream can make a substantial contribution; the fat profile varies.', 'Added sugars and starches depend on formulation.', 'Some root fibre may remain, but portions and root percentage vary.', 'Assess added sugar and the finished recipe; no glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Pungency does not establish a digestive, antimicrobial or gut-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Recipe-dependent: may contain EGG, MUSTARD, MILK or sulphites. Horseradish root itself must not automatically be labelled as the regulated mustard allergen.', 'People with relevant allergies or sulphite sensitivity; check the full ingredient list for each brand.', 'Condiments, roast accompaniments, sandwiches, dressings and prepared meals.', 'Horseradish Sauce; Prepared horseradish sauce; creamy horseradish sauce', 'A suitable allergen-appropriate sauce or a recipe using plain horseradish; root and prepared sauce are not interchangeable specifications.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No universal gluten status; assess thickeners, flavourings, other recipe ingredients and cross-contact.', 'Context dependent', 'Compound condiment requiring recipe-specific allergen assessment', 'Moderate', 'Apply compound-ingredient and allergen rules to the actual recipe. Sulphite declaration depends on the applicable concentration conditions.', 'Horseradish sauce is a variable compound condiment. Egg, mustard, dairy and sulphites require product-specific checking.', 'horseradish sauce|prepared horseradish sauce|creamy horseradish sauce', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Horseradish Paste (UIL-0500); Salad Cream (UIL-0344)', 'Some recipes contain xanthan gum, preservatives or other additives; the cited Colman''s example includes xanthan gum and sodium metabisulphite, not a universal formula.', 'https://www.colmans.co.uk/p/horseradish-sauce.html/08714100536209 | https://www.tracklements.co.uk/product/strong-horseradish-cream/ | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses?c=Linux', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('cracker-crumb', 'UIL-0475', 'Cracker Crumb', 'Cracker crumbs; crushed crackers; ground crackers', 'Bakery and cereal bases', 'Ground baked-cracker ingredient', 'Crackers crushed or milled into crumbs for coating, binding or bases. The original cracker recipe determines the resulting ingredient.', 'Baked crackers made from the specified flour, fats, salt, raising agents and other ingredients, then ground.', 'Crunch, coating, binding and a crumb structure.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually supplies cereal carbohydrate, with fat, salt, sugar and fibre depending on the cracker.', 'Depends mainly on the flour and other recipe ingredients; not a protein isolate.', 'Added oil or fat varies by cracker recipe.', 'Commonly starch-rich; sweet cracker variants also contain sugars.', 'Wholegrain content and flour refinement determine the fibre contribution.', 'Assess starch, sugars and portion in the finished food; no universal glycaemic index assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned; gluten and individual tolerance depend on the recipe.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Common wheat-cracker grades contain WHEAT. Other cereals, milk, egg, soya, sesame or other allergens are recipe-dependent.', 'People with wheat allergy or coeliac disease and anyone needing the original cracker specification.', 'Coatings, meat or vegetable binders, pie bases, toppings and prepared foods.', 'Cracker Crumb; Cracker crumbs; crushed crackers; ground crackers', 'A verified suitable gluten-free or allergen-appropriate crumb matched to texture; another baked crumb is not automatically suitable.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Common wheat-based grades contain gluten; gluten-free variants need their own verified specification.', 'Context dependent', 'Baked compound crumb requiring original-recipe context', 'Moderate', 'Retain the constituent ingredients and required allergen information. Cracker crumb is not interchangeable with raw flour or an unspecified breadcrumb.', 'Cracker crumb inherits the nutrients and allergens of its crackers. Check the actual flour, fats, sugars and other ingredients.', 'cracker crumb|cracker crumbs|crushed crackers|ground crackers', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Breadcrumbs (UIL-0241); Biscuit Crumb (UIL-0397); Wheat Crumbs (UIL-0304); Panko Breadcrumbs (UIL-0319)', 'Raising agents, emulsifiers or other additives may carry through from the cracker; identify them from the actual recipe.', 'https://rovirabiscuits.com/crakr-crums/original/ | https://www.mondelezawayfromhome.com/Product/ProductDetails/ProductId%3D10019320008266/index.html | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses?c=Linux', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('lactobacillus-plantarum', 'UIL-0476', 'Lactobacillus Plantarum', 'Lactiplantibacillus plantarum; L. plantarum', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Lactic-acid bacterial culture', 'A bacterial species now named Lactiplantibacillus plantarum, formerly Lactobacillus plantarum. Effects and technical properties depend on the strain and preparation.', 'Cultured bacteria supplied as live, dried or otherwise prepared cultures with specified carriers.', 'Fermentation and, in specified products, addition as a named bacterial culture.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Typically added for culture function rather than a meaningful macronutrient contribution; carriers may differ.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at usual culture-use levels.', 'Carrier-dependent; no fixed fat profile.', 'Carriers or fermentation substrates can contribute small amounts.', 'The bacterial name does not establish fibre or a prebiotic.', 'No species-wide glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Any benefit requires evidence for the exact strain, dose, viability and intended outcome; the species name alone is insufficient.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Bacteria are not themselves a UK-regulated allergen. Milk or other allergens may be present in carriers or the supplied preparation.', 'People with carrier allergies and anyone assessing a claimed probiotic effect; higher-risk patients need product-specific clinical advice.', 'Fermented vegetables, other fermented foods, culture preparations and some supplements.', 'Lactobacillus Plantarum; Lactiplantibacillus plantarum; L. plantarum', 'A culture selected for the required fermentation function; probiotic findings cannot be transferred to another strain by name alone.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Depends on the supplied preparation, carriers and cross-contact; taxonomy alone does not establish gluten-free suitability.', 'Context dependent', 'Species-level culture identity requiring strain and viability context', 'Insufficient', 'Species identification does not establish an authorised health claim. Probiotic wording can imply a health benefit and needs applicable claims compliance.', 'Lactobacillus plantarum is now Lactiplantibacillus plantarum. Record the strain and preparation before assessing viability or any claimed benefit.', 'lactobacillus plantarum|lactiplantibacillus plantarum', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Lactic Acid Bacteria Culture (UIL-0242)', 'Carriers, cryoprotectants and other ingredients depend on the culture preparation; no food-additive E-number follows from the species name.', 'https://www.lpsn.dsmz.de/species/lactiplantibacillus-plantarum | https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/probiotics-usefulness-and-safety | https://www.asa.org.uk/advice-online/food-probiotic-claims.html | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('dl-alpha-tocopheryl-acetate', 'UIL-0477', 'DL-Alpha-Tocopheryl Acetate', 'DL-alpha tocopheryl acetate; all-rac-alpha-tocopheryl acetate; all-rac alpha tocopheryl acetate', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Synthetic vitamin E ester', 'The acetate ester of synthetic all-rac-alpha-tocopherol, a vitamin E form. The body hydrolyses the ester to alpha-tocopherol.', 'Manufactured vitamin E ingredient; carriers, encapsulation and the finished formulation require confirmation.', 'Vitamin E fortification or supplementation in appropriate food-grade preparations.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Provides vitamin E activity at an identified dose; activity differs from natural RRR/d-alpha forms.', 'Not a protein ingredient.', 'Fat-soluble vitamin form, not a meaningful serving of dietary fat; carriers may add oil.', 'No inherent carbohydrate in the pure compound; carriers can contribute.', 'None in the pure compound.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in the pure chemical identity; check carriers and capsules.', 'People taking high-dose vitamin E or anticoagulant medicines should assess supplement exposure with a clinician; ordinary food fortification is a different exposure.', 'Vitamin premixes, fortified foods and supplements.', 'DL-Alpha-Tocopheryl Acetate; DL-alpha tocopheryl acetate; all-rac-alpha-tocopheryl acetate; all-rac alpha tocopheryl acetate', 'Another permitted vitamin E form with the correct activity conversion and formulation; equal ingredient mass need not provide equal vitamin activity.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Specific vitamin E ester requiring activity and dose context', 'High', 'The GB vitamin/mineral register lists DL-alpha-tocopheryl acetate as a vitamin E form. Product, dosage and claims requirements still apply.', 'DL-alpha-tocopheryl acetate is a synthetic vitamin E form. Keep its identity distinct and use the appropriate vitamin-activity conversion.', 'dl-alpha-tocopheryl acetate|dl-alpha tocopheryl acetate|all-rac-alpha-tocopheryl acetate|all-rac alpha tocopheryl acetate', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Vitamin E (UIL-0451); D-Alpha-Tocopherol (UIL-0503)', 'Do not automatically assign E307 or E306: alpha-tocopherol and tocopherol-rich extract are not the same chemical identity as this acetate ester.', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/VitaminE-HealthProfessional/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('magnesium-chloride', 'UIL-0478', 'Magnesium Chloride', 'Magnesium chloride hexahydrate; E511; E 511; INS 511', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Magnesium salt', 'A magnesium chloride salt supplied in food-grade forms, including hydrated grades. Water of crystallisation changes the elemental-magnesium proportion by weight.', 'Purified mineral-salt manufacture; source, hydration and food-grade specification must be confirmed.', 'A permitted magnesium source and, where authorised, a functional food additive such as a firming agent.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Can supply elemental magnesium; the compound weight is not the same as the magnesium dose.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'None in the pure salt; blends may contain carriers.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'No generic glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Higher supplemental doses can cause diarrhoea or abdominal symptoms; this does not describe every food-use exposure.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in the pure mineral salt; check the preparation.', 'People with impaired kidney function or interacting medicines need clinical advice before supplementation; assess elemental dose rather than salt weight.', 'Specified functional food preparations, mineral fortification and supplements.', 'Magnesium Chloride; Magnesium chloride hexahydrate; E511; E 511; INS 511', 'Another authorised magnesium source or functional ingredient matched to the purpose; dose and technological performance differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Mineral salt with food-additive and nutrient-source roles', 'High', 'Magnesium chloride is E511 on the approved additive list and a listed GB magnesium source. Permission depends on the intended use and applicable food conditions, not merely appearance on a list.', 'Magnesium chloride can provide magnesium or a food-processing function. Check food grade, hydration, permitted use and elemental dose.', 'magnesium chloride|magnesium chloride hexahydrate|e511|e 511|ins 511', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Magnesium Oxide (UIL-0400); Magnesium Citrate (UIL-0426); Magnesium Carbonate (UIL-0452); Magnesium Sulphate (UIL-0504)', 'E511 identifies magnesium chloride when used as an additive; this is not evidence that every use is for the same function or that every nigari blend is pure magnesium chloride.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers | https://apps.who.int/food-additives-contaminants-jecfa-database/Home/Chemical/3331 | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/magnesium-healthprofessional/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('l-threonine', 'UIL-0479', 'L-Threonine', 'L threonine; L-threonine amino acid', 'Amino acids and functional nutrition', 'Essential amino acid', 'The L form of threonine, one of the amino acids humans need from dietary sources.', 'Manufactured and purified to a specified grade; production route and carriers require confirmation.', 'Amino-acid composition in specified nutritional or food formulations.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Provides one essential amino acid; it does not replace a balanced protein source.', 'A free amino acid, not an intact or complete protein.', 'None in the pure compound.', 'None in the pure compound; assess carriers.', 'None in the pure compound.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Its physiological role does not establish a gut-barrier, mucin or digestive-treatment benefit from supplementation.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in the pure amino-acid identity; check carriers and residual-source specifications where relevant.', 'Anyone using an isolated-amino-acid supplement or specialist nutritional formula should assess dose and the complete formulation.', 'Specified amino-acid blends, nutritional formulations and supplements.', 'L-Threonine; L threonine; L-threonine amino acid', 'A complete dietary protein or an appropriately formulated amino-acid mixture, depending on the nutritional purpose.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Isolated essential amino acid requiring grade and dose context', 'High', 'Food suitability and permission depend on the actual grade, product category and intended use. Pharmaceutical or feed specifications do not alone establish food permission.', 'L-threonine is an essential amino acid. Its isolated form needs grade and formulation checks and is not a complete protein.', 'l-threonine|l threonine|l-threonine amino acid', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'L-Leucine (UIL-0323); L-Isoleucine (UIL-0349)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://ajiaminoscience.eu/aminoacid/product/l-threonine/ | https://www.ajihealthandnutrition.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/productsheet-l-threonine.pdf | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/ExerciseAndAthleticPerformance-HealthProfessional/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('vegetable-juice-concentrate', 'UIL-0480', 'Vegetable Juice Concentrate', 'Concentrated vegetable juice; vegetable juice concentrates', 'Water and liquid bases', 'Concentrated vegetable juice', 'Vegetable juice with part of its water removed. The vegetable species, blend and concentration determine the resulting ingredient.', 'Juice from one or more specified vegetables, concentrated by the supplier''s process.', 'Vegetable flavour, colour, liquid solids and, in some recipes, sweetness.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Concentrates juice components; it is not nutritionally equivalent to a serving of whole vegetables.', 'Usually not a concentrated protein source; species and concentration matter.', 'Usually limited in plain juice concentrates; blends can differ.', 'Contains concentrated juice sugars in species-dependent amounts; these count as free sugars.', 'Juicing removes much of the whole vegetable''s fibre; do not assume a whole-vegetable fibre contribution.', 'Assess sugars, dilution and portion; no universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Source-dependent: CELERY is a regulated allergen if present. Other individual vegetable allergies and added ingredients require assessment.', 'People with celery or other relevant allergies, and anyone assessing free sugars or the actual vegetable source.', 'Drinks, soups, sauces, savoury foods, bakery and formulations using vegetable colour or flavour.', 'Vegetable Juice Concentrate; Concentrated vegetable juice; vegetable juice concentrates', 'Specified single-strength juice, puree or whole vegetables where suitable; water, fibre and technical performance differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Concentrated liquid plant ingredient requiring species and use context', 'Moderate', 'Identify the vegetables and relevant allergens accurately. A colouring-food use and an authorised colour additive require different assessments; concentrate alone establishes neither an E-number nor a preservative exemption.', 'Vegetable juice concentrate supplies concentrated juice solids, colour or flavour. Check the source vegetables, sugars, dilution and allergens.', 'vegetable juice concentrate|concentrated vegetable juice|vegetable juice concentrates', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Vegetable Juice (UIL-0454); Beetroot Juice Concentrate (UIL-0176); Potato Juice Concentrate (UIL-0355)', 'No automatic E162, nitrate-preservative identity or preservative-free status. Added preservatives and the regulatory role depend on the supplied product and intended use.', 'https://www.svz.com/products/juice-concentrates/ | https://lemonconcentrate.com/carrot-juice-concentrate/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses?c=Linux', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('fenugreek-seed', 'UIL-0481', 'Fenugreek Seed', 'Fenugreek seeds; methi seeds; Trigonella foenum-graecum seeds', 'Herbs, spices and seasonings', 'Culinary spice seed', 'Seeds of Trigonella foenum-graecum used whole or ground as a spice. Culinary use differs from concentrated extracts and supplements.', 'Harvested and dried fenugreek seeds; roasting or grinding depends on the preparation.', 'Characteristic bitter, aromatic flavour in spice blends and foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'The seeds contain protein, carbohydrate and fibre, but small seasoning portions limit the nutrient contribution.', 'Contains seed protein; a spice portion is not a main protein serving.', 'Contains some seed fat; do not treat the spice as an oil ingredient.', 'Contains carbohydrate; no fixed carbohydrate contribution without the portion.', 'Contains seed fibre, with a small contribution at usual seasoning levels.', 'Some supplementation studies suggest effects on blood glucose, but evidence limitations and doses prevent assigning a culinary-seed treatment benefit.', 'Higher amounts can cause digestive symptoms; ordinary seasoning and supplements are different exposures.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Fenugreek allergy is possible, including serious reactions. It is outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens; spice blends may contain regulated allergens.', 'People with fenugreek allergy. Larger-than-food amounts require particular care during pregnancy or with medicines; the risks of supplements should not be assigned to a pinch of spice.', 'Curry blends, pickles, breads, spice pastes and regional dishes.', 'Fenugreek Seed; Fenugreek seeds; methi seeds; Trigonella foenum-graecum seeds', 'A tolerated spice blend matched to flavour needs; another legume is not automatically suitable for a diagnosed allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Culinary spice requiring allergy and dose context', 'Moderate', 'Describe the seed and any blend ingredients accurately. Traditional use and supplement research do not establish an authorised health claim for a food.', 'Fenugreek seed is a flavouring spice. Keep culinary portions distinct from supplements, and retain its potential for allergy.', 'fenugreek seed|fenugreek seeds|methi seeds|trigonella foenum-graecum seeds', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Curry Powder (UIL-0986); Cumin (UIL-0215)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/fenugreek | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('smoked-salt', 'UIL-0482', 'Smoked Salt', 'Smoked sea salt; smoked salt flakes; oak-smoked sea salt', 'Salt and savoury bases', 'Flavoured culinary salt', 'Culinary salt given a smoky flavour, for example by exposure to wood smoke. The product specification should identify the process and any added flavourings.', 'Food-grade salt, with smoking or other stated flavour preparation; salt source and wood type vary.', 'Salty taste and smoky aroma in small quantities.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Primarily a salt and sodium contribution; smoking does not make an otherwise ordinary salt low in sodium.', 'None inherent in plain smoked salt.', 'None inherent in plain smoked salt.', 'None inherent in salt; sugar or flavour carriers can occur in blends.', 'None in plain smoked salt.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in a plain salt-and-smoke preparation; blends and flavour carriers need separate assessment.', 'People monitoring salt intake and anyone distinguishing directly smoked salt from a flavoured seasoning blend.', 'Finishing salts, rubs, marinades, barbecue seasoning and savoury recipes.', 'Smoked Salt; Smoked sea salt; smoked salt flakes; oak-smoked sea salt', 'A smaller amount of salt or a suitable herb/spice mixture where appropriate; ordinary sea salt is not a sodium-free alternative.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Culinary salt requiring sodium and flavour-process context', 'High', 'Use an accurate ingredient description. Where smoke flavourings are added, their identity and applicable permissions require separate checks; direct smoking and an added smoke flavouring are not the same process.', 'Smoked salt adds smoky flavour and salt. Check additions and process, and count its sodium within the overall diet.', 'smoked salt|smoked sea salt|smoked salt flakes|oak-smoked sea salt', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Sea Salt (UIL-0222); Table Salt (UIL-0274); Himalayan Pink Salt (UIL-0326); Smoked Paprika (UIL-0202)', 'No additive is inherent in directly smoked salt. Anti-caking agents, added smoke flavourings or other seasonings depend on the actual product.', 'https://maldonsalt.com/product/smoked-sea-salt-flakes-125g/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/salt-in-your-diet/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('balsamic-glaze', 'UIL-0483', 'Balsamic Glaze', 'Balsamic vinegar glaze; glaze with balsamic vinegar; balsamic reduction', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Compound vinegar-based condiment', 'A thick balsamic-flavoured condiment, made by reduction or formulated with balsamic vinegar and other ingredients. Sugar, grape components and thickeners vary.', 'Balsamic vinegar or grape-derived components with the specified sweeteners, thickeners and other ingredients.', 'Sweet-sour flavour, viscosity and decorative drizzling.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Often a concentrated sugar-containing condiment; the actual recipe and serving determine its nutritional contribution.', 'Usually little protein.', 'Usually little fat in a plain glaze; added ingredients can change this.', 'Sugars can come from grape components and added sweeteners; assess the formulation.', 'Not a substitute for the fibre in whole grapes.', 'Assess sugars and portion; acidity does not establish a glucose-treatment benefit.', 'No established gut-treatment or probiotic effect assigned to a vinegar-based glaze.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Sulphites may require declaration depending on the actual concentration. Other allergens depend on the recipe and additions.', 'People with sulphite sensitivity or relevant recipe allergies, and those monitoring free sugars.', 'Salads, cheese accompaniments, grilled foods, sauces and desserts.', 'Balsamic Glaze; Balsamic vinegar glaze; glaze with balsamic vinegar; balsamic reduction', 'A smaller amount of suitable vinegar or another tolerated dressing; acidity, sweetness and texture will differ.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No universal gluten status; assess the vinegar, thickeners, flavourings and other ingredients.', 'Context dependent', 'Variable compound condiment requiring sugar and allergen context', 'Moderate', 'A glaze containing a protected balsamic vinegar is not automatically the protected vinegar itself. Use accurate compound-ingredient and allergen information for the actual product.', 'Balsamic glaze adds concentrated sweet-sour flavour. Check sugar, sulphites and thickeners rather than treating it as plain balsamic vinegar.', 'balsamic glaze|balsamic vinegar glaze|glaze with balsamic vinegar|balsamic reduction', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Balsamic Vinegar (UIL-0353)', 'Some commercial glazes contain modified starch, gums, colours or sulphur dioxide. No particular additive is universal to all reductions or glazes.', 'https://global.filippoberio.com/products/vinegars/balsamic-glaze/classic/ | https://filippoberio.com/products/vinegar/classic-balsamic-glaze/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('peach-juice-concentrate', 'UIL-0484', 'Peach Juice Concentrate', 'Concentrated peach juice', 'Fruit ingredients', 'Concentrated fruit juice', 'Peach juice with part of its water removed. It differs from peach puree, puree concentrate and a peach-flavoured syrup.', 'Pressed peach juice concentrated by the supplier''s process; clear and cloudy grades may differ.', 'Peach flavour, juice solids, sweetness and formulation convenience.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Contains concentrated juice components; dilution, clarity and grade determine the final composition.', 'Not a concentrated protein ingredient.', 'Usually little fat in plain juice concentrate.', 'Contains fruit-juice sugars, which count as free sugars.', 'Usually much less fibre than whole peaches; do not assume the fibre profile of puree.', 'Assess sugars, dilution and serving; no universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Peach allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check blends and other added ingredients.', 'People with peach allergy or sensitivity, and anyone assessing free sugars or distinguishing juice from puree.', 'Drinks, desserts, confectionery, sauces and fruit-flavoured preparations.', 'Peach Juice Concentrate; Concentrated peach juice', 'Whole peach, puree or single-strength juice where the recipe permits; water, fibre and sweetness differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Concentrated fruit juice requiring grade and dilution context', 'High', 'Use an accurate juice/concentrate description for the supplied ingredient. A flavoured syrup containing a little concentrate is a different compound product.', 'Peach juice concentrate adds peach juice solids and free sugars. It is not nutritionally interchangeable with whole peaches or peach puree.', 'peach juice concentrate|concentrated peach juice', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Peach Puree (UIL-0458); Peach Powder (UIL-0510); Dried Peach (UIL-0536); Fruit Juice Concentrate (UIL-0006)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://eebriansmith.com/ingredient/peach-juice-concentrate/ | https://eebriansmith.com/ingredient/peach-puree-concentrate/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('tapioca-pearls', 'UIL-0485', 'Tapioca Pearls', 'Tapioca pearl; pearl tapioca; tapioca balls', 'Vegetable ingredients', 'Formed cassava-starch ingredient', 'Pearls formed from tapioca/cassava starch for cooking into a chewy or thickened food. Sweetened, coloured and quick-cook grades differ from plain dried pearls.', 'Cassava-root starch formed into pearls, with preparation-specific water, cooking or drying steps and possible additions.', 'Chewy texture in drinks and desserts, and thickening in suitable recipes.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Plain pearls are predominantly starch; syrups and other additions can add free sugars.', 'Usually little protein.', 'Usually little fat in plain pearls.', 'Mainly starch before any sweetening; cooking and portion affect digestion.', 'Usually little fibre; not equivalent to whole cassava.', 'Assess starch, syrup and portion; no universal glycaemic index or resistant-starch benefit assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in plain tapioca starch. Check formulated pearls, the cooking liquid and the complete drink or dessert.', 'People assessing added sugars or recipe allergens; use food-grade pearls and follow cooking and storage instructions.', 'Tapioca pudding, bubble tea, sweet soups and other desserts.', 'Tapioca Pearls; Tapioca pearl; pearl tapioca; tapioca balls', 'Another suitable starch preparation matched to texture; sago, fruit-flavoured popping pearls and tapioca are not automatically the same ingredient.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Formed starch ingredient with formulation-dependent additions', 'High', 'Describe the starch source and added ingredients accurately. Tapioca pearls alone do not establish the allergen or dietary status of a milk tea or dessert.', 'Tapioca pearls mainly provide starch and texture. Check whether they are plain, sweetened or otherwise formulated, and assess the full dish.', 'tapioca pearls|tapioca pearl|pearl tapioca|tapioca balls', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Tapioca starch (UIL-0032); Cassava Starch (UIL-0539); Sago Starch (UIL-0461); Modified Tapioca Starch (UIL-0279)', 'Plain dried pearls may contain only tapioca starch. Colours, preservatives, modified starches and sweeteners in formulated grades must be assessed individually.', 'https://www.bobsredmill.com/product/small-pearl-tapioca | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('malted-wheat-flour', 'UIL-0486', 'Malted Wheat Flour', 'Wheat malt flour; milled wheat malt', 'Cereal and grain derivatives', 'Milled malted wheat', 'Flour produced by milling wheat that has been germinated and dried during malting. Milling grade and enzyme activity depend on the product.', 'Wheat grain malted by controlled steeping, germination and drying, then milled.', 'Malty flavour, colour, cereal solids and, in suitable grades, enzyme activity in food manufacture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Contains cereal carbohydrate and wheat protein; fibre and sugars vary with milling and malting conditions.', 'Contains wheat protein, including gluten.', 'Usually a limited grain-fat contribution; milling affects the amount.', 'Contains starch and variable sugars; malting can change starch breakdown.', 'Depends on wholegrain retention and refinement; malted does not automatically mean wholemeal.', 'No fixed glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Malting does not establish coeliac suitability or a digestive-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains WHEAT, a regulated allergen. Other malted cereals require their own ingredient identification.', 'People with wheat allergy or coeliac disease, and formulators needing to know whether the flour is diastatic.', 'Malted breads, biscuits, bakery, cereal preparations and specified manufacturing blends.', 'Malted Wheat Flour; Wheat malt flour; milled wheat malt', 'A verified suitable non-wheat ingredient matched to flavour and enzyme needs; another malt is not automatically gluten-free.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'Contains wheat gluten; malting and milling do not make ordinary malted wheat flour gluten-free.', 'Context dependent', 'Milled malted cereal requiring wheat and enzyme context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise wheat. Generic malt does not identify a cereal source, and malted flour is distinct from a malt extract or syrup.', 'Malted wheat flour adds cereal flavour and sometimes enzyme activity. It still contains wheat/gluten, and the milling grade determines its fibre contribution.', 'malted wheat flour|wheat malt flour|milled wheat malt', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Wheat Malt (UIL-0460); Malted Wheat Flakes (UIL-0631); Barley Malt Flour (UIL-0512); Barley malt extract (UIL-0026)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.muntons.com/food_beverage/wheat-malt-flour/ | https://www.muntons.com/food_type/flour/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('arrowroot-starch', 'UIL-0487', 'Arrowroot Starch', 'Arrowroot powder; Maranta arundinacea starch; arrowroot flour', 'Starches and carbohydrate ingredients', 'Purified rhizome starch', 'Food-grade starch obtained from arrowroot, commonly Maranta arundinacea. Commercial names and starch blends require source confirmation.', 'Starch separated from arrowroot rhizomes and dried to a powder.', 'Thickening, binding and a relatively neutral flavour in sauces, desserts and baking.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Mainly starch; it does not retain the nutrient balance of whole rhizome tissue.', 'Usually little protein in purified starch.', 'Usually little fat.', 'Predominantly starch; assess portion and cooking.', 'Usually little fibre; not automatically resistant starch.', 'No universal glycaemic index or glucose-lowering effect assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in plain arrowroot starch; assess blends and relevant cross-contact.', 'Anyone confirming botanical source, food grade or a gluten-free claim on the actual preparation.', 'Sauces, gravies, puddings, baking and starch blends.', 'Arrowroot Starch; Arrowroot powder; Maranta arundinacea starch; arrowroot flour', 'Tapioca, potato or maize starch matched to the intended texture; source identities differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Refined plant starch requiring botanical-source context', 'High', 'Use the correct starch-source description. A supplier''s gluten-free or food-grade status does not apply to every product called arrowroot powder.', 'Arrowroot starch is mainly carbohydrate used for texture. Check its botanical source and any blending rather than assuming whole-root nutrition.', 'arrowroot starch|arrowroot powder|maranta arundinacea starch|arrowroot flour', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Tapioca starch (UIL-0032); Potato starch (UIL-0031); Maize Starch (UIL-0008); Native Starch (UIL-0565)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.ingredients-uk.com/product/arrowroot-powder/ | https://www.ingredients-uk.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/12141-G-Arrow-Root-Powder-v5.pdf | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('black-treacle', 'UIL-0488', 'Black Treacle', 'Black treacle syrup; dark treacle', 'Sugars, syrups and sweetening ingredients', 'Dark sugar-refining syrup', 'A dark, strongly flavoured sugar-refining syrup used in British cooking and baking. It is related to molasses, but the supplied formulation and grade still matter.', 'Cane-sugar-refining syrup or molasses-based preparation; check the supplier''s ingredient declaration.', 'Bittersweet flavour, dark colour, sweetness and moisture.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'A sugar-containing syrup with variable minerals; dark colour is not a reliable measure of its nutritional value.', 'Not a main protein source at typical use levels.', 'Usually little fat.', 'Contains free sugars; quantities depend on the grade and serving.', 'Not equivalent to a fibre-rich whole plant food.', 'Count its sugars within the recipe; no diabetes-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Check sulphites and other declared ingredients in the supplied product. A dark sugar syrup is not inherently a nut, milk or cereal allergen.', 'People with sulphite sensitivity and those monitoring free sugars.', 'Gingerbread, parkin, Christmas pudding, dark cakes, treacle toffee, marinades and glazes.', 'Black Treacle; Black treacle syrup; dark treacle', 'A suitable syrup matched to flavour and recipe needs; replacing one sugar syrup with another does not automatically reduce free sugars.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Sugar-containing culinary syrup with grade-dependent composition', 'Moderate', 'Identify the actual syrup and any required allergens. Mineral or health claims need the supplied product''s composition and applicable conditions.', 'Black treacle adds dark, bittersweet flavour and free sugars. Its composition and any sulphite information require the actual product label.', 'black treacle|black treacle syrup|dark treacle', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Molasses (UIL-0462); Golden syrup (UIL-0024); Cane Sugar (UIL-0228); Brown Sugar (UIL-0358)', 'Dark colour does not establish a caramel-colour additive. Sulphites and other additions need the product specification; do not infer an E-number from colour.', 'https://www.lylesgoldensyrup.com/blog/black-treacle-vs-molasses-what-are-the-key-differences/ | https://www.lylesgoldensyrup.com/product/bottle-1/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('pea-protein-concentrate', 'UIL-0489', 'Pea Protein Concentrate', 'Pea protein concentrate powder; yellow pea protein concentrate', 'Legumes and pulse derivatives', 'Concentrated pea protein', 'A pea-derived ingredient enriched in protein relative to pea flour. Concentration methods and the retained starch and fibre vary by grade.', 'Peas processed to separate a protein-enriched fraction; dry milling and air classification are used for some commercial grades.', 'Protein addition, water binding, emulsification and texture in food formulation.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Supplies plant protein with variable residual starch, fibre, fat and minerals.', 'Protein concentration and amino-acid quality need the actual grade; concentrate is not interchangeable with isolate.', 'Residual pea fat varies.', 'Often retains some pea carbohydrate; not automatically carbohydrate-free.', 'Retained pea fibre varies with separation method.', 'No generic glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Tolerance depends on the grade and serving; concentration alone does not establish a digestive or prebiotic benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pea allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Relevant cross-contact and added ingredients need separate assessment.', 'People with pea allergy or individual pulse intolerance, and anyone comparing concentrates with isolates or whole peas.', 'Plant-based meat alternatives, bakery, snacks, sauces and nutritional formulations.', 'Pea Protein Concentrate; Pea protein concentrate powder; yellow pea protein concentrate', 'A tolerated protein ingredient matched to the recipe; other legumes and proteins require their own allergen checks.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Protein-enriched pulse fraction requiring grade context', 'High', 'Protein claims require the actual finished-food composition. A pea ingredient is not automatically allergen-free because pea is outside the regulated 14.', 'Pea protein concentrate provides concentrated plant protein while retaining variable other pea components. Check the grade rather than assuming isolate-level purity.', 'pea protein concentrate|pea protein concentrate powder|yellow pea protein concentrate', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pea Flour (UIL-0437); Yellow Pea Flour (UIL-0463); Pea Protein Isolate (UIL-0016); Pea Starch (UIL-0383); Hydrolysed Pea Protein (UIL-0496)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.aminola.com/en/products/pea-protein-concentrate-55/ | https://www.ingredion.com/content/dam/ingredion/technical-documents/emea/VITESSENCE%20Prista%20P%20155_70000518_EN.pdf | https://allergynorthwest.nhs.uk/home-patient/managing-allergies/patient-leaflets/legume-allergy-2/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('walnut-paste', 'UIL-0490', 'Walnut Paste', 'Walnut butter; pure walnut paste; ground walnut paste', 'Nut and seed derivatives', 'Ground walnut preparation', 'Walnuts ground to a paste or nut butter. Plain 100% walnut products differ from sweetened praline, flavoured paste and compound fillings.', 'Walnut kernels, raw or roasted as specified, ground until their oil and solids form a paste.', 'Walnut flavour, richness, fat and a spreadable or filling texture.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Plain whole-kernel paste retains walnut fat, protein and fibre; additions change the profile.', 'Contains walnut protein; not a protein isolate.', 'Fat-rich, mainly unsaturated fat in plain walnut paste; do not assign one fatty-acid percentage.', 'Plain paste differs from sugar-rich praline or sweetened fillings.', 'Retains walnut fibre when the whole kernel is used.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains WALNUT, a regulated tree-nut allergen. Grinding and roasting do not establish suitability for walnut allergy.', 'People with walnut allergy and anyone checking whether a paste is pure walnut or a sweetened compound product.', 'Bakery, pralines, ice cream, sauces, spreads and fillings.', 'Walnut Paste; Walnut butter; pure walnut paste; ground walnut paste', 'A tolerated nut-free or seed-based preparation where appropriate; another tree nut is not automatically safe for walnut allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Ground whole-nut preparation requiring allergen and recipe context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise walnut. Pure-paste and no-added-sugar descriptions must reflect the actual product.', 'Plain walnut paste retains whole-kernel walnut nutrients and remains a walnut al