  ('hemp-seed-oil', 'UIL-0491', 'Hemp Seed Oil', 'Hempseed oil; edible hemp seed oil; Cannabis sativa seed oil', 'Oils and fats', 'Culinary seed oil', 'Edible oil obtained from hemp seeds. It is a different ingredient from CBD extracts or cannabinoid-enriched oils.', 'Food-grade hemp seeds pressed or otherwise processed to recover oil; refining and filtration depend on the product.', 'Culinary fat, nutty flavour where retained, and a carrier in suitable formulations.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'A concentrated fat and energy source with predominantly unsaturated fats; it does not retain the protein and fibre profile of whole hemp seeds.', 'Not a meaningful protein source in plain oil.', 'Typically rich in polyunsaturated fats, including plant omega-3; exact proportions vary by grade.', 'Little carbohydrate in plain oil.', 'None in plain oil.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Hemp allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check blends and relevant cross-contact.', 'People with hemp allergy, and anyone distinguishing food-grade seed oil from CBD, cosmetic or cannabinoid-enriched products.', 'Dressings, culinary oils, sauces and food formulations.', 'Hemp Seed Oil; Hempseed oil; edible hemp seed oil; Cannabis sativa seed oil', 'A tolerated food-grade oil matched to cooking and flavour needs; different oils have different fatty-acid profiles.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 2', 'Culinary seed oil requiring grade and cannabinoid-product distinction', 'High', 'FSA guidance distinguishes conventional hemp seed oil from CBD extracts. Added cannabinoids and product claims require their own regulatory assessment; seed-oil identity is not blanket permission for a CBD product.', 'Hemp seed oil supplies culinary fat, including unsaturated fatty acids. Confirm food grade and keep it distinct from CBD oil.', 'hemp seed oil|hempseed oil|edible hemp seed oil|cannabis sativa seed oil', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Hemp Seeds (UIL-0157); Hemp Protein (UIL-0080); Hemp Protein Concentrate (UIL-0314)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.goodhemp.com/our-products/extra-virgin-hemp-seed-oil/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cannabidiol-cbd-guidance/cannabidiol-cbd-guidance | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Omega3FattyAcids-HealthProfessional/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('whipping-cream', 'UIL-0492', 'Whipping Cream', 'Dairy whipping cream; cream for whipping', 'Dairy ingredients', 'Dairy cream', 'Dairy cream with a fat content and formulation suitable for whipping. It differs from whipped toppings and vegetable-fat alternatives.', 'The milk-fat-rich fraction of dairy milk; heat treatment, stabilisation and other additions depend on the grade.', 'Whipping, aeration, richness and texture in desserts and other foods.', 'Processed culinary ingredient', 'Provides milk fat, including saturated fat, with some milk protein and lactose; the amount and formulation determine the contribution.', 'Contains milk protein; not a concentrated protein ingredient.', 'Fat-rich; use the actual product''s milk-fat content rather than assuming one universal percentage.', 'Contains lactose unless specifically reduced; sweetened grades add other sugars.', 'None inherent in plain dairy cream.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; assess lactose and added sugars in the recipe.', 'Lactose tolerance varies. Lactose-free dairy whipping cream still requires milk-allergen assessment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MILK, a regulated allergen. Heat treatment does not establish suitability for milk allergy.', 'People with milk allergy or lactose intolerance, and anyone assessing saturated fat, serving size or a stabilised formulation.', 'Whipped desserts, cakes, fillings, mousses, sauces and dairy preparations.', 'Whipping Cream; Dairy whipping cream; cream for whipping', 'A verified milk-free whipping preparation for milk allergy; check its own allergens and recipe performance.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Dairy cream requiring milk-allergen and formulation context', 'High', 'The Dairy UK/PTF code retains customary cream compositional descriptions; former statutory cream fat limits were revoked in December 2018. General food-information and milk-allergen requirements still apply.', 'Whipping cream adds dairy fat and can hold air when whipped. Check the actual fat content, additions and milk-allergen information.', 'whipping cream|dairy whipping cream|cream for whipping', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cream (UIL-0414); Single Cream (UIL-0466); Double Cream (UIL-0440); Cream Powder (UIL-0570)', 'Some UHT or stabilised grades contain stabilisers or emulsifiers; these are not universal to dairy whipping cream.', 'https://www.arlapro.com/en-gb/product-catalogue/arla-pro-high-extra-stability-35-fat-whipping-cream-1l/ | https://www.dairyuk.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/FINAL-Compositional-Standards-Cream.pdf | https://www.provtrade.co.uk/technical-and-legislation/labelling-and-standards.aspx | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/milk-and-dairy-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('sugared-egg-yolk', 'UIL-0493', 'Sugared Egg Yolk', 'Sweetened egg yolk; sugared liquid egg yolk; egg yolk with sugar', 'Egg ingredients', 'Sweetened egg-yolk preparation', 'Egg yolk prepared with added sugar, commonly supplied as a commercial liquid product. Solids and sugar content depend on the grade.', 'Separated egg yolks combined with sugar and processed to the supplied specification.', 'Yolk functionality, richness, colour and sweetness in food manufacture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Provides yolk fat and protein plus added free sugars; water and sugar levels change the composition.', 'Contains egg protein.', 'Contains yolk fat, phospholipids and cholesterol; amounts depend on the formulation.', 'Added sugar contributes free sugars; do not use the carbohydrate profile of unsweetened yolk.', 'None inherent in egg yolk and sugar.', 'Assess added sugars and portion; no glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains EGG, a regulated allergen. Sweetening does not remove egg-allergen relevance.', 'People with egg allergy, those monitoring free sugars, and anyone preparing uncooked or lightly cooked foods.', 'Ice cream, custard, bakery, confectionery and sweet emulsified preparations.', 'Sugared Egg Yolk; Sweetened egg yolk; sugared liquid egg yolk; egg yolk with sugar', 'A suitable egg-free recipe for egg allergy; plain yolk requires separate adjustment of sugar and processing conditions.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Sweetened egg preparation requiring sugar and handling context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise egg. The word sugared does not establish pasteurisation, shelf stability or safety for raw use; follow the product''s storage and handling instructions.', 'Sugared egg yolk supplies yolk functionality with added sugar. Confirm the grade, handling requirements and egg-allergen information.', 'sugared egg yolk|sweetened egg yolk|sugared liquid egg yolk|egg yolk with sugar', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Egg Yolk (UIL-0415); Liquid Egg Yolk (UIL-0441); Salted Egg Yolk (UIL-0467); Egg Yolk Powder (UIL-0072)', 'Sugar is part of this preparation. Preservatives or other ingredients depend on the supplied grade; no additive E-number follows from sugared.', 'https://www.bouwhuis-enthoven.com/our-products-and-solutions/organoleptic/sugared-liquid-egg-yolk/ | https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-on-safe-storage-handling-and-use-of-eggs-for-catering | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('pork-stock-concentrate', 'UIL-0494', 'Pork Stock Concentrate', 'Concentrated pork stock; pork broth concentrate; concentrated pork broth', 'Meat and poultry ingredients', 'Concentrated animal stock preparation', 'A concentrated pork-derived stock or broth ingredient, sometimes formulated with salt, flavourings and other ingredients.', 'Pork-derived stock concentrated or otherwise prepared to the supplier''s specification; meat, bone, fat and added ingredients vary.', 'Pork flavour, savoury depth and liquid or paste solids in food manufacture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Protein, gelatin, fat and salt depend on the product and dilution; concentrate does not automatically mean high protein.', 'May contain meat-derived or gelatin-rich protein; quantity and amino-acid balance are grade-dependent.', 'Variable residual or added fat.', 'Sugars, maltodextrin or other carbohydrate ingredients may be added.', 'None inherent in the animal stock; plant additions may contribute small amounts.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; assess added carbohydrate and the complete recipe.', 'Broth or gelatin content does not establish a gut-healing or digestive-treatment effect.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pork is outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens, but compound stocks can contain CELERY, SOYA, MILK, cereals or other allergens depending on the recipe.', 'People avoiding pork for dietary or religious reasons, people with relevant allergies, and those monitoring salt intake.', 'Soups, sauces, gravies, ramen, ready meals and meat preparations.', 'Pork Stock Concentrate; Concentrated pork stock; pork broth concentrate; concentrated pork broth', 'A suitable vegetable or non-porcine stock matched to the dietary and technical need; check its own salt and allergens.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No universal gluten status; assess the stock recipe, flavourings, hydrolysed ingredients and cross-contact.', 'Context dependent', 'Animal-derived compound stock requiring recipe and dilution context', 'Moderate', 'Identify the animal source and compound ingredients accurately. Nutrition and salt assessment should use the stated preparation/dilution conditions.', 'Pork stock concentrate adds pork flavour, with variable salt, fat and protein. Check the full recipe and intended dilution.', 'pork stock concentrate|concentrated pork stock|pork broth concentrate|concentrated pork broth', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pork (UIL-0416); Pork Protein (UIL-0468); Pork Gelatine (UIL-0520); Pork Fat (UIL-0947)', 'Some preparations contain thickeners, flavour enhancers or other additives; no specific additive or MSG content is inherent in stock concentrate.', 'https://essentiaproteins.com/int/ingredients/savory/stocks/probase-pork-stocks/ | https://kettlecuisine.com/products/reduced-sodium-pork-liquid-concentrated-base | https://www.karlsburger.com/products/bases/pork-base/xtra-fine-pork-base/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/salt-in-your-diet/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('hake', 'UIL-0495', 'Hake', 'Hake fish; hake fillet; Merluccius species', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'White fish', 'A commercial white-fish name. The UK designation Hake covers species of Merluccius; the exact species and product form still need confirmation.', 'Fish of the specified species and catch origin; the generic name does not identify a single fishery.', 'White-fish flesh, protein and texture in meals and seafood products.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Plain hake flesh supplies protein and is generally low-fat; coatings, sauces and added ingredients change the profile.', 'Provides fish protein.', 'Generally a lean white fish; do not assign an oily-fish omega-3 profile.', 'Little inherent carbohydrate in plain flesh; coatings and sauces can add starch or sugar.', 'None in plain fish.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains FISH, a regulated allergen. Cooking or freezing does not establish suitability for fish allergy.', 'People with fish allergy and anyone verifying the species, catch origin or a formulated seafood product.', 'Fillets, seafood meals, coated fish, fish pies and other prepared dishes.', 'Hake; Hake fish; hake fillet; Merluccius species', 'Another tolerated fish or an appropriate fish-free recipe; another fish species is not automatically safe for fish allergy.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'White-fish ingredient requiring species and product context', 'High', 'Use the appropriate commercial/scientific designation and any origin information required for the product. Qualified names such as Cape hake have species-specific meaning.', 'Hake is a lean white-fish ingredient and a fish allergen. Confirm the scientific species and assess coatings or sauces separately.', 'hake|hake fish|hake fillet', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Cod (UIL-0391); Haddock (UIL-0417); Pollock (UIL-0443); Alaska Pollock (UIL-0469)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/commercial-designations-of-fish-united-kingdom/commercial-designations-of-fish | https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/pacific-whiting/seafood | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/fish-and-shellfish-nutrition/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('hydrolysed-pea-protein', 'UIL-0496', 'Hydrolysed Pea Protein', 'Hydrolyzed pea protein; pea protein hydrolysate; hydrolysed pea proteins; hydrolyzed pea proteins', 'Plant proteins and meat alternatives', 'Pea protein hydrolysate', 'Pea protein broken into smaller peptides and amino acids by controlled hydrolysis. Degree of hydrolysis and functional properties vary by grade.', 'Pea-derived protein hydrolysed and processed to a food-grade specification.', 'Protein fortification, reduced viscosity, solubility or other formulation functions depending on the product.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'A protein-derived ingredient with grade-dependent peptide sizes, amino-acid balance and other components.', 'Provides pea-derived peptides and amino acids; not identical to intact pea protein isolate or concentrate.', 'Usually limited in a purified grade; carriers and blends can differ.', 'Residual carbohydrate and carriers depend on the specification.', 'Not automatically a meaningful source of pea fibre.', 'No generic glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Hydrolysis alone does not establish better tolerance, hypoallergenicity or a gut-treatment effect in people.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pea allergy remains relevant despite hydrolysis. Pea is outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens; assess other ingredients and cross-contact.', 'People with pea allergy or individual pulse intolerance, and anyone comparing hydrolysates with intact pea proteins.', 'Protein drinks, bars, bakery, extruded snacks and other specified nutritional formulations.', 'Hydrolysed Pea Protein; Hydrolyzed pea protein; pea protein hydrolysate; hydrolysed pea proteins; hydrolyzed pea proteins', 'A tolerated protein ingredient matched to the technical need; different sources and degrees of hydrolysis behave differently.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Hydrolysed pulse protein requiring allergy and grade context', 'Moderate', 'Use an accurate protein-source description. Hydrolysed does not establish an authorised digestibility, health or allergen-free claim.', 'Hydrolysed pea protein supplies pea-derived peptides for food formulation. Check the grade and retain pea-allergy relevance.', 'hydrolysed pea protein|hydrolyzed pea protein|pea protein hydrolysate|hydrolysed pea proteins|hydrolyzed pea proteins', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Pea Protein Isolate (UIL-0016); Pea Protein Concentrate (UIL-0489); Hydrolysed Wheat Protein (UIL-0470)', 'No fixed MSG content or E621 identity follows from hydrolysis. Added salts, carriers and other ingredients require their own assessment.', 'https://www.puris.com/ingredients/pea-proteins/p870h/ | https://www.roquette.com/food-nutrition/product-catalog/nutralys-h85 | https://allergynorthwest.nhs.uk/home-patient/managing-allergies/patient-leaflets/legume-allergy-2/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('lupin-fibre', 'UIL-0497', 'Lupin Fibre', 'Lupin fiber; lupin kernel fibre; lupin kernel fiber', 'Fibres and prebiotic ingredients', 'Lupin-derived fibre fraction', 'A fibre-rich ingredient separated from lupin seeds, including commercial kernel-fibre grades. Kernel and hull-derived materials need distinct specifications.', 'Food-grade lupin seed fractions processed to separate and recover fibre; the retained protein and other components depend on the grade.', 'Fibre enrichment, water and oil binding, and texture adjustment.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Primarily a fibre contribution with variable residual protein, fat and digestible carbohydrate.', 'May retain lupin protein; low protein does not establish allergen removal.', 'Residual lupin fat varies with processing.', 'Digestible carbohydrate depends on the grade; fibre is not interchangeable with starch.', 'Typically fibre-rich, with soluble/insoluble characteristics and amounts depending on the material.', 'No generic glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Fibre can affect stool characteristics and tolerance; no automatic species-wide prebiotic or digestive-treatment claim assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'LUPIN-derived and subject to relevant lupin-allergen declaration. Fibre extraction does not establish suitability for lupin allergy.', 'People with lupin allergy or a diagnosed relevant legume allergy, and those sensitive to concentrated fibre.', 'Fibre-enriched bakery, snacks, plant-based foods and other formulated products.', 'Lupin Fibre; Lupin fiber; lupin kernel fibre; lupin kernel fiber', 'A verified suitable non-lupin fibre matched to technical function and tolerance.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Concentrated plant fibre retaining lupin-allergen relevance', 'Moderate', 'Declare a