  ('milk-chocolate-crumb', 'UIL-0498', 'Milk Chocolate Crumb', 'Milk-chocolate crumb; milk choco crumb; milk chocolate manufacturing crumb', 'Cocoa, coffee and tea derivatives', 'Milk/cocoa chocolate-manufacturing intermediate', 'A dried manufacturing intermediate made from milk, sugar and cocoa mass/liquor, used in chocolate production. It is different from crumbled cake or biscuit.', 'The milk, sugar and cocoa mixture is heat processed, concentrated or dried, and milled according to the supplier''s process.', 'Dairy and cocoa flavour, caramelised notes where developed, and solids for chocolate manufacture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Contains sugar, milk components and cocoa components in recipe-dependent proportions.', 'Contains milk protein; amount depends on milk solids and recipe.', 'Milk and cocoa contribute variable fat, including saturated fat.', 'Contains added sugar and may contain lactose.', 'Cocoa may contribute some fibre; no generic high-fibre claim.', 'Assess sugars and the finished-food portion; no glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Lactose may be relevant; no established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains MILK in the conventional preparation. Soya, nuts, cereals and other allergens depend on the full specification and cross-contact.', 'People with milk allergy or lactose intolerance, and anyone distinguishing chocolate-manufacturing crumb from a baked topping.', 'Milk chocolate and chocolate-flavoured manufacturing formulations.', 'Milk Chocolate Crumb; Milk-chocolate crumb; milk choco crumb; milk chocolate manufacturing crumb', 'A verified suitable milk-free chocolate ingredient matched to the process; ordinary crumbs are not a direct manufacturing equivalent.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the milk/sugar/cocoa baseline; additional ingredients and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Dairy/cocoa compound intermediate requiring recipe context', 'High', 'Retain milk-allergen and compound-ingredient information. The crumb is an intermediate and does not by itself establish compliance with a finished milk-chocolate compositional standard.', 'Milk chocolate crumb combines milk, sugar and cocoa for chocolate manufacture. It contains milk and differs from cake or biscuit crumbs.', 'milk chocolate crumb|milk-chocolate crumb|milk choco crumb|milk chocolate manufacturing crumb', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Chocolate Crumb (UIL-0472); Cocoa Mass (UIL-0182); Cocoa Solids (UIL-0184); Cake Crumb (UIL-0449); Biscuit Crumb (UIL-0397)', 'Emulsifiers, flavourings and other additives depend on the supplied formulation; none follows automatically from crumb.', 'https://www.delica.com/media/wnvdoofr/enflyerchocoblondcrumbhighres.pdf | https://meadowfoods.co.uk/products/meadow-confectionery/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('mint-extract', 'UIL-0499', 'Mint Extract', 'Culinary mint extract; pure mint extract; mint flavour extract; mint flavor extract', 'Flavouring food ingredients', 'Botanical flavour extract', 'A concentrated culinary mint-flavour preparation. It may use spearmint, peppermint or a blend, with carriers depending on the product.', 'Mint-derived flavour components, for example oils of spearmint and peppermint in an alcohol/water carrier.', 'Mint flavour in small quantities.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Primarily a flavour contribution; any alcohol, sugars and energy depend on the carrier and use level.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at flavouring levels.', 'Mint oils may be present, but this is not a dietary-fat serving.', 'Sugar or syrup carriers vary by preparation.', 'Not equivalent to the fibre in mint leaves.', 'No glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Culinary extract is not equivalent to medicinal peppermint-oil capsules; no digestive or IBS-treatment claim assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Mint allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check the complete flavour preparation and carriers.', 'People with mint allergy or carrier restrictions, including those avoiding alcohol.', 'Confectionery, chocolate, baking, desserts and flavoured drinks.', 'Mint Extract; Culinary mint extract; pure mint extract; mint flavour extract; mint flavor extract', 'Another suitable flavour preparation or mint leaf where appropriate; strength and carrier differ.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Commonly used in NOVA 4 foods', 'Variable mint flavour preparation requiring species and carrier context', 'Moderate', 'Use an accurate flavouring description and assess claims for the actual food. Generic mint does not establish one botanical species or medicinal preparation.', 'Mint extract adds concentrated mint flavour. Confirm the mint source and carriers rather than automatically treating it as peppermint extract.', 'mint extract|culinary mint extract|pure mint extract|mint flavour extract|mint flavor extract', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Peppermint Extract (UIL-0473); Mint (UIL-0637); Peppermint Leaf (UIL-0662); Spearmint Leaf (UIL-0687); Mint Sauce (UIL-0526)', 'Carriers, preservatives or emulsifiers depend on the supplied preparation. Extract alone does not establish an additive E-number.', 'https://www.mccormick.com/products/mccormick-pure-mint-extract-1-fl-oz | https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/peppermint-oil/about-peppermint-oil/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('horseradish-paste', 'UIL-0500', 'Horseradish Paste', 'Horseradish root paste; ground horseradish paste', 'Sauces, pastes and compound bases', 'Prepared root condiment', 'Ground horseradish root supplied as a paste, often with vinegar, water, salt or other ingredients. Recipes range from simple prepared root to compound wasabi-style pastes.', 'Horseradish root ground and combined with the specified preserving or flavour ingredients.', 'Pungent flavour and a convenient paste texture.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Root solids and any added oil, sugar or salt determine the contribution; a small condiment serving is not a whole-vegetable portion.', 'Usually limited at typical use levels; recipe-dependent.', 'Added oil varies; plain root and oil-based paste differ.', 'Root carbohydrate and any added sugars or starches vary.', 'Some root fibre may remain; amount depends on root proportion and serving.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Pungency does not establish an antimicrobial or digestive-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Horseradish root is not automatically the regulated mustard allergen. Compound pastes may contain MUSTARD, SOYA, WHEAT or other allergens; check the recipe.', 'People with horseradish or recipe-ingredient allergy, and anyone distinguishing root paste, creamy sauce and wasabi-style products.', 'Condiments, sauces, dressings, sandwich fillings and wasabi-style preparations.', 'Horseradish Paste; Horseradish root paste; ground horseradish paste', 'A suitable tolerated root preparation or condiment matched to the flavour need; true wasabi and horseradish are different plants.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in plain horseradish root; compound pastes may contain wheat-containing soya sauce or other gluten sources.', 'Context dependent', 'Prepared root ingredient requiring recipe and allergen context', 'Moderate', 'Identify the root and any compound ingredients accurately. Wasabi-style wording does not establish a product made solely from true wasabi.', 'Horseradish paste provides concentrated root flavour. Check additions, allergens and whether it is a simple paste or a compound wasabi-style product.', 'horseradish paste|horseradish root paste|ground horseradish paste', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Horseradish Sauce (UIL-0474)', 'Some preparations contain thickeners, colours, flavourings or preservatives; none is universal to every horseradish paste.', 'https://www.silverspringfoods.com/products/prepared-horseradish/ | https://biona.co.uk/products/biona-organic-wasabi-paste | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('sourdough-starter', 'UIL-0501', 'Sourdough Starter', 'Sourdough mother; sourdough levain; sourdough starter culture', 'Bakery and cereal bases', 'Fermented flour culture', 'A flour-and-liquid culture containing yeasts and lactic acid bacteria, used to begin dough fermentation. Flour source, recipe and culture activity vary.', 'Flour mixed with water or another specified liquid and maintained or supplied as a fermentation culture.', 'Leavening, acidity, flavour and fermentation in dough.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Mainly reflects the flour, liquid and inclusion level; fermentation changes some components but does not establish one fixed nutrient profile.', 'Cereal protein depends on flour; wheat-based starters retain wheat-allergen relevance.', 'Usually limited in a plain flour/water starter; recipe-dependent.', 'Contains flour carbohydrate with fermentation-dependent changes.', 'Depends on flour refinement and retained grain material.', 'No universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit follows from adding a starter.', 'Fermentation can change food components, but the starter name alone does not establish better tolerance or a probiotic benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Common starters contain WHEAT or RYE; other cereals and MILK can occur depending on the recipe. Identify the actual flour and liquid.', 'People with cereal allergy or coeliac disease, and anyone checking culture activity or a gluten-free claim.', 'Sourdough breads, bakery, pizza dough and fermented cereal preparations.', 'Sourdough Starter; Sourdough mother; sourdough levain; sourdough starter culture', 'A verified suitable gluten-free starter where needed, or another leavening system; flavour and processing requirements differ.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Wheat, rye or barley starters retain gluten relevance. Ordinary sourdough fermentation does not establish coeliac suitability.', 'Context dependent', 'Fermented culture requiring flour, recipe and activity context', 'High', 'Declare the actual cereal and any other required allergens. Sourdough wording does not by itself establish gluten-free or authorised health-claim status.', 'Sourdough starter begins dough fermentation. Check its flour, liquid and activity; the name alone does not establish gluten-free or probiotic suitability.', 'sourdough starter|sourdough mother|sourdough levain|sourdough starter culture', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Sourdough Culture (UIL-0346); Starter Culture (UIL-0372); Wheat Sourdough (UIL-0434); Rye Sourdough Starter (UIL-0527); Wheat Sourdough Starter (UIL-0553)', 'Carriers, stabilisers and other additions vary in commercial preparations; no additive E-number follows from starter.', 'https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/learn/guides/sourdough | https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/sourdough-starter-recipe | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance | https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/probiotics-usefulness-and-safety', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('lactobacillus-casei', 'UIL-0502', 'Lactobacillus Casei', 'Lacticaseibacillus casei', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Lactic-acid bacterial culture', 'A bacterial species now named Lacticaseibacillus casei, formerly Lactobacillus casei. Strain and preparation determine its technical and biological properties.', 'Cultured bacteria supplied in a specified live, dried or otherwise prepared form with product-specific carriers.', 'Fermentation or addition as a specified bacterial culture.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Generally added for culture function, not a meaningful macronutrient contribution; carriers may differ.', 'Not a meaningful protein source at usual culture-use levels.', 'Carrier-dependent; no fixed fat profile.', 'Carriers or substrates may contribute small amounts.', 'The bacterial name does not establish dietary fibre or a prebiotic.', 'No species-wide glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Any claimed benefit needs evidence for the exact strain, dose, viability and intended outcome; species identity alone is insufficient.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The bacterium is not itself a UK-regulated allergen. Milk or other allergens may be present in carriers or the supplied preparation.', 'People with carrier allergies and anyone assessing a claimed probiotic effect; higher-risk patients need product-specific clinical advice.', 'Fermented foods, culture preparations and some supplements.', 'Lactobacillus Casei; Lacticaseibacillus casei', 'A culture selected for the required function; evidence for another strain cannot be transferred by species name alone.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'Depends on the preparation, carriers and cross-contact; bacterial taxonomy alone does not establish gluten-free suitability.', 'Context dependent', 'Species-level culture requiring strain, taxonomy and viability context', 'Insufficient', 'Species identification does not establish an authorised health claim. Probiotic wording requires applicable claims compliance for the actual product.', 'Lactobacillus casei is now Lacticaseibacillus casei. Record the exact strain and preparation before assessing any claimed benefit.', 'lactobacillus casei|lacticaseibacillus casei', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Lactic Acid Bacteria Culture (UIL-0242); Starter Culture (UIL-0372); Lactobacillus Plantarum (UIL-0476)', 'Carriers and protective ingredients vary; no additive E-number follows from the species name.', 'https://lpsn.dsmz.de/species/lacticaseibacillus-casei | https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/probiotics-usefulness-and-safety | https://www.asa.org.uk/advice-online/food-probiotic-claims.html | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('d-alpha-tocopherol', 'UIL-0503', 'D-Alpha-Tocopherol', 'D-alpha tocopherol; RRR-alpha-tocopherol; RRR alpha tocopherol', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Specific vitamin E form', 'The RRR stereoisomer of alpha-tocopherol, commonly labelled d-alpha-tocopherol. It differs from synthetic all-rac/DL forms and from tocopheryl esters.', 'A manufactured vitamin E ingredient, commonly naturally sourced; actual source, purity and carriers require confirmation.', 'Vitamin E fortification or supplementation and, in suitable preparations, antioxidant function.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Provides vitamin E activity at a known dose; activity comparisons require the correct form and conversion.', 'Not a protein ingredient.', 'A fat-soluble vitamin, not a meaningful serving of dietary fat; oil carriers can contribute fat.', 'None inherent in the pure compound; carriers may contribute.', 'None in the pure compound.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in the pure chemical identity. Check oil sources, carriers, residual-protein specifications and capsules.', 'People taking high-dose vitamin E or anticoagulant medicines need clinical assessment of supplement exposure; food fortification is a different exposure.', 'Vitamin premixes, fortified foods, supplements and specified antioxidant preparations.', 'D-Alpha-Tocopherol; D-alpha tocopherol; RRR-alpha-tocopherol; RRR alpha tocopherol', 'Another permitted vitamin E form with appropriate activity conversion and formulation; equal ingredient mass need not provide equal vitamin activity.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Specific vitamin E stereoisomer requiring identity and dose context', 'High', 'The GB vitamin/mineral register lists d-alpha-tocopherol. Nutrient-source and antioxidant-additive uses have separate applicable conditions.', 'D-alpha-tocopherol is a specific vitamin E form. Keep it distinct from DL forms and esters, and assess dose and carriers.', 'd-alpha-tocopherol|d-alpha tocopherol|rrr-alpha-tocopherol|rrr alpha tocopherol', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Vitamin E (UIL-0451); DL-Alpha-Tocopheryl Acetate (UIL-0477)', 'Alpha-tocopherol is listed as E307 for additive use, but E307 alone does not establish RRR stereochemistry or source. Do not merge tocopherol-rich extract (E306) or tocopheryl acetate with this identity.', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/VitaminE-HealthProfessional/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('magnesium-sulphate', 'UIL-0504', 'Magnesium Sulphate', 'Magnesium sulfate; magnesium sulphate heptahydrate; magnesium sulfate heptahydrate; Epsom salt (food-grade heptahydrate)', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Magnesium mineral salt', 'A magnesium salt supplied in specified hydration states. The heptahydrate is known as Epsom salt; food-grade material is distinct from bath or technical products.', 'Purified mineral-salt manufacture; source, hydration and food-grade specification need confirmation.', 'A magnesium nutrient source and specified manufacturing functions where the intended use is permitted.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Can supply elemental magnesium; total salt weight is not the elemental-magnesium dose.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'None in the pure salt; blends may contain carriers.', 'None in the pure salt.', 'No generic glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Higher oral supplemental or medicinal exposure can cause diarrhoea; this does not describe every food-use exposure.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in the pure mineral salt; assess the supplied preparation.', 'People with impaired kidney function or interacting medicines need clinical advice before supplementation. Bath salts must not be assumed suitable for oral use.', 'Specified mineral premixes, fortified products and other preparations subject to their intended-use requirements.', 'Magnesium Sulphate; Magnesium sulfate; magnesium sulphate heptahydrate; magnesium sulfate heptahydrate; Epsom salt (food-grade heptahydrate)', 'Another permitted magnesium source matched to the application; elemental content, dose and technological function differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Mineral source requiring grade, hydration and intended-use checks', 'High', 'The GB vitamin/mineral register lists magnesium sulphate. The FSA approved-additive overview reviewed does not list E518; a nutrient-source listing or JECFA INS number does not establish general UK food-additive permission.', 'Magnesium sulphate can provide magnesium in an appropriate preparation. Check food grade, hydration, elemental dose and the legal basis for the intended use.', 'magnesium sulphate|magnesium sulfate|magnesium sulphate heptahydrate|magnesium sulfate heptahydrate', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Magnesium Chloride (UIL-0478); Magnesium Oxide (UIL-0400); Magnesium Citrate (UIL-0426); Magnesium Carbonate (UIL-0452)', 'JECFA identifies magnesium sulfate as INS 518. Do not treat that international identifier as proof of current UK E518 authorisation; additive and nutrient-source permissions require separate assessment.', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/register-on-adding-vitamins-and-minerals-to-foods/great-britain-register-on-the-addition-of-vitamins-and-minerals-and-of-certain-other-substances-to-foods | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers | https://www.fao.org/fileadmin/user_upload/jecfa_additives/docs/monograph4/additive-268-m4.pdf | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/magnesium-healthprofessional/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('l-histidine', 'UIL-0505', 'L-Histidine', 'L histidine; L-histidine amino acid', 'Amino acids and functional nutrition', 'Essential amino acid', 'The L form of histidine, one of the amino acids humans need from dietary sources.', 'Manufactured and purified to a specified grade; production route and carriers require confirmation.', 'Amino-acid composition in specified nutritional and food formulations.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Provides one essential amino acid; it does not replace a balanced protein source.', 'A free amino acid, not an intact or complete protein.', 'None in the pure compound.', 'None in the pure compound; carriers may contribute.', 'None in the pure compound.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'No UK-regulated allergen inherent in the pure amino-acid identity; check carriers and relevant residual-source specifications.', 'Anyone using isolated-amino-acid supplements or specialist nutritional formulas should assess dose and the complete formulation.', 'Specified amino-acid mixtures, nutritional formulations and supplements.', 'L-Histidine; L histidine; L-histidine amino acid', 'A complete dietary protein or an appropriately formulated amino-acid mixture, depending on the purpose.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Isolated essential amino acid requiring grade and dose context', 'High', 'Food suitability and permission depend on the grade, product category and intended use. Injectable or feed specifications do not alone establish food permission.', 'L-histidine is an essential amino acid. Its isolated form needs grade and formulation checks and is not a complete protein.', 'l-histidine|l histidine|l-histidine amino acid', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'L-Threonine (UIL-0479); L-Leucine (UIL-0323); L-Isoleucine (UIL-0349)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.ajihealthandnutrition.com/product/l-histidine/ | https://ajiaminoscience.eu/aminoacid/product/l-histidine/ | https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/ExerciseAndAthleticPerformance-HealthProfessional/', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('carrot-juice', 'UIL-0506', 'Carrot Juice', 'Pressed carrot juice; carrot juice ingredient', 'Water and liquid bases', 'Vegetable juice', 'Juice extracted from carrots, supplied plain or as a specified preparation. Concentrate, puree and blended drinks are different products.', 'Carrots pressed or otherwise processed to recover juice; pulp retention, heat treatment and additions vary.', 'Carrot flavour, colour, liquid and vegetable solids.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Can contribute carotenoids such as beta-carotene and juice sugars; amounts depend on variety, processing and use level.', 'Not a concentrated protein ingredient.', 'Usually little fat in plain carrot juice.', 'Contains juice sugars, which count as free sugars; blends can add other sugars.', 'Usually less fibre than whole carrots; pulp retention changes the amount.', 'Assess sugars and portion; no universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned to generic carrot juice.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Carrot allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check blends and other ingredients.', 'People with carrot allergy or sensitivity, and anyone assessing free sugars or whole-vegetable equivalence.', 'Drinks, soups, sauces, bakery and foods using carrot flavour or colour.', 'Carrot Juice; Pressed carrot juice; carrot juice ingredient', 'Whole carrots, puree or another specified liquid where appropriate; water, fibre and texture differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Vegetable juice requiring preparation and portion context', 'High', 'Use an accurate juice description and identify added ingredients. Nutrient or health claims require the actual composition and applicable conditions.', 'Carrot juice supplies carrot flavour, colour and juice sugars. It differs from whole carrots, puree and concentrate, especially in fibre and dilution.', 'carrot juice|pressed carrot juice', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Vegetable Juice (UIL-0454); Carrot Concentrate (UIL-0177); Carrot Puree (UIL-0563); Carrot Powder (UIL-0589); Carrot Fibre (UIL-0615)', 'Preservatives, acidity regulators or other additions depend on the preparation; carrot''s colour does not automatically establish a colour-additive E-number.', 'https://www.rabenhorst.de/en/our-juices/organic-carrot-juice/ | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/how-does-sugar-in-our-diet-affect-our-health/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('dill-seed', 'UIL-0507', 'Dill Seed', 'Dill seeds; dill fruit; whole dill seed', 'Herbs, spices and seasonings', 'Culinary spice', 'The dried fruit of the dill plant, commonly called dill seed. It is distinct from the leafy herb called dill weed.', 'Harvested dill fruits, dried and supplied whole or crushed.', 'Aromatic spice flavour in pickles, breads and savoury dishes.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Contains seed/fruit solids, but small seasoning portions limit macronutrient and mineral contribution.', 'Not a main protein source at usual seasoning portions.', 'Contains aromatic components and some fat; not a dietary-oil serving.', 'Contains plant carbohydrate; contribution depends on the small use level.', 'Some plant fibre, generally a small amount per seasoning portion.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Traditional digestive use does not establish a clinical gut-treatment benefit from the spice.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Dill allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Blends may contain regulated allergens.', 'People with dill allergy and anyone distinguishing the seed spice from dill leaf or a concentrated oil.', 'Pickling blends, breads, soups, curries, seafood recipes and savoury seasoning.', 'Dill Seed; Dill seeds; dill fruit; whole dill seed', 'A tolerated herb or spice suited to the dish; dill weed has a different flavour and concentration.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Culinary spice requiring plant-part and use-level context', 'High', 'Describe the seed/fruit spice and any blend ingredients accurately. Traditional use is not an authorised health claim.', 'Dill seed is an aromatic spice from the dill plant''s fruit. Keep it distinct from dill weed and concentrated essential-oil products.', 'dill seed|dill seeds|dill fruit|whole dill seed', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Dill Weed (UIL-0533); Cumin (UIL-0215)', 'None inherent in the plain ingredient; assess the full formulation.', 'https://www.mccormick.com/products/mccormick-r-dill-seed-0-85-oz | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
