  ('soy-sauce', 'UIL-0509', 'Soy Sauce', 'Soya sauce; shoyu; soy sauce seasoning', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Soya-based savoury condiment', 'A savoury liquid seasoning made from soya ingredients, commonly by fermentation with wheat, water and salt. Recipes and production methods vary.', 'Soya beans or soya-derived ingredients with the stated cereals, salt and other additions.', 'Salty, savoury flavour, aroma and colour.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually a significant salt contribution at condiment concentrations; sugars and other nutrients vary by recipe.', 'Contains soya-derived components but is not a main protein serving at normal condiment portions.', 'Usually little fat in plain sauce.', 'Wheat processing and added sugar or syrup influence carbohydrate; sweet sauces differ.', 'Not equivalent to whole soya-bean fibre.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned; assess any added sugars and portion.', 'Fermented does not automatically mean live probiotic, gluten-free or suitable for every digestive sensitivity.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains SOYA. Many standard recipes also contain WHEAT; identify the actual cereal and other allergens.', 'People with soya or wheat allergy, coeliac disease, or salt restrictions; check the exact product.', 'Asian-style cooking, marinades, dressings, sauces, soups and prepared foods.', 'Soy Sauce; Soya sauce; shoyu; soy sauce seasoning', 'A verified suitable wheat-free/gluten-free sauce where needed; tamari is not automatically gluten-free or free of soya.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'Common wheat-based soy sauces contain gluten. Fermentation alone does not establish gluten-free suitability; verify the actual product.', 'Context dependent', 'Soya condiment requiring cereal, salt and recipe context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise soya and any wheat or other regulated allergens. Gluten-free and reduced-salt claims require product-specific compliance.', 'Soy sauce adds savoury flavour and salt. It contains soya and often wheat; check the exact recipe and gluten-free status.', 'soy sauce|soya sauce|shoyu|soy sauce seasoning', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Light Soy Sauce (UIL-0535); Dark Soy Sauce (UIL-0561); Soy Sauce Powder (UIL-0863)', 'Preservatives, sweeteners, colours or other additions vary. Fermentation-derived glutamate does not establish added MSG (E621).', 'https://www.kikkoman.co.uk/industrial/liquid-soy-sauce/soy-sauce-standard | https://www.kikkoman.com/en/cookbook/glossary/soysauce.html | https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/food-types/salt-in-your-diet/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('peach-powder', 'UIL-0510', 'Peach Powder', 'Peach fruit powder; dried peach powder; freeze-dried peach powder', 'Fruit ingredients', 'Dried fruit ingredient', 'A peach-derived dried powder. Whole-fruit/puree powders and juice-based powders with carriers have different compositions.', 'Peach material dried and milled or otherwise powdered; starting material, drying method and carriers depend on the grade.', 'Peach flavour, colour and fruit solids in dry or formulated foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Concentrates peach-derived solids; sugars, fibre and micronutrients depend on the fruit fraction, drying and carriers.', 'Not usually a concentrated protein source.', 'Usually limited in plain fruit powder; carriers or blends can differ.', 'Contains peach sugars; juice-derived grades and added carriers need separate assessment.', 'Whole-fruit/puree grades can retain fibre; clarified juice powders may contain much less.', 'Assess sugar, carrier and portion; no universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Peach allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check carriers, blends and cross-contact.', 'People with peach allergy, and anyone checking whether the powder is pure fruit or a carrier-based preparation.', 'Bakery, confectionery, desserts, drink mixes, fillings and dry food blends.', 'Peach Powder; Peach fruit powder; dried peach powder; freeze-dried peach powder', 'Peach puree, dried peach or another specified peach ingredient where the recipe permits; water, fibre and flavour strength differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Fruit powder requiring fruit-fraction and carrier context', 'Moderate', 'Pure-fruit, no-added-sugar and nutrient claims must reflect the actual specification. Powder alone does not establish a drying method or fruit percentage.', 'Peach powder adds peach solids and flavour. Confirm whether it is whole-fruit, puree-based or juice/carrier-based before assigning nutrients.', 'peach powder|peach fruit powder|dried peach powder|freeze-dried peach powder', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'Peach Puree (UIL-0458); Peach Juice Concentrate (UIL-0484); Dried Peach (UIL-0536)', 'Carriers, anti-caking agents, preservatives or other additions depend on the grade; none is universal to plain dried peach.', 'https://sheersuperfood.com/product/freeze-dried-peach-powder/ | https://chaucerfoods.com/products/freeze-dried/powder/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses/allergen-guidance-for-food-businesses', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('yam-powder', 'UIL-0511', 'Yam Powder', 'Yam flour; dried yam powder; Dioscorea tuber powder', 'Vegetable ingredients', 'Dried edible-yam ingredient', 'Powder or flour made from edible yam tubers in the Dioscorea genus. Whole-tuber powder differs from isolated starch and concentrated wild-yam extracts.', 'Specified edible yam tubers dried and milled, sometimes after a preparatory cooking step; species and process vary.', 'Starchy solids, thickening, texture and yam flavour in foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Usually starch-rich, with variable fibre, protein and micronutrients from the retained tuber material.', 'Contains some tuber protein; not a protein isolate.', 'Usually limited in a plain yam flour.', 'Mainly starch; species, cooking and formulation affect digestion.', 'Retained tuber fibre depends on peeling and refinement; not equivalent to purified yam starch.', 'No universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established prebiotic or gut-treatment effect assigned; grade and preparation affect tolerance.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Yam allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check blends and cross-contact.', 'People with yam allergy and anyone checking edible species, food grade or cooking requirements.', 'Pounded-yam preparations, bakery, soups, cereal mixtures and dry food blends.', 'Yam Powder; Yam flour; dried yam powder; Dioscorea tuber powder', 'Another suitable tuber flour matched to texture and dietary needs; sweet potato is a different botanical source.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Dried tuber ingredient requiring species and preparation context', 'Moderate', 'Identify the actual edible yam and any added ingredients. Food-grade flour and concentrated botanical extracts have 