  ('pea-fibre', 'UIL-0515', 'Pea Fibre', 'Pea fiber; pea hull fibre; pea hull fiber; inner pea fibre', 'Legumes and pulse derivatives', 'Pea-derived fibre fraction', 'A fibre-containing ingredient from peas, including hull-derived and inner-cell-wall grades. These fractions can retain different amounts of starch and protein.', 'Pea material separated, milled or otherwise processed to recover a specified fibre fraction.', 'Fibre enrichment, water/fat binding and texture adjustment.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Provides fibre with variable residual starch, protein and other pea components.', 'May retain pea protein; fibre separation does not establish removal of pea-allergy relevance.', 'Residual fat varies by fraction and process.', 'Inner-fibre grades can retain starch; pea fibre does not automatically mean carbohydrate-free.', 'Amount, particle size and soluble/insoluble characteristics depend on the grade.', 'No generic glucose-treatment effect assigned.', 'Fibre properties, dose and individual tolerance matter; no automatic prebiotic or gut-treatment claim assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pea allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Do not assume a fibre ingredient is free of allergenic pea protein.', 'People with pea allergy or sensitivity to concentrated fibre, and anyone checking inner versus hull fibre.', 'Bakery, savoury foods, meat/plant-based formulations and other fibre-containing foods.', 'Pea Fibre; Pea fiber; pea hull fibre; pea hull fiber; inner pea fibre', 'A tolerated fibre matched to texture and water-binding requirements; other pulse fibres need separate allergen assessment.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Processed pulse fibre requiring fraction and composition context', 'Moderate', 'Use the actual ingr