  ('cashew-flour', 'UIL-0516', 'Cashew Flour', 'Cashew nut flour; cashew meal; ground cashew flour', 'Nut and seed derivatives', 'Ground cashew-kernel ingredient', 'Cashew kernels processed into flour or meal. Full-fat ground kernels and partly defatted flours have different compositions.', 'Food-grade cashew kernels milled, with roasting and oil removal depending on the grade.', 'Nut flavour, flour solids, texture and protein contribution.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Contains cashew protein, fat, carbohydrate and fibre in grade-dependent proportions.', 'Contains cashew protein; defatting can increase its proportion.', 'Whole-kernel flour retains substantial nut fat; partly defatted flour contains less.', 'Contains cashew carbohydrate; not automatically carbohydrate-free.', 'Contains kernel fibre, with concentration affected by processing.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'No established gut-treatment effect assigned.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Contains CASHEW, a regulated tree-nut allergen. Milling, roasting or partial defatting does not establish suitability for cashew allergy.', 'People with cashew allergy and anyone comparing whole-kernel and defatted flours.', 'Bakery, sauces, nut-based foods, coatings and plant-based formulations.', 'Cashew Flour; Cashew nut flour; cashew meal; ground cashew flour', 'A tolerated nut-free flour matched to the recipe; another tree nut is not automatically appropriate for cashew allergy.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Tree-nut flour requiring allergen and defatting context', 'High', 'Declare and emphasise cashew. Flour alone does not establish a fat or protein percentage, or gluten-free certification.', 'Cashew flour contributes cashew solids and remains a cashew allergen. Confirm whether it is whole-ke