  ('pork-gelatine', 'UIL-0520', 'Pork Gelatine', 'Pork gelatin; porcine gelatine; porcine gelatin', 'Meat and poultry ingredients', 'Porcine collagen-derived gelling protein', 'Gelatine obtained by processing collagen-rich pig tissues. It differs from intact meat protein and from more extensively hydrolysed collagen-peptide preparations.', 'Food-grade porcine collagen-rich materials, commonly skin, processed, extracted and purified to the supplied gelatine grade.', 'Gelling, thickening, stabilisation, texture and suitable capsule manufacture.', 'Refined ingredient', 'A collagen-derived protein ingredient with a characteristic amino-acid balance; use level determines its nutritional contribution.', 'Provides protein but is not a balanced complete-protein substitute for whole egg or lean meat.', 'Usually little fat in purified gelatine.', 'Little carbohydrate in pure gelatine; sweetened gels and premixes differ.', 'None in pure gelatine.', 'No glucose-treatment benefit assigned.', 'Gelling or collagen origin does not establish a gut-healing or digestive-treatment effect.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Gelatine/porcine allergy is possible outside the UK list of 14 regulated allergens. Check additives, carriers and the complete food.', 'People avoiding pork for dietary or religious reasons, people with relevant allergy, and those evaluating protein quality or a capsule''s source.', 'Gelled desserts, confectionery, bakery, dairy preparations, meat products and capsules.', 'Pork Gelatine; Pork gelatin; porcine gelatine; porcine gelatin', 'A suitable non-animal gelling ingredient for dietary needs; agar or pectin have different texture and processing requirements.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Animal-derived gelling protein requiring species and grade