  ('vitamin-k1', 'UIL-0529', 'Vitamin K1', 'Phylloquinone; phytomenadione; phytonadione; vitamin K 1', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Fat-soluble vitamin K1', 'Vitamin K1, also called phylloquinone; distinct from the vitamin K2 menaquinones and from menadione (K3).', 'A specified food-grade K1 preparation; manufacturing route, strength and carriers require supplier confirmation.', 'Vitamin fortification and supplement formulations where the form and use are permitted.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'An essential micronutrient involved in normal blood clotting and bone-protein function; contribution depends on the actual K1 amount.', 'Not a protein source; any protein-containing carrier needs separate assessment.', 'Fat-soluble does not mean the vitamin itself is a dietary-fat serving; oil carriers may contribute fat.', 'Only carriers or other formulation components contribute meaningful carbohydrate.', 'Not a dietary fibre source.', 'Its clotting function is not a blood-glucose-lowering effect; no generic glycaemic claim.', 'Not a probiotic; gut-bacterial production of some K forms does not establish a K1 supplement gut benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'K1 itself is not one of the UK 14 allergens; check oils, carriers, capsule materials and other components.', 'People taking warfarin or similar vitamin-K-antagonist medicines; changes in vitamin K intake need clinician-guided management.', 'Fortified foods, vitamin premixes and supplements.', 'Vitamin K1; Phylloquinone; phytomenadione; phytonadione; vitamin K 1', 'Another permitted K1 preparation for the intended use; K2 and K3 are not automatic equivalents.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Added vitamin; assess chemical form, amount and carrier', 'High', 'Check the permitted vitamin form a