  ('iron', 'UIL-0530', 'Iron', 'Dietary iron; added iron', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Essential mineral nutrient', 'The nutrient iron; this broad term does not identify the chemical form used in a food or supplement.', 'Specified iron salts, elemental preparations or other permitted sources; haem-derived preparations require an animal-source check.', 'Mineral fortification and supplement formulations; function and permitted use depend on form.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'An essential micronutrient in haemoglobin and oxygen transport; elemental iron amount, form and diet affect its contribution.', 'Iron itself is not protein; a haem-derived or protein-containing preparation needs separate assessment.', 'No meaningful fat in pure mineral material; carriers vary.', 'No meaningful carbohydrate in pure mineral material; carriers vary.', 'Not a dietary fibre source.', 'Haemoglobin and oxygen-transport roles do not establish a blood-glucose benefit or diagnose iron deficiency.', 'Some supplemental forms and doses cause gastrointestinal effects; the generic name does not establish one tolerance profile.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Iron itself is not one of the UK 14 allergens; assess source preparations, residues and carriers.', 'People taking iron supplements, with iron-overload disorders or relevant medicine interactions; form and elemental dose matter.', 'Fortified cereals, flour, nutrition products, mineral premixes and supplements.', 'Iron; Dietary iron; added iron', 'An appropriately assessed permitted iron source; chemical forms are not interchangeable by equal ingredient weight.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Mineral term requiring chemical-form and dose identification', 'High', 'Verify the authorised iron source for the product and