  ('l-arginine', 'UIL-0531', 'L-Arginine', 'L arginine; arginine', 'Amino acids and functional nutrition', 'Free amino acid', 'The L-form of arginine, an amino acid used in protein formation and other body processes; the body can also make it.', 'A specified food-grade amino-acid preparation; production route, purity and any carriers require confirmation.', 'Amino-acid and nutrition formulations, subject to the intended use and product rules.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Supplies a single amino acid; it is not a complete protein or a replacement for a balanced protein intake.', 'Free arginine is not an intact protein and does not supply all indispensable amino acids.', 'Little fat in pure material; blends vary.', 'Little carbohydrate in pure material; carriers vary.', 'Not a dietary fibre source.', 'No generic blood-glucose-lowering claim. A role in nitric-oxide synthesis does not establish a treatment effect from supplementation.', 'Not a probiotic; supplemental doses may cause gastrointestinal effects, with tolerance depending on amount and formulation.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pure arginine is not one of the UK 14 allergens; assess production residues, carriers and other ingredients.', 'People using amino-acid supplements or medicines; concentrated supplemental use needs product-specific suitability assessment.', 'Amino-acid blends, supplements and specialised nutrition formulations.', 'L-Arginine; L arginine; arginine', 'An appropriately assessed amino-acid formulation for the intended purpose; whole proteins and other amino acids are not direct equivalents.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Isolated amino acid; assess form and use', 'High', 'Confirm food-grade identity and lawful use in the relevant product category. Performance or health claims need their own applicable evidence and authorisation.', 'L-arginine is a single amino acid that the body can also make. Its presence does not establish a complete protein or an exercise benefit.', 'l-arginine|l arginine|arginine', 'None specifically validated; spelling corrections must not override exact ingredient/allergen matching.', 'L-Citrulline (UIL-0557); L-Lysine (UIL-0401); L-Glutamine (UIL-0583)', 'No additive E-number follows from L-arginine; separately identify carriers or other formulation ingredients.', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/ExerciseAndAthleticPerformance-HealthProfessional/ | https://www.ajihealthandnutrition.com/product/l-arginine/ | https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance/food-allergen-labelling-and-information-requirements-technical-guidance', '2026-10-16', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('beetroot-juice', 'UIL-0532', 'Beetroot Juice', 'Beet juice; red beetroot juice; red beet juice', 'Water and liquid bases', 'Vegetable juice', 'Juice expressed or extracted from edible beetroot; plain juice, concentrate and mixed drinks are different preparations.', 'Beetroot (Beta vulgaris) processed to separate juice; concentration, heat treatment and blending vary.', 'Drink base, beetroot flavour and colour in foods.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Provides water and sugars with variable other constituents; juice is not nutritionally equivalent to whole beetroot.', 'Usually a limited protein contribution; check the product.', 'Usually little fat in plain juice.', 'Contains free sugars from the juice, even without separately added sugar.', 'Usually less fibre than whole beetroot; pulp retention varies.', 'Assess sugars and serving size. No universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit follows from the name.', 'Not automatically probiotic; juice, pulp and any fermentation need separate assessment.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Beetroot allergy is possible although outside the UK 14 allergens; check blends and other ingredients.', 'People checking free sugars, nitrate amount or concentrated juice products; actual composition and serving matter.', 'Vegetable juices, smoothies, juice blends and foods using beetroot juice for colour or flavour.', 'Beetroot Juice; Beet juice; red beetroot juice; red beet juice', 'Whole beetroot for a different fibre profile, or a suitable vegetable juice; culinary and nutritional functions differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Vegetable juice; concentration and blending matter', 'High', 'Verify juice identity and formulation; nitrate, nutrition or health statements need actual product data and applicable claim cond