  ('light-soy-sauce', 'UIL-0535', 'Light Soy Sauce', 'Light soya sauce; Chinese light soy sauce; light-style soy sauce', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Fermented soya condiment', 'A light-style soy sauce used chiefly for savoury seasoning; light describes the sauce style, not an assurance of reduced salt.', 'A specified fermented soya preparation, commonly including wheat, salt and water; recipes differ.', 'Savoury and umami flavour in marinades, sauces, stir-fries and dips.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually contributes salt at condiment servings; protein, sugars and other components depend on the formulation.', 'Contains soya-derived components; not a standard protein serving at ordinary use levels.', 'Usually little fat; recipe-dependent.', 'Sugars or other carbohydrate depend on recipe and fermentation.', 'Usually little fibre; not equivalent to whole soya beans.', 'No fixed glycaemic index or glucose-control benefit; assess actual recipe and use.', 'Fermentation does not establish a live probiotic product or digestive-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'SOYA; WHEAT is common in conventional light soy sauce. Fermentation does not automatically remove cereal-allergen relevance.', 'People with soya or wheat allergy, coeliac disease or salt-intake concerns.', 'Marinades, stir-fries, dips, dressings and savoury sauces.', 'Light Soy Sauce; Light soya sauce; Chinese light soy sauce; light-style soy sauce', 'A verified suitable gluten-free or reduced-salt sauce when needed; these are separate specifications and may still contain soya.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'Conventional grades commonly contain wheat; use specific compliant gluten-free product evidence. Light style does not establish gluten-free status.', 'Context dependent', 'Fermented condiment; style, allergens and salt need context', 'High', 'Declare SOYA and WHEAT where present. Gluten-free