  ('dried-peach', 'UIL-0536', 'Dried Peach', 'Dried peaches; dehydrated peach; dehydrated peaches', 'Fruit ingredients', 'Dried fruit', 'Peach flesh with much of its water removed; it may be plain, sulphited, sweetened or otherwise treated.', 'Peaches dried as pieces, slices or halves; pretreatment and retained moisture vary.', 'Fruit flavour, sweetness and texture in snacks, bakery, cereals and desserts.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Drying concentrates sugars and energy per gram and retains some fibre; actual values depend on moisture and additions.', 'Not usually a major protein source.', 'Usually little fat unless oil or another ingredient is added.', 'Naturally present fruit sugars are concentrated. Added sugar or syrup needs separate assessment; intact dried-fruit sugars are not all automatically free sugars.', 'Retained fruit tissue supplies fibre; amount depends on the preparation.', 'Carbohydrate amount and portion matter; no universal glycaemic index or glucose-lowering benefit.', 'Fibre and amount may affect tolerance; no generic probiotic or gut-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Peach allergy is possible. SULPHITES require declaration when above the applicable threshold; their presence is not universal.', 'People with peach allergy or sulphite sensitivity, and those checking added sugar and portions.', 'Dried-fruit mixes, cereals, snack bars, bakery and desserts.', 'Dried Peach; Dried peaches; dehydrated peach; dehydrated peaches', 'Fresh peach or another suitably assessed fruit; water, texture, sugar concentration and allergens differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Dried fruit; assess sweetening and preservation separately', 'High', 'Check the actual recipe and declare sulphur dioxide/sulphites above 10 mg/kg or 10 mg/L, exp