  ('cellulose-fibre', 'UIL-0549', 'Cellulose Fibre', 'Cellulose fiber; cellulosic fibre; cellulosic fiber', 'Fibres and prebiotic ingredients', 'Cellulose-based plant fibre', 'A cellulose-based fibre ingredient from plant material. The generic term does not distinguish powdered cellulose, microcrystalline material or a broader plant-fibre preparation.', 'Specified plant-derived cellulose, separated and processed to the declared food-grade form.', 'Fibre enrichment, bulking, water management, texture or powder handling, depending on grade.', 'Refined ingredient', 'Mainly a fibre/structural contribution; purity and other constituents require specification.', 'Purified cellulose is not a protein source; residual components vary in less-purified preparations.', 'Little fat in purified cellulose.', 'Cellulose is a carbohydrate polymer but is not digested like ordinary starch by human digestive enzymes.', 'Predominantly insoluble fibre; verify actual identity, measured content and any nutrition-claim conditions.', 'Do not count pure cellulose as equivalent to digestible glucose; no generic glucose-lowering claim established.', 'Can contribute to stool bulk; fermentation and tolerance depend on the grade and amount. The name alone does not prove a specific prebiotic effect.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pure cellulose is not one of the UK 14 allergens. Starting-material residues, blends and cross-contact require assessment.', 'People checking fibre tolerance, source residues or whether the material is a named food additive.', 'Fibre-enriched foods, bakery, dry mixes and selected texture/anti-caking systems.', 'Cellulose Fibre; Cellulose fiber; cellulosic fibre; cellulosic fiber', 'Another specified fibre or texturising system; physical and digestive properties differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need sepa