  ('dark-soy-sauce', 'UIL-0561', 'Dark Soy Sauce', 'Dark soya sauce; Chinese dark soy sauce; dark-style soy sauce', 'Vinegars and fermented condiments', 'Fermented soya condiment', 'A dark-style soy sauce used for colour and savoury flavour; recipe, sweetness, salt and thickness vary.', 'A specified fermented soya preparation, commonly including wheat, salt and water, with recipe-dependent additions.', 'Deep colour and savoury flavour in marinades, stews, stir-fries and sauces.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Usually contributes salt at condiment servings; sugar and other components depend on the formulation.', 'Contains soya-derived components; not a standard protein serving at ordinary use levels.', 'Usually little fat; recipe-dependent.', 'Added sugars, syrups or other carbohydrate vary by recipe.', 'Usually little fibre; not equivalent to whole soya beans.', 'No fixed glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit; assess the recipe and portion.', 'Fermentation does not establish live probiotic organisms or improved digestion in the finished sauce.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'SOYA; WHEAT is common in conventional dark soy sauce. Fermentation does not automatically remove cereal-allergen relevance.', 'People with soya or wheat allergy, coeliac disease or concerns about salt and added sugars.', 'Marinades, braised dishes, noodles, stir-fries and savoury sauces.', 'Dark Soy Sauce; Dark soya sauce; Chinese dark soy sauce; dark-style soy sauce', 'A verified suitable sauce for the intended dietary need; light, reduced-salt and gluten-free are different specifications.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'Conventional grades commonly contain wheat; use specific compliant gluten-free product evidence.', 'Context dependent', 'Fermented condiment; style and recipe matter', 'High', 'Declare SOYA and WHEAT where present. Dark style does not establish a reduced-salt, gluten-free or health