  ('fava-bean', 'UIL-0567', 'Fava Bean', 'Faba bean; broad bean; broad beans; fava beans; faba beans', 'Legumes and pulse derivatives', 'Food legume', 'The edible bean of Vicia faba, known as fava, faba or broad bean; fresh, dried and cooked forms differ.', 'Food-grade fava/broad-bean seeds, supplied fresh, dried, split, cooked or otherwise specified.', 'Plant protein, starch, texture and flavour in meals and ingredient preparations.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Provides protein, carbohydrate and fibre; water content makes fresh, dried and cooked values very different.', 'A plant-protein food; not equivalent to a fava-protein isolate or a fixed amino-acid serving.', 'Usually a relatively limited contribution in plain beans; added fats change this.', 'Contains starch and other carbohydrate; preparation and portion matter.', 'Retained bean tissue supplies fibre; dehulling or fractionation changes it.', 'No universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit follows from the name.', 'Fibre and fermentable components can affect individual tolerance; no generic probiotic or gut-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Fava/broad bean can cause allergy although outside the UK 14 allergens. It is distinct from the separate G6PD-related favism risk.', 'People with G6PD deficiency should avoid fava/broad beans in line with clinical advice because they can trigger haemolysis. Also relevant to people with fava-bean allergy.', 'Bean dishes, soups, salads, dips and other legume-based foods.', 'Fava Bean; Faba bean; broad bean; broad beans; fava beans; faba beans', 'Another suitable protein food chosen for the individual''s needs; do not generalise the fava/G6PD warning to every legume.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Whole legume; preparation and G6PD-rel