  ('quail-egg', 'UIL-0571', 'Quail Egg', 'Quail eggs; quail''s egg; quails'' eggs', 'Egg ingredients', 'Whole avian egg', 'An egg laid by a quail, supplied whole or as a specified preparation; egg size and edible portion differ from hen eggs.', 'Food-grade quail eggs, with shell, white and yolk preparations distinguished where relevant.', 'Protein, binding, emulsification, structure, flavour and appearance in foods.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Provides protein and fat with other nutrients; composition per egg depends on size and preparation.', 'Contains egg proteins; do not copy a hen-egg serving or fixed amino-acid values.', 'Mainly associated with yolk; whole-egg and white-only preparations differ.', 'Usually little carbohydrate in plain whole egg.', 'Plain egg does not supply dietary fibre.', 'No fixed glycaemic index or blood-glucose-treatment benefit follows from this name.', 'No established probiotic or gut-treatment benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'EGG: quail egg is covered by egg-allergen requirements. It is not automatically safe for someone with hen-egg allergy.', 'People with egg allergy and anyone preparing raw or lightly cooked dishes; quail eggs need thorough cooking.', 'Cooked egg dishes, salads, bakery, desserts and pickled-egg preparations.', 'Quail Egg; Quail eggs; quail''s egg; quails'' eggs', 'An appropriately assessed egg or egg-replacement system; allergy and functional properties differ.', 'Not vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Whole egg; assess species and preparation', 'High', 'Declare EGG where required. Current FSA advice says quail eggs should be cooked thoroughly and not used in raw or lightly cooked dishes.', 'Quail eggs provide protein and fat and contain the egg allergen. Cook them thoroughly; hen-egg assurance advice i