  ('anchovy', 'UIL-0573', 'Anchovy', 'Anchovies; anchovy fish', 'Fish and seafood ingredients', 'Oily fish', 'An anchovy fish ingredient; whole fish, fillets, salt-cured fish and paste are different preparations.', 'A specified anchovy species supplied fresh, frozen, cooked, cured or packed as declared.', 'Fish protein, flavour and texture; cured preparations are also used for concentrated savoury flavour.', 'Whole/minimally processed', 'Provides fish protein and fat including omega-3 fats; curing, bones, oil and serving size affect composition.', 'Fish protein; amount depends on edible portion and preparation.', 'Contains fish fats; added packing oil can materially change the overall profile.', 'Little carbohydrate in plain fish; sauces or other ingredients can add it.', 'Plain fish does not supply dietary fibre.', 'No universal glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit follows from this name.', 'Curing or fermentation does not automatically establish a probiotic product or gut benefit.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'FISH: anchovy is a regulated fish allergen. Small quantities used as flavouring can still matter for fish allergy.', 'People with fish allergy and those checking salt-cured products, packing oils, species or preparation.', 'Fish dishes, sauces, dressings, spreads, pizza toppings and savoury seasonings.', 'Anchovy; Anchovies; anchovy fish', 'Another suitable fish or savoury ingredient; allergens, salt, nutrients and flavour differ.', 'Not vegan', 'Not vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Usually NOVA 1', 'Oily fish; assess curing and formulation', 'High', 'Use the appropriate fish identity and declare FISH where required, including in compound foods using anchovy for flavour.', 'Anchovies are fish providing protein and flavour. They contain the fish allergen; cured products c