  ('microcrystalline-cellulose-fibre', 'UIL-0575', 'Microcrystalline Cellulose Fibre', 'Microcrystalline cellulose fiber; microcrystalline cellulose; micro-crystalline cellulose', 'Fibres and prebiotic ingredients', 'Purified cellulose ingredient', 'A purified, partially depolymerised cellulose preparation; distinct from powdered cellulose and chemically substituted cellulose derivatives.', 'Specified plant-derived cellulose processed to the food-grade microcrystalline form.', 'Bulking, texturising, powder handling or other permitted technological functions depending on the application.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Mainly a non-digestible cellulose contribution; not an ordinary starch, protein or fat ingredient.', 'Not a protein source as purified cellulose.', 'Little fat in the plain purified ingredient.', 'A carbohydrate polymer not digested like ordinary starch by human digestive enzymes.', 'Cellulose is an insoluble fibre; any declared fibre content or claim needs the actual grade, analysis and conditions.', 'Do not treat pure cellulose as digestible glucose; no generic glucose-lowering benefit established.', 'Can contribute to stool bulk; grade, amount and tolerance matter. No universal prebiotic or clinical benefit follows from this name.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Pure microcrystalline cellulose is not one of the UK 14 allergens; assess source residues, blends and cross-contact.', 'People checking fibre tolerance, preparation identity or the actual additive/formulation grade.', 'Specified food texturising/bulking systems and other preparations using food-grade cellulose.', 'Microcrystalline Cellulose Fibre; Microcrystalline cellulose fiber; microcrystalline cellulose; micro-crystalline cellulose', 'Another suitable fibre or technological system; physical and digestive behaviour can differ.', 'Vegan', 'Vegetarian', 'No inherent gluten in the plain