  ('coffee-powder', 'UIL-0576', 'Coffee Powder', 'Powdered coffee; coffee ingredient powder', 'Cocoa, coffee and tea derivatives', 'Coffee-derived ingredient', 'An ambiguous coffee ingredient term that may refer to finely ground roasted beans or a dried soluble coffee extract; confirm the actual preparation.', 'Coffee beans ground after roasting, or coffee extract dried into powder, as specified; decaffeination and blends need separate identification.', 'Coffee flavour, colour and, in caffeinated grades, caffeine contribution in foods and drinks.', 'Processed ingredient', 'Depends on ground versus soluble form, serving, extraction and any added ingredients; do not copy brewed-drink values to dry powder.', 'Contribution depends on form and use level; not a standard protein concentrate.', 'Ground-bean and soluble-extract fat contents differ; added creamers or oils change the recipe.', 'Coffee solids and any added sugars or carriers differ by preparation.', 'Ground material and soluble extract have different retained components; not automatically a fibre-rich serving.', 'No fixed glycaemic index or glucose-treatment benefit; sweetened mixes and plain coffee need separate assessment.', 'Caffeine and individual tolerance may matter; no generic probiotic or gut-treatment benefit from the powder name.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Coffee allergy is possible although outside the UK 14 allergens. MILK, SOYA or other allergens may occur in compound coffee mixes.', 'People monitoring caffeine, including during pregnancy, or sensitive to caffeine and sleep effects; check actual caffeine and serving data.', 'Coffee drinks, bakery, desserts, confectionery and other coffee-flavoured formulations.', 'Coffee Powder; Powdered coffee; coffee ingredient powder', 'A specified coffee preparation or verified suitable decaffeinated ingredient; flavour, caffeine and functional behaviour d