  ('bifidobacterium-lactis', 'UIL-0580', 'Bifidobacterium Lactis', 'Bifidobacterium animalis subsp. lactis; Bifidobacterium animalis subspecies lactis', 'Cultures and fermentation ingredients', 'Bacterial culture', 'A bacterium currently classified as Bifidobacterium animalis subsp. lactis; the older lactis name does not identify a commercial strain or its evidence.', 'A specified bacterial strain cultivated and supplied with grade-dependent carriers, culture residues or other components.', 'Selected fermented-food cultures and microbial supplement preparations, subject to the actual strain and use.', 'Additive/functional ingredient', 'Normally used at small levels; carriers and inclusion rate determine direct macronutrient contribution.', 'Not a replacement for dietary protein; assess culture residues and any protein-containing carrier.', 'Usually minor at use levels; carrier-dependent.', 'Carriers can contribute carbohydrate; the organism name does not specify them.', 'Not a dietary fibre ingredient; identify any fibre carrier separately.', 'No generic blood-glucose-control benefit established by this name.', 'Any benefit needs evidence matching the exact strain, dose, viability and studied outcome/population; do not generalise across all preparations.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Check growth media, residues and carriers, including MILK or SOYA where relevant. The taxonomic word lactis does not itself prove a milk ingredient.', 'People with relevant allergies and anyone checking live microbial products; medically vulnerable users need product-specific suitability assessment.', 'Selected fermented foods, culture preparations and microbial supplements.', 'Bifidobacterium Lactis; Bifidobacterium animalis subsp. lactis; Bifidobacterium animalis subspecies lactis', 'An identified culture with evidence for the intended use; strains and species are not automatic subs