  ('vitamin-c', 'UIL-0581', 'Vitamin C', 'Added vitamin C; vitamin C preparation', 'Vitamin ingredients', 'Water-soluble vitamin nutrient', 'The vitamin C nutrient, commonly supplied as L-ascorbic acid or a specified vitamin-C-containing preparation; the label term does not identify every carrier or salt form.', 'A documented food-grade vitamin C source; chemical form, manufacture, strength and carriers require specification.', 'Vitamin fortification or supplementation and, for specified forms, permitted technological functions.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'An essential micronutrient involved in collagen formation, antioxidant and immune functions and non-haem iron absorption; contribution depends on amount.', 'Not a dietary protein source.', 'Not a dietary fat source; any fat comes from carriers or other ingredients.', 'Not a carbohydrate serving; sugar or other carriers can contribute carbohydrate.', 'Not a dietary fibre source.', 'No generic blood-glucose-treatment effect established by vitamin C on a label.', 'Not a probiotic; high supplemental intakes can cause gastrointestinal upset. Form and amount matter.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'Vitamin C itself is not one of the UK 14 allergens; check carriers, capsules and other components.', 'People using concentrated supplements or with relevant clinical restrictions, including iron-overload conditions; total amount and formulation matter.', 'Fortified foods, drinks, vitamin premixes, supplements and specified food formulations.', 'Vitamin C; Added vitamin C; vitamin C preparation', 'Another permitted vitamin C preparation suitable for the intended purpose; match vitamin amount and technological function rather than ingredient weight alone.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Vitamin nu