  ('ferrous-fumarate', 'UIL-0582', 'Ferrous Fumarate', 'Iron(II) fumarate; ferrous iron fumarate', 'Mineral ingredients', 'Ferrous iron salt', 'An iron(II) salt of fumaric acid used as a specified iron source; commercial preparations may contain carriers or other ingredients.', 'A manufactured food-grade ferrous fumarate preparation with defined purity, form and elemental-iron content.', 'Iron fortification and supplement formulations where permitted.', 'Highly refined ingredient', 'Supplies iron, an essential micronutrient in haemoglobin and oxygen transport; contribution depends on the elemental-iron amount.', 'Not a dietary protein source.', 'No meaningful fat in the pure mineral salt; carriers vary.', 'Not a carbohydrate serving; carriers may contribute.', 'Not a dietary fibre source.', 'Iron''s haemoglobin role is not a blood-glucose effect or a diagnosis of iron deficiency.', 'Supplemental iron can cause gastrointestinal effects such as nausea or constipation; form, amount and individual tolerance matter.', 'No inflammation rating assigned: this generic profile does not establish an inflammatory or anti-inflammatory effect in people.', 'The pure salt is not one of the UK 14 allergens; assess carriers, coatings and other formulation components.', 'People using iron supplements, with iron-overload conditions or relevant medicine interactions; elemental dose matters.', 'Fortified foods, mineral premixes and specified iron supplements.', 'Ferrous Fumarate; Iron(II) fumarate; ferrous iron fumarate', 'Another permitted iron source where appropriate; equal ingredient weights do not provide equal elemental-iron amounts.', 'Source-dependent', 'Source-dependent', 'No inherent gluten in the plain ingredient; blends and cross-contact need separate assessment.', 'Context dependent', 'Specified iron salt; elemental amount and preparation matter', 'High', 'Ferrous fumarate is listed as a permitted mineral source in the GB VMS register; verify actual grade, product category a